{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once","id":1365948,"title":"Can your Big Bad Villain take 5 Solars at once?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-06T22:58:36-08:00","id":1365948,"title":"Can your Big Bad Villain take 5 Solars at once?","content":"<img src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/498704231407288320/675179180048121876/image0.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> So I was playing Pillar of Eternity 2, and one of the boss is this god of erosion and entropy, basically the final end instead of a death-rebirth cycle, he looks like a very scary snow moo.<br /> <br /> And my party wipes our asses using his ugly cow face since 5 people ganging up on one enemy is just that strong of an advantage, the same thing happens in many other games that I play where a group of people beat-up one singled boss who will only pose any dangers if they have some annoying gimmick such as wiping the party if they don't perform X/Y/Z actions.<br /> <br /> But when I look at fictions the opposite of the above happens i.e One single villain soloing the whole party, and it usually ends with a one-on-one duel between the villain and the hero (and sometimes their love interested or rival), the other teammates are basically window-dressing to show how strong the villain is (which is pretty eeeeeh in TTRPG).<br /> <br /> So how do you prefer your boss battle in Exalted? Do you railroad it through fluff and crunch to make it happen like fiction? Or do let the PCs beat the shit out of the lone villain through number advantage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T23:25:50-08:00","id":1365951,"title":"","content":"Sometimes a bad guy has minions he employs during the fight so that it\u2019s not five dudes dogpiling onto one guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T00:57:43-08:00","id":1365961,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1357571-how-2-god-fite-making-single-enemies-work\">Isn't this exact thread on page two?</a><br /> <br /> But yeah. I don't believe in boss fights for Exalted.<br /> <br /> I prefer a cerebral villain. Screenslaver or Mr. Glass sort of thing. &quot;It was Old Man Jenkins all along!&quot; &quot;Kill me and I'll break the dam and flood the village!&quot;<br /> <br /> Individual PCs get their &quot;Hello. My name is Inago Montoya.&quot; moments where they solo someone important to them. But a Circle of Five does not get to face down an epic boss. If I have eight hours to spare to run that fight, I'd rather play Twilight Imperium.<br /> <br /> You're supposed to win. You are Exalted. You're not meant to have some nail-bitingly close fight where the Cleric wonders how much diamond dust this is going to cost. And you're not meant to end your campaign with a TPK and darkness swallowing Creation. The PCs are meant to win, and the published antagonists reflect that.<br /> <br /> This said, things like the giant lava monster are supposed to keep things novel.<br /> <br /> But if you've got time to run the combat between Mnemon, bound Octavian, a Size 2 group of Blood Apes, a Size 5 group of Imperial Legionaries led by combat focused Essence 4 General and with two Essence 3 (Experienced Dragon-Blooded) Dragon-lord Mnemon scions vs the Solar Circle then more power to you, I guess. (Don't forget to scale up the opposition once the PCs hit Essence 3.)<br /> <br /> Lunars and Dragon-Blooded can, of course, just be given Solars as boss fights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-07-2020, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T01:23:26-08:00","id":1365967,"title":"","content":"I prefer boss squad to just solo-boss, and if a solo-boss some way to keep up (lots of counter attacks/reflexive actions)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T05:13:26-08:00","id":1365983,"title":"","content":"This topic comes up regularly (I am certain there were at least three thread devoted to it). I am firmly convinced that there should be a room for satisfying fights with one singularly powerful enemy, because of its central narrative role.<br /> <br /> I homebrewed some charms which are intended to help the boss survive the fight, by essentially giving them extra initiative tracks. So, you just virtually treat the boss as separate combatants, but describe them as a single person.<br /> <br /> The way charms are written are intended for a use both for NPCs and PCs, but you can easily ignore it and treat it as exclusively NPC feature, (and it's a Solar version only, I plan to modify them for different splats).<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Milosz, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>GENERAL </b></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>COMBAT CHARMS</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Steel Faster than Thought [Fist Faster Than Thought]</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Cost: 1</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">0</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> m, </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">6</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">i, 1 wp</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Mins: Meele [Brawl, Martial Arts] 4, Essence </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">3</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Keywords: Perilous, </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Stackable,</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Heavily Apocryphal</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Duration: </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">One Scene</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prerequisite Charms: Any </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">fifteen</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Meele [Brawl, Martial Arts] Charms</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>This charm cannot be learned before reaching Essence </b></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>3</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Upon paying the cost of this charm, Solar opens an additional </span><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Initiative Track</span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">. Effectively, the combatant now has two Initiative scores. The initial value of the </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">new </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">score is determined by a Join Battle roll. Whenever the character makes a </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>withering </b></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">attack, she can make an additional attack with an additional track at the tick determined by the Initiative value in </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">the</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> respective tracks. Initiative gathered with attacks is stored in the respective track. Whenever an enemy makes a withering attack, its their choice which track is affected. </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Milosz, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">If an attack would bring an Initiative score in one of the tracks below zero, this track is closed. Remaining withering damage affects remaining Initiative tracks chosen by the attacker.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">If any effect other than a withering attack grants Solar Initiative, the player might add this Initiative to any chosen track. Initiative cost of charms and evocations may be paid from any track chosen by the player. Effects which subtract character's Initiative, subtract it from any track chosen by the player who invoked the effect.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Milosz, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Decisive</b></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">attacks </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">can use only Initiative from one track per attack but </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">reset all Initiative tracks to their base value. Additional initiative tracks do not allow a character to make additional decisive attacks. If a character is able to make several decisive attacks in one turn, the Initiative from different Initiative tracks may be used in these attacks. Initiative from two different tracks can</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">not</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">be combined in one attack. </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Milosz, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Whenever initiative value in the additional track becomes zero, that track is closed, and has to be reopened using this charm. This does not count as Initiative Crash, unless all tracks are closed.</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Milosz, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This charm can be purchased [Essence \u2013 2] times, allowing to have the number of opened initiative tracks equal to the number of times this charm was purchased.</span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Milosz, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Master's Blade Strikes [Master's Fist Strikes]</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Cost: </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">6</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">m</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Mins: Meele 5, Essence </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">4</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Type: </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Keywords: Dual, Heavily Apocryphal</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Duration: Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prerequisite: Steel Faster Than Thought [Fist Faster Than Thought]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>This charm cannot be learned before reaching Essence </b></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>4</b></span><br /> <br /> In her turn, <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Solar can </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">reflexively </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">close one of the Initiative Tracks and make a </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>decisive</b></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">attack using Initiative exclusively from that track. </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">The attack happens on the tick determined by the initiative value of the closed track. </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Milosz, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">If the rest of attacks are </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>withering</b></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">, this does not reset them to base Initiative. If the rest of attacks are </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>decisive</b></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">, this creates an additional attack that does not count towards the limit of the number of attacks generated by other charms (although the Initiative from this attack may be split into more attacks using the normal rules of charms generating these additional attacks).</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Milosz, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Unsurpassed Battle Awarness</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Cost: -</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Mins: Meele [Brawl, Martial Arts] 5, Essence 5</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Type:</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Keywords: Heavily Apocryphal, </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Perilous</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Duration: Permament</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prerequisite: Steel Faster Than Thought [Fist Faster Than Thought]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>This charm cannot be learned before reaching Essence 5</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">This charm enhances its prerequisite. </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Whenever Solar rolls join battle, survives an initiative crash or closes the last opened </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">additional </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">initiative track </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">while not in the initiative crash</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">, she reflexively opens one initiative track </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">at the beginning of her turn</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">. </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Initiative value in th</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">at</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> track is set equal to the </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">base</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> value if</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">the track was closed by performing a decisive attack or to one otherwise. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Interaction with Single Point Shining in the Void</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">The Initiative tracks generated by the Solar charm are considered separate from the Sword's track. Steel Faster than Thought cannot create additional tracks for the Sword.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>BRAWL SPECIF</b></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>I</b></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>C CHARMS</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Wounded Lion Bites</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Cost: </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">5</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">m</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Mins: Brawl 4, Essence </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">4</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Keywords: Withering-Only, Heavily Apocryphal</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Duration: Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prerequisite: Fist Faster Than Thought</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">When in Initiative Crash and making a </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>withering</b></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">attack, the character may launch an additional </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>withering attack</b></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">on the same tick.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>MELEE SPE</b></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>C</b></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>I</b></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>F</b></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>IC CHARMS</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Finesse of Supreme Balance</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Cost: 2m + 1m for 1i</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Mins: Meele 4, Essence </span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">4</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Keywords: Heavily Apocryphal</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Duration: Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prerequisite: Steel Faster Than Thought</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">When a</span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>withering </b></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">attack would close an Initiative track, Solar may reflexively mitigate the damage by transferring the Initiative from any of the remaining tracks. This costs 1m for one point of transferred Initiative. The final Initiative value in the target track cannot exceed its value before receiving the attack.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Solar Impossible Defence</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Cost: 4m</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Mins: Meele 5, Essence 5</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Keywords: Heavily Apocryphal</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Duration: Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prerequisite: Steel Faster Than Thought, Protection of Celestial Bliss</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Solar may close any chosen Initiative track and add [Initiative in the closed track/2 rounded down] Initiative for one tick to the pool generated by Protection of Celestial Bliss. This may be used after the attack roll of the opponent is made but before the damage roll.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, this somewhat aligns with others' suggestions that the boss better be made multiple opponents, since I was really looking for a way to make the boss mechanically close to multiple opponents while not going in that direction in the narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-07-2020, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T07:40:04-08:00","id":1366015,"title":"","content":"I usually try to have boss fights that aren\u2019t solo encounters, even in DnD. One lone dragon dies in like two turns to a good 4-person party even without the wizard pulling shenanigans. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s a bit more extreme in Exaltwd for two reasons.<br /> <br /> 1. Solars are supposed to be very strong. So strong that the greatest Solar warriors are the equal Or maybe even greater than directional war gods. Which is appropriate because they\u2019re the biggest sworn enemy of the worlds greatest nation, the worlds largest religion, the worlds more prevalent exalted, the demons of hell, monsters of the underworld, and nightmares of the feywyld. If they weren\u2019t badass enough to easily beat Octavian 5v1 they wouldn\u2019t stand a chance.<br /> <br /> 2. The way players build PCs is often to make them always a badass warrior in addition to whatever their concept is. So your big bad god monster isn\u2019t just fighting five solars, he\u2019s fighting five great Solar warriors with a dozen combat charms each. Which turns a battle that should require some thinking into a cakewalk. Which is true even if your PCs aren\u2019t Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1365961#post1365961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars and Dragon-Blooded can, of course, just be given Solars as boss fights.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even then that\u2019s hard. If you try to run the Prince Resplendent or the Wandering Deathknight or any of the characters from Tomb of Dreams as a boss against a circle of DBs or even worse Lunars they\u2019re going to die FAST and not accomplish much before they do. You could raise up the Tomb of Dreams characters to chargen level and run the whole circle against a group of Lunars or DBs and it would still be easy. Most of them are just missing charms anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even if you\u2019re building a Solar out of the corebook unless you build it and play it exactly the right way it\u2019s not going to work. They\u2019re just going to run out of motes and get their spine broken by a Lunar or be torn apart by terrestrial animas 95% of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T07:58:22-08:00","id":1366018,"title":"","content":"One of my first really successful Big Bad Guy Battle was one where I divided the characters in order for them to have strong narrative fights : The Twilight fought his Lunar mate, the Night Infiltrated the enemy 2nd Circle Demon, the Dawn and the Eclipse protected the Immaculate Temple against the enemy champion (but not big boss) and his troops, and finally when everything was done those of them that were not exhausted fought the Abyssal leading the enemies.<br /> <br /> It worked real wonders. Never seen my players being so involved. But I find it difficult to reproduce, some groups accept this kind of thing naturally, others are not interested.<br /> <br /> My second Big Boss Battle was also successful from the &quot;fight&quot; perspective, but I believe less from the emotional perspective (because the Big Bad Guy showed up recently, so less connection) : Basically a Legendary size, with an elemental duckflame mounting a giant salamander, and a spirit of fire possessing the sister of one of the players. Like I said rather good fight, but less emotional drama (the other was the conclusion of a 2 year campaign). Still taught me a lot on how to handle strong NPC's and how to make a lot of good stuff. But clearly One Big Bad guy doesn't work, or else you make him acting so much or having so much powers it becomes a caricature of power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T10:37:37-08:00","id":1366062,"title":"","content":"I think the constraints of the basic 1e setting core on this are maybe slightly less inhibiting towards this than might be thought. <br /> <br /> The designers and setting writers could've come down more than they did on the side of giving each of the Solar Castes a bit more power in each of their venues (combat, infiltration, magic, discovery, social skills and so on) in buffing a small circle of other Solars, and slightly less emphasis on isolated personal power, and maybe slightly less power overall, while still basically fulfilling them being what the 1e core said they were (strong heroes in each of their Caste domains, and the mightiest of Exalted, in circle and hosts). <br /> <br /> They didn't very much! It doesn't seem like Solar Circles being more than the sum of their parts has been a huge mechanical priority (and I might be wrong about this). But totally nothing about the basic setting limits that, it's just not that emphasized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T10:51:03-08:00","id":1366064,"title":"","content":"I agree with people's suggestions of multiple opponents. That's generally how I do it. One might be &quot;the boss&quot; but he can have a couple of lieutenants and a battle group of mooks (battle groups are nice tar-pits, as they don't give out a lot of initiative and can attack most of the PCs simultaneously).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T11:12:22-08:00","id":1366072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366062#post1366062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the constraints of the basic 1e setting core on this are maybe slightly less inhibiting towards this than might be thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1e core also seemed to have a different idea about what epic Exalted heroes really means. Before the Castebooks/Aspect books came out the charms were a lot more low-key. Still way more epic than starting DnD characters but much less than what it turned into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T14:19:20-08:00","id":1366112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366072#post1366072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The 1e core also seemed to have a different idea about what epic Exalted heroes really means. Before the Castebooks/Aspect books came out the charms were a lot more low-key. Still way more epic than starting DnD characters but much less than what it turned into.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember getting the Corebook when it was new and complaining about how majorly broken it was. Reflexive Dodge with Shadow Over Water? Scene long Dodge with Flow Like Blood?!? Hax!<br /> <br /> How little we knew...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T16:15:38-08:00","id":1366148,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a>, certainly true, although to clarify, I perhaps should have said &quot;Base premises of the setting&quot; and left out the bit about 1e, as less wanting to say stuff about shifting premises over time (or, worse anything which could be construed as making claims about &quot;How things were back when they were AWESOME!&quot;)and emphasis more about what the basic nature of the setting allows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T22:31:43-08:00","id":1366242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366112#post1366112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember getting the Corebook when it was new and complaining about how majorly broken it was. Reflexive Dodge with Shadow Over Water? Scene long Dodge with Flow Like Blood?!? Hax!<br /> <br /> How little we knew...</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't even thinking so much about crazy dice tricks, it was a lot more like other RPG systems in what it focused on and what it made you roll for. It feels a lot more Crouching Tiger Hidden Dragon, or House of Flying Daggers than Asura's Wrath or Herculean Trials. I mean, one of the many enemies it says Solars have to face is mobs of angry mortals because enough men with bows can bring down any hero.<br /> <br /> The Storyteller section even suggests not making your characters the most important people in the world, and warns against conflating good drama with powerful characters. Citing Superman and Batman of all things. Which is hilarious considering by Autocthonians they statted up the Lion to be basically invincible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366148#post1366148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a>, certainly true, although to clarify, I perhaps should have said &quot;Base premises of the setting&quot; and left out the bit about 1e, as less wanting to say stuff about shifting premises over time (or, worse anything which could be construed as making claims about &quot;How things were back when they were AWESOME!&quot;)and emphasis more about what the basic nature of the setting allows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah I see. I think the best way to represent Solars requiring eachother in teamwork is to array them against a wide variety of challenges. The Dawn might be invincible in combat but you can't kill a storm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T03:22:14-08:00","id":1366279,"title":"","content":"How interesting, so people always aim to make the combat Big Bad a boss-type of confrontation by giving them henchmen or effect that counter the PC's superior number.<br /> <br /> Is this because battling the villain through a long combat session is just what people expect supposed to happen at the end of the story? Is it possible to get some good drama when your PCs complete crushes FaFL when he tries to solo you like an Evil Overlord?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T03:29:31-08:00","id":1366282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366279#post1366279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How interesting, so people always aim to make the combat Big Bad a boss-type of confrontation by giving them henchmen or effect that counter the PC's superior number.<br /> <br /> Is this because battling the villain through a long combat session is just what people expect supposed to happen at the end of the story? Is it possible to get some good drama when your PCs complete crushes FaFL when he tries to solo you like an Evil Overlord?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind, the only examples we have so far are in the published materials, so we don't know how OP Deathlords are.<br /> <br /> Technically, it is possible to make rules that lets one character take on 5. (Like I'm sure if DrLoveMonkey, JohnDoe and myself got together and said &quot;Lets make the Mother of all bosses&quot; we could think up something that makes PCs weep).<br /> <br /> Lunar Elders from the book couldn't take on a circle of Solars though, this I'm pretty sure, barring shennanigans.<br /> <br /> prototype00<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T04:27:30-08:00","id":1366293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366279#post1366279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this because battling the villain through a long combat session is just what people expect supposed to happen at the end of the story? Is it possible to get some good drama when your PCs complete crushes FaFL when he tries to solo you like an Evil Overlord?</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, it's a mix.<br /> <br /> Firstly... it's the big boss. <i>Boss</i>. Why would he/she turn up to the battle by his/herself? There are lieutenants, bodyguards, etc. When the PCs fought the sorcerer Moku Star-Spear, he brought 30 raiders. On the opposite end of the scale, when Ahlat ambushed the PCs, he brought 100 minor war-gods.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, a bit like JohnDoe, I do prefer more mental villains, who probably have a couple of burly combat dudes to fight for them. Palpatine and Darth Vader.<br /> <br /> Coincidentally... this makes for much better fights, because unless you build specifically for it, it's very difficult for any one creature to fight 5 Solars, even if it's one Dawn, his combat-focused Night sidekick, a crafter with a crossbow, a Zenith who's tough but a mediocre swordsman, and the Eclipse with 2 kung-fu charms. There's still 5, and one's a Dawn. And when the PCs bring their own minions (demons, elementals, random dudes they've recruited, etc), it's even worse.<br /> <br /> I also find it makes for better stories, because there's more characters opposing the PCs. You can also have multiple boss fights of course, as they chop through the enemy; so even if the PCs do easily kill a villain, he's got his mates. Also, different PCs can face off against people in similar areas; the PC General can face the NPC General, the socialite can intrigue against the NPC politician, etc. And then at the end they can all have a big fight, where the Dawn faces the top combat dude on the enemy side, but the other PCs can fight their own nemeses.<br /> <br /> Because Solars are some of the world's greatest heroes, it can feel silly when there's one enemy who can do what every member of the circle can do, so splitting it up is better.<br /> <br /> I used to find that PCs would just kill any villains before they could really, well, develop any character, so I thought a fair bit about how to deal with that. Having a group of foes is one way. (See below for an example from my Solar game.)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">For example, in my e4 Solar game, they battled a rival band of Celestials, the Crimson Masters.<br /> First, they met the Cardinal of the Cathedral Encarmine (Twilight), the Leper Prince (Liminal), and some Tiger Warriors. The Cardinal was torturing suspected demon cultists, and the Liminal had been controlling a ghost the PCs were friends with (he claimed to stop a demon cult controlling him). The PCs killed the Leper Prince and Tiger Warriors, captured the Cardinal, then let him go after interrogating him.<br /> Later, the Crimson Masters sent the Godslayer (their Eclipse) to meet the PCs (at a wedding, seemed safe) to negotiate some sort of peace deal, dividing up zones of influence. But Timid Silk Blossom (Casteless PC) attacked him, so they fought him and his Tiger Warriors, he fled, and the Full Moon hunted him down and killed him.<br /> So then the Crimson Masters turned their army around and marched it back towards the PCs.<br /> The PC Zenith went to negotiate with the Prophet of the Crimson Word (Zenith) and failed, the PC Full Moon attacked her army but had to flee their Tiger Warrior archers, and then the PC Solar sorcerer nuked their army with Death Ray, and they scattered.<br /> However, the other half of their army, led by their Night Caste leader Pride Khan and the Leper Prince, had gone through the Underworld to attack the city the PCs had seized to use as a buffer state. Their sorcerer, the Cardinal of the Cathedral Encarmine, used Heart of Darkness to cover the city in arcane gloom. He and his Lunar friend the Cardinal of the Cathedral Encarmine ambushed the PC Dawn and Twilight, but failed to kill them and had to flee.<br /> Meanwhile, the Solar sorcerer (having sped back), attacked and Death Ray'd Pride Khan and an unknown Lunar to dust, along with some of their soldiers, but the Leper Prince escaped into the Underworld with half the army.<br /> <br /> The Crimson Prophet was able to reform some of her army, and took them north to attack the PCs' closer buffer states (the PCs had a lot of buffer states). But the Dawn met her 1000 Tiger Warriors with his 70 horsemen and his ally, a mortal fish-man king with a few thousand peasant archers/spearmen.<br /> The Dawn smashed the Prophet's forces, and killed her in single combat.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Leper Prince and Cardinal took their survivors through the Underworld, where they fought the local Viceroy of the First and Forsaken Lion, an Abyssal who's the father of one of the PCs. He killed them and smashed their army.<br /> <br /> So then the PCs went home to relax, but while relaxing in their ziggurat, the Cardinal and Leper Prince flew a giant owl onto the top of the ziggurat, and the Leper Prince threw them all into the Underworld, where they were attacked by Pride Khan, the Prophet and the Godslayer, and a bunch of Tiger Warrior. Obviously the Solars beat them because ghosts are pretty easy for Solars to beat.<br /> <br /> Anyway, later on the PC Zenith went to negotiate with their enemy the Leopard Empress, daughter of Ahlat and ruler of Harborhead, Varang and some other places (her sorcerer had kidnapped their friend ages before, so they killed him, so she didn't like them. Fairly straightforward). Turned out she had the Cardinal of the Cathedral Encarmine, the Leper Prince, and the Cardinal of the Cathedral Encarmine living with her as they'd taken refuge with the enemy of their enemy. She arrested the PC, and was going to execute him.<br /> <br /> The other PCs (except the Dawn who was lured away by Sidereal machinations) turned up to save Light. They had to battle the Leopard Empress, the Cardinal of the Cathedral Encarmine, the Leper Prince, and the Cardinal of the Cathedral Encarmine. So there were 2 or 3 Solar PCs, 2 Lunar PCs, and their Second Circle Demon buddy (Mara). If they'd just been fighting the Leopard Empress, they'd have killed her anti-climactically. But because I'd combined her with another set of bad guys they'd half-beaten, they faced an e4 God-Blood, a Solar, a Lunar, a Liminal, some Brides of Ahlat, and a bunch of regular troops. The PCs still won (as I expected and wanted them to), but one lost an arm. I feel that's about right for the final big battle of a story arc.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, in the campaign I'm running, the Big Bad is either the Elemental Dragon Mela, or the Bull of the North (who may be an ancient body-stealing parasite recently escaped from Hell). Obviously they both claim the other one is the Big Bad.<br /> <br /> But the PCs didn't just go straight to Mela. They battled Dragonblood multiple times, which built up to them reaching Mela's castle, where they beat some Dragonblood protecting it (who'd been injured by demons). Now they've reached her throne room. On the one side, is Yurgen Kaneko (not his real name, which is Teshub, just the one he's currently using), who has five other... Solars? Infernals? Solar Akuma? with him. On the other side is Mela, whose throne is surrounded by ashigaru, led by the Shogun (an Air Aspect) and some Dragonblood lieutenants.<br /> <br /> So the 6 PCs could battle a Dawn (or Slayer? Or demon possessing a human body?) and some other much-less combat-orientated Solars. That means the combat-optimised Full Moon can battle a Dawn, while the others fight a Zenith (Or Malefactor?) sorcerer, Twilight (or whatever) crafter, etc. (Though I suspect the arrogant but not-combat-orientated Aurochs-totem Full Moon will want to fight the Bull of the North to prove he's the best bull.)<br /> <br /> Alternatively, they can fight 3 or 4 Dragonblood and a battle group, and a massive essence 10 Dragon, which is a harder fight, but they'll have some Solars to help them. So they can probably choose the people they want to fight depending on their personality/bravery, while NPCs can fight the other NPCs.<br /> <br /> (Or, if they're really cunning, maybe they'll wait for the NPCs to fight each other, then mop up the survivors. Not sure. They're going to try negotiating first; very difficult, but I want the Changing Moon to have the opportunity, you never know.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T05:52:48-08:00","id":1366303,"title":"","content":"As opposed to many posters on this forum, I strongly prefer single nemesis-type boss, so I would like to chime in. (Let me start with reiterating: mechanically, I think it's not as hard to have a singular powerful boss, as many people claim: just make them mechanically equivalent to many combatants, but narrate as a single entity. <i>Carthage delenda est</i>.)<br /> <br /> Now, I'd like to address two points <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a> made. (I hide it that behind spoilers for better parsing.)<br /> <br /> 1. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366293#post1366293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also find it makes for better stories, because there's more characters opposing the PCs. You can also have multiple boss fights of course, as they chop through the enemy; so even if the PCs do easily kill a villain, he's got his mates. Also, different PCs can face off against people in similar areas; the PC General can face the NPC General, the socialite can intrigue against the NPC politician, etc. And then at the end they can all have a big fight, where the Dawn faces the top combat dude on the enemy side, but the other PCs can fight their own nemeses.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> It of course makes little sense in general to ask what is better: multiple enemies or a single nemesis. However, I personally think that there is certain specific and highy desirable balance, when there are two kinds of opposition:<br /> - rivals;<br /> - nemeses.<br /> <br /> Rivals are plural. They have rather intricate web of interactions. Some of them may be scary, some of them may be goofy. They may oppose one another. Some of them can have personal history with the characters. You can make allies of some of them. They don't have to be personally powerful, I think it's a great role to be played by a cunning mortal.<br /> <br /> Nemeses on the other hand are the focal point of the campaign or at least the story arc. <i>In some kinds of anime-like </i>stories which seem appropriate for the Exalted, Nemesis should be also personally competent enough as combatants to oppose the whole circle of protagonists. The point is: the nemesis is a focus. It's not a subplot to be ignored. It's all about them. They have they own music theme (I actually do that in my sessions, I play a specific piece whenever the Nemesis is mentioned). Rivals are scared of them.<br /> <br /> Of course, your Nemesis can bring back some allies. Making the final fight the final <i>battle</i> definitely has some specific feel to it. However, it's not neutral for the tone. Final battle is reminiscent more of bronze-age myths or of Tolkien. I think that more anime-like stories are better served, when the final fight takes place in isolation: protagonists vs the Nemesis. They could bring their mooks and lieutenants, but then that what the allies of protagonists are fighting outside the palace, when the real fight takes place already in the throne chamber.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> 2. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366293#post1366293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Solars are some of the world's greatest heroes, it can feel silly when there's one enemy who can do what every member of the circle can do, so splitting it up is better.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> That's an interesting point that keeps being raised on this forum. I think that the key point here is maintaining certain <i>illusion</i>. In many sources, the protagonists are presented as over-the-top and Exalted explicitly introduces Solars as that. But I think it's not good to actually treat that statement too seriously.<br /> <br /> On many occasions, if you present the protagonists as the absolute peak of human skill or better, you try to illustrate that by showing how effortlessly that win with the regular opponents (and regular may be clearly competent within-the-setting). However, when it comes to your nemesis, it turns out they desperately surpass you. The key point is to build up to this confrontation. You need to constantly remind the audience that yes, your protagonists are still as over-the-top as they were last week, and no one could see this coming. I think that the real trap here is when Nemeses are too numerous or the trivial opposition too rare.<br /> <br /> Now, I think that the main trap in portraying this in rpg is as follows. In the narrative you want to keep the illusion that the protagonist is absolutely at the top of the food chain <i>except for that unique foe</i>. However, when righting a core book to an rpg you are forced to be more systematic. So you don't want to portray too many opponents as more powerful in order to avoid the impression that your protagonists are not so strong after all. For instance, you won;t portray Elder Sidereals as powerful enough to oppose a whole circle of Solars, because that would make Solars feel unimportant.<br /> <br /> I think that it is a trap and it should be resolved on the Storyteller's level: you should just pick your opposition very carefully so that the illusion is maintained that it's just <i>that one foe</i> that's out of the reach. Even if your players know well that this particular elder Sidereal is not more powerful then the rest of them, you should still try to make it look as if they were.<br /> <br /> By the way, someone could advise that stories with a singular Nemesis are better handled when playing Dragon-Blooded. Well, the point is: with Dragon-Blooded you wouldn't have this delight of playing the best warrior in the world. It is an important narrative feature. I just don't think it should be treated one hundred percent seriously when we actually start statting things out.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a> Please, do tell us, what happens next in your campaign!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-08-2020, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T06:07:28-08:00","id":1366305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366282#post1366282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind, the only examples we have so far are in the published materials, so we don't know how OP Deathlords are.<br /> <br /> Technically, it is possible to make rules that lets one character take on 5. (Like I'm sure if DrLoveMonkey, JohnDoe and myself got together and said &quot;Lets make the Mother of all bosses&quot; we could think up something that makes PCs weep).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going past essence 6 it's not all that difficult. The charms that create extra actions become a game changer if there's a significant difference in mote pool sizes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar Elders from the book couldn't take on a circle of Solars though, this I'm pretty sure, barring shennanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ma-Ha-Suchi currently could but he'd need a battle group which might go against the premise of this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-08-2020, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T08:09:53-08:00","id":1366327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366279#post1366279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this because battling the villain through a long combat session is just what people expect supposed to happen at the end of the story? Is it possible to get some good drama when your PCs complete crushes FaFL when he tries to solo you like an Evil Overlord?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> A curbstomp is pretty much never interesting to play through. If the expectation is that the enemy will get mowed down with little consequence, it's not worth even bothering to reach for the dice-- just throw out some narrative descriptions to set the scene and let the most thematically appropriate player describe their deathblow. Even the &quot;defeated villain at bay, almost certainly doomed but with nothing to lose&quot; scenario only works if they can actually <i>threaten</i> the players. Otherwise you get a sense of &quot;wait, <i>that's </i>who we were scared of this whole time?&quot; <br /> <br /> As you note in the original post, the action economy is a huge issue in any context. It's worse in tabletop games where everyone (rightly) expects to share the spotlight and at least <i>contribute </i>to major scenes. And it's worse yet in Exalted 3e, because the way the system links &quot;health&quot; and &quot;offensive power&quot;-- you can't have every attack against them miss, because that's no fun, but if they're getting hit with any sort of regularity, they're never going to build up enough Initiative to be a threat. Or worse, they'll build up <i>too </i>much initiative and one-shot a character-- also no fun. Add in onslaught penalties and the attrition element (run out of motes and you got splat pretty quickly) and pretty much the whole system is working against the outnumbered character. If you want to overcome that, you've got to bend things pretty damn hard. The thread JohnDoe244 linked earlier was my best attempt at dealing with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T12:21:25-08:00","id":1366370,"title":"","content":"So, I don't believe in the one size fits all solution to boss fights and don't consider 5 on 1 leading to a relatively quick defeat <i>inherently</i> a problem.<br /> <br /> To me it's an issue if it plays out exactly the same way. A couple of examples from my game to illustrate my point.<br /> <br /> There was a nine on one fight (some NPCs were helping) I was pretty happy with because the opponent was a big monster with acid blood, due to <i>everyone </i>having to resist an environmental hazard it managed to wound two of the PCs via acid shower before it was overwhelmed and slain. The size of the group worked in my favour here because with 9 characters rolling at difficulty 5 the odds of someone rolling horribly were pretty good and Legendary Size proved to be a good obstacle to the fight ending too quick even against a Dawn, a Dusk, a Full Moon, a Zenith, a Night, a Twilight, a Fire Aspect a Water Aspect and (for ease of communication) an Exigent. The main misgiving I had was that once the Night Caste made her attack she was pretty much locked out of participating due to the creature's high soak and her only having a knife.<br /> <br /> There was later a seven on one fight against a mad axe murderer Dawn Caste. He wounded the PC Dawn with his opening move and held out for four rounds due to hail shattering practice and a lucky win in a clash preventing the PCs from building much in the way of initiative also, notably he did 5 dice of lethal on his withering attacks so his own initiative wasn't relevant to the threat he posed. His method of denying initiative was shortcircuted by the Night who'd learnt from the previous encounter and used Stalking Wolf Attitude to build up initiative by evading detection instead of attacking, something she was better at and he was worse at. Appropriately, she was the one who turned the tide in round 3 when she stabbed him and took him down to his -4s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T14:30:57-08:00","id":1366400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366282#post1366282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, it is possible to make rules that lets one character take on 5. (Like I'm sure if DrLoveMonkey, JohnDoe and myself got together and said &quot;Lets make the Mother of all bosses&quot; we could think up something that makes PCs weep).</div> </div> </div> </div>I did! I have no clue how he actually runs, I just designed him to be absurdly strong and imagine he's beatable because Solars are BS.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1356871#post1356871\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1356871#post1356871\"> The After-shock war, in the Age of Sorrows - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1356871#post1356871\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353218-the-after-shock-war-in-the-age-of-sorrows?p=1356871#post1356871 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Many thanks to Omicron of SB, whom I cant seem to contact https://forums.spacebattles.com/thre...#post-12209803 (https://forums.spacebattles.com/threads/general </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366303#post1366303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As opposed to many posters on this forum, I strongly prefer single nemesis-type boss, so I would like to chime in. (Let me start with reiterating: mechanically, I think it's not as hard to have a singular powerful boss, as many people claim: just make them mechanically equivalent to many combatants, but narrate as a single entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That can work mechanically, there's lots of ways to do it, it just doesn't work well fluff-wise for Solars. It's like an RPG where the PCs are Olympian gods in the setting of Greek myth. Who can stand alone against the combined might of Zeus, Poseidon, Hades, Hera, and Ares? Nobody except maybe a Titan.<br /> <br /> You <i>could</i> do it if you managed to get your players to show an enormous amount of restraint. If they didn't want to be the greatest Solar-X in the world, for example. If you could convince the Dawn of the group to take like, 6 combat charms, and mostly from Essence 1 abilities, and have maybe 1-2 people with artifact weapons and armor. Also have people pick appropriate ability spreads with a wide variety of characters. Like if your character wasn't at least as good as a professional, full-time soldier, they can't take more than melee 1. Players don't like that though, in general. So you end up with a party of Sun Wukong, Heracles, Karna, Gilgamesh, and Cu Chulainn instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> It isn't as much a problem for Lunars, or especially Dragonblooded. If you pit Fakharu against a group of DBs who weren't all totally optimized for combat that might be a pretty good matchup. Or a circle of Lunars who there might only be 3 of. There are reasons why Solars are only one splat among a half dozen, though. They're cool, but there's things they can't do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T17:45:57-08:00","id":1366443,"title":"","content":"Firts of all, I strongly encourage you to run this fight and share its results!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366400#post1366400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You <i>could</i> do it if you managed to get your players to show an enormous amount of restraint. If they didn't want to be the greatest Solar-X in the world, for example. If you could convince the Dawn of the group to take like, 6 combat charms, and mostly from Essence 1 abilities, and have maybe 1-2 people with artifact weapons and armor. Also have people pick appropriate ability spreads with a wide variety of characters. Like if your character wasn't at least as good as a professional, full-time soldier, they can't take more than melee 1. Players don't like that though, in general. So you end up with a party of Sun Wukong, Heracles, Karna, Gilgamesh, and Cu Chulainn instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, you are saying here two things. First, as of now, it's very hard to find a fair match for 5 Solars playing by the book. With that, I <i>of course </i>absolutely agree. That's why I generally propose houserules/broken charms which would enable Storyteller to keep up in this arms' race (provided that everyone is ok with the changes, but the groups I play with generally trust me).<br /> <br /> Now, the second, more interesting part is that groups of Solars <i>should</i> be overwhelming. It's a widespread opinion with which I don't agree. If we really wanted Solars to be unbeatable, we could imagine a diceless game, say, like Chuubo's Wish-Granting Machine, in which the Solar warrior would simply have: <i>I win</i> button. I actually think that this could be a very interesting game, but by presenting this extreme, <br /> <br /> However, it's rather common in some media in the broad inspiration circle of Exalted that protagonists are portrayed as extremely skilled or gifted. Really the best of the best. However, this doesn't prevent their Nemeses to be still better. Now, the subtle art, is to make the audience sure that this situation is completely unique and that generally the protagonists are as awesome as initially suggested. <br /> <br /> Of course, if every second foe turns out to be a fair match to our protagonists, then the situation is getting out of control and the inflation of power becomes ridiculous. This is exaclty the same problem in rpg as in every other media. So it's a Storyteller job to make sure that protagonists are awesome. <br /> <br /> In other words, I believe that the claim that as a matter of fact in the setting the protagonists absolutely dominate essentially every opponent, shouldn't lead us to think that <i>in the story</i> they will be able to beat every actual opponent. <br /> <br /> For example, Geralt in the Witcher books and Benedict in the Amber saga, are both constantly and consistently portrayed as inhumanly skilled warriors who completely surpass everyone around. The authors of the books make great effort to remind us that they are exactly <i>that </i>good. However, like one-third of the time, when we see them fighting on-screen, they loose. Of course, it's important for the author to underline that this doesn't make them any less awesome.<br /> <br /> So, in a nutshell, I just think that genre-emulation (or, emulation of <i>some</i> genres mixed in the Exalted), require that the best-of-the-best sometimes be matched with a powerful singular Nemesis... and then be reminded that they are still essentially the best. Note that this could not simply done by playing a Dragon-Blooded campaign, since those Dragon-Blooded are not narrated to be the best. They are by design outmatched by several different human-like kinds of beings, it's the narrative premise. So them meeting an overwhelming opposition would not be a story about the best being defeated unless they raise and fight again, but about hitting above your weightclass. An intereseting story, but still a different one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T23:48:12-08:00","id":1366493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366443#post1366443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firts of all, I strongly encourage you to run this fight and share its results!</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't, sadly. I even dare to say that nobody can alone. It takes almost an entire day and an enormous amount of effort to run a combat with only two or three exalted in play. Doing one with six massively powerful and diverse characters is beyond the capacity of a single brain to handle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366443#post1366443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the second, more interesting part is that groups of Solars <i>should</i> be overwhelming. It's a widespread opinion with which I don't agree. If we really wanted Solars to be unbeatable, we could imagine a diceless game, say, like Chuubo's Wish-Granting Machine, in which the Solar warrior would simply have: <i>I win</i> button. I actually think that this could be a very interesting game, but by presenting this extreme,</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but here's the thing. Solars do not just win all the time always and forever. They get beaten, a lot, often quite resoundingly. They are &quot;only&quot; the the people in Creation who have singularly the greatest potential for power. There's lots of young Solars, most even, who can't beat an Elder Terrestrial warrior in a fight without crazy luck, either because they haven't realized their full potential, or their potential is lower than other Solars. These are not typically PC Solars.<br /> <br /> Even the most powerful ones can't fight the whole Realm on their own, they can't even fight a whole legion on their own without a hundred tricks up their sleeves at least. It's just that if they manage to get a DB alone in a room when both are fresh and ready for combat the powerful Solar is going to have to get really unlucky to lose that fight. I've seen it happen, a Dawn MA Supernal got, not just beaten but 100% perfected by a Dragonblooded princess in my second game of Third Edition. She got lucky though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366443#post1366443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, it's rather common in some media in the broad inspiration circle of Exalted that protagonists are portrayed as extremely skilled or gifted. Really the best of the best. However, this doesn't prevent their Nemeses to be still better. Now, the subtle art, is to make the audience sure that this situation is completely unique and that generally the protagonists are as awesome as initially suggested.</div> </div> </div> </div>For better or worse, that's not what the Solar exalted are billed as. The idea behind them is if you make a Dawn who's a fighter, and you make him the best fighter in the world, then actually, no, nobody is better than you. You're not the best 99.9% of the time, but there's this one really bad dude who's way better and the only way you have a chance of beating him is by teaming up with your circle. If you make a Solar who focuses on nothing but being the greatest warrior, then you are, you really really are, the greatest human warrior. The only people who might beat you 1v1 are very elder exalted, or beings like the Sun, Malfeas, Ligier, Balor, Mela, etc.<br /> <br /> Because of that though, it means that 5 Solars are definitely more powerful than basically any other singular thing. If the players make 5 characters who are all really good at fighting, no elder Exalt is going to be badass enough to take 5 full other characters who are 70%/40/%40%/30%/30% as powerful as them all at the same time in a straight fight. Even in stuff like the Witcher, when was the last time Geralt of Rivia, Vesemir, Yennefer of Vengerberg, Letho of Gulet, and Cirilla all teamed up against a single foe, completely fresh, prepared and ready to fight, and lost?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It also doesn't necessarily have to be that way. If you had an incomplete circle, like just three PCs, and they were a social butterfly Eclipse, a preacher Zenith, and a grand inventor Twilight, that could work. Especially if they decided that none of them have more than 3 dots in combat abilities or dexterity, and none of them really feel the need to carry artifacts. They give away their Exalted nature anyway, and that's often a fast track to the Wyld Hunt. In that case? Oh yeah, Fakharu is going to wreck their faces off. They don't just automatically win without rolling and no investment because they're Solars.<br /> <br /> What makes it so hard is that you often DO have full circles, or sometimes even more, and among them that Dawn is an unmitigated powerhouse, the Twilight is a warrior-inventor, the Eclipse is a warrior-sailor, the Night is a warrior-ninja, and the Zenith is a warrior-priest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T00:04:36-08:00","id":1366494,"title":"","content":"And this is why running Lunar or DB games is so much easier...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T00:16:40-08:00","id":1366495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366494#post1366494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is why running Lunar or DB games is so much easier...</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Tenchars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T00:22:16-08:00","id":1366497,"title":"","content":"Lunars do have that amusing thing where even the weediest No Moon can become a Legendary Sized Murder Machine with a small one charm investment.<br /> <br /> But that isn\u2019t Solar-perfection-at-combat, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-09-2020, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T00:47:28-08:00","id":1366501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366497#post1366497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars do have that amusing thing where even the weediest No Moon can become a Legendary Sized Murder Machine with a small one charm investment.<br /> <br /> But that isn\u2019t Solar-perfection-at-combat, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren\u2019t your forms dicepools capped by your excellency cap anyway? Like, still amazing but a dex1 Brawl 0 Lunar isn\u2019t getting all that much use out of a tyrant lizard form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T00:55:19-08:00","id":1366503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366501#post1366501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren\u2019t your forms dicepools capped by your excellency cap anyway? Like, still amazing but a dex1 Brawl 0 Lunar isn\u2019t getting all that much use out of a tyrant lizard form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Form Dicepool &gt; Yours, use the higher. <br /> <br /> All dice over your base regular pool are considered charm dice which necessarily limits how many dice you can add using excellencies, yes.<br /> <br /> Dex 1, Brawl 0 No Moon is still rolling the Tyrant Lizard\u2019s base dice pool, which as you said, amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-09-2020, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T01:17:22-08:00","id":1366504,"title":"","content":"They're rolling 2 dice, surely, because that's their cap. Dex 1+1 charm dice. Possibly more if they use a stunt, of course. Good damage though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunars</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When she takes an action the animal has a listed dice pool for, she may use its dice pool. Any dice over her own base (Attribute + Ability) pool <b>count as Charm dice and are subject to her dice cap</b>, <b>potentially preventing her from using a form\u2019s full dice pool. </b>If the animal\u2019s pool is lower than hers, or it has no listed pool, she may use her own dice pool, although the Storyteller may assess penalties if her shape is ill-suited to that action.<br /> \u2022 She may use the animal\u2019s natural weapons, including their listed dice pool and damage value. (Note that she uses the same pool for withering and decisive attacks). Any dice over her own base (Dexterity + Brawl) count as Charm dice, but damage doesn\u2019t count against the amount she may add with the Strength Excellency. If her (Dexterity + Brawl) pool is higher than the attack pool for a natural weapon, her withering attacks with it gain +1 Accuracy</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-09-2020, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T01:31:14-08:00","id":1366506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366495#post1366495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. Tenchars.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a less annoying note for people who want to play Solars, I do play an E4-5 game where 2 of the four Solars have pretty minimal combat ability, for that level. My Zenith is physical tertiary. The other two characters are better at combat, but they're still stealth first, combat second. The other characters are a cowardly Changing Moon, a Dragonblood martial artist, and a Raksha.<br /> So when we very occasionally get in a big fight (rare, because it's not a combat-focused game, it's more about investigation and the occult, a kind of Exalted Call of Cthulu I guess), actually we are not that great. So it's not so difficult to make a &quot;big boss&quot; that is a challenge for the group.<br /> <br /> There is the issue though that the ST sometimes undercooks encounters for the two guys who are the only ones out of 7 who are pretty good at combat, and overcooks encounters for everyone else. But then, he'd be the first to admit that combat mechanics are not his forte.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T01:31:48-08:00","id":1366507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366504#post1366504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're rolling 2 dice, surely, because that's their cap. Dex 1+1 charm dice. Possibly more if they use a stunt, of course.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, indeed you are correct, my mistake. Its animal damage and soak that ignores other considerations. So if you had a Dex 5 Brawl X, Str 1 No Moon, they'd still hit like a truck and tank like a brick wall.<br /> <br /> By the way, I recommend Dex 5 for Phys Tert Lunars for obvious reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-09-2020, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T01:32:40-08:00","id":1366508,"title":"","content":"Sigh... yeah. It's just sad though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T01:57:21-08:00","id":1366509,"title":"","content":"Does that mean a Dex 5 Brawl 1 Lunar with say, Int 5 in Tyrant Lizard form would normally have a dice cap of 11 (due to Base of 6 + Dex 5) but they could stunt in Int 5 at any time for <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>no mote cost</b></u></span> to raise the dice cap to 16 (due to base of 6 + Dex 5 + Int 5) and thus access the full Tyrant Lizard dice pool for say...<br /> <br /> Attack (Slam): 12 dice (Damage 14, minimum 4). The<br /> tyrant lizard uses its head or tail to bash an enemy, and<br /> can make a smashing attack<br /> <br /> Thats pretty amazing (man that word is being chucked around a lot).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T02:28:27-08:00","id":1366510,"title":"","content":"I'm confused by you talking about 16 and then having a 12-dice example. But yes, a Dex 5 Brawl 1 Lunar who stunts to use another attribute at 5 as well can roll 16 dice (well, 18, as it's a stunt), and if the animal has 16 dice then this costs 0 motes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Although perhaps this should be on another thread, and we should get back to boss fights?<br /> <br /> <br /> So yes, people have linked to other threads, but tldr: if you want a boss who can take on 5 PCs, they'll need huge soak, loads of health levels, ways to counteract Overwhelming penalties, and preferably some way to attack multiple times at good damage. Preferably attacking everyone rather than one person multiple times.<br /> The soak, health levels and anti-Overwhelming are the key things though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-09-2020, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T03:17:20-08:00","id":1366514,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one to ST 3-4 people at most ? Because I believe it also helps a lot to make sort of &quot;boss fight&quot; easier since there are less parties involved. I'm very impressed (and I must say also very scared) when Wizard of Oz describes a game with apparently 4 Solars, a Lunar, a Drabon Blooded and a Raksha. An Exalted game with 7 players. How do you even manage to end a scene ? Or go to another scene ? I always get at least 2 players wanting to do 10 mns interscene actions and stuff, does it take one whole hour when the party is this huge ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T05:26:03-08:00","id":1366532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366494#post1366494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is why running Lunar or DB games is so much easier...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but Lunars are consistently present as something very different <i>narratively</i> from Solars. Solars are humans, but jut that good. Lunars are human, but ... just with tentacles, weird wall-crawling abilities, and most likely wings?<br /> <br /> Ok, I guess there are two discussions here which would be great to disentangle:<br /> <br /> 1. How powerful Solars should be, given their narrative role?<br /> 2. If we decide that a circle of 5 Solars should beatable by a single (human-type) foe, could we make such foes (possibly stepping outside the current design paradigm)?<br /> <br /> I think that the answer to (2) is simply &quot;yes&quot;. If you think that a group of five Abyssals can beat your Solars, then just make an elder Abyssal with five Initiative tracks and possibly some extra shenanigans with mitigating decisive damage by spending motes or Initiative. That's actually simple. I don't want to make too strong claims how it works, but I tried to prepare solutions in this vein and I intend to playtest it.<br /> <br /> The answer to (1), I guess, is an irreducible disagreement between us. I don't really think that the basic premise of Exalted is that you can literally be the best warrior rules-wise. For me the basic premise is that you are returned hero, completely surpassing everyone around, of the kind that used to rule the Creation, but you're hunted, and now you want to change the world. (A premise very different from Lunars'.) For <i>that</i> premise it's really not necessary that you are literally the best rules-wise. It is important that you are way above average folks though.<br /> <br /> If in your group you play Solars to be literally at the top of the food chain, then yes, I guess that it would be bad for you to have human or human-like opponents which are fair match for five of these. I definitely see people here that see Solar exactly like this. But I don't think I'm the only one playing Exalted that is more compelled with &quot;returning hero narrative&quot; and doesn't really care about being literally the best. I know that this is how Exalted is often sold on forum, but I don't really see it in corebook of any edition (including second which comes closest to that).<br /> <br /> Ideally, I would love the Solars to start somewhat weaker and grow significantly stronger, stretching up to uncharted territories past Essence 5 with potential for truly cosmic scale over there. Generally, I'd love to see the games with wider power level spread, and the power level being generally more dependent on Essence rating than on splats (I fully endorse flattening the gaps between splats) and to see more differences in <i>potential</i> rather than raw power.<br /> <br /> Concerning the Witcher (literal spoilers):<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Well, a group of competent characters: Geralt, Milva, Angoul\u00eame, Caehir, Emiel, faced Vilgefortz and defeated him, but at great cost. He is a good example of Nemesis-like character.<br /> <br /> The same with Bonhart and Ciri's gang -- consistently depicted as comprising of very strong individuals.<br /> <br /> But mostly, in books you rarely find the kind of protagonists we see in rpg: five equally super-competent people working together.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-09-2020, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T05:38:42-08:00","id":1366533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366532#post1366532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer to (1), I guess, is an irreducible disagreement between us. I don't really think that the basic premise of Exalted is that you can literally be the best warrior rules-wise. For me the basic premise is that you are returned hero, completely surpassing everyone around, of the kind that used to rule the Creation, but you hunted, and now you want to change the world. (A premise very different from Lunars'.) For <i>that</i> premise it's really not necessary that you are literally the best rules-wise. It is important that you are way above average folks though.<br /> <br /> If in your group you play Solars to be literally at the top of the food chain, then yes, I guess that it would be bad for you to have human or human-like opponents which are fair match for five of these. I definitely see people here that see Solar exactly like this. But I don't think I'm the only one playing Exalted that is more compelled with &quot;returning hero narrative&quot; and doesn't really care about being literally the best. I know that this is how Exalted is often sold on forum, but I don't really see it in corebook of any edition (including second which comes closest to that).<br /> <br /> Ideally, I would love the Solars to start somewhat weaker and grow significantly stronger, stretching up to uncharted territories past Essence 5 with potential for truly cosmic scale over there. Generally, I'd love to see the games with wider power level spread, and the power level being generally more dependent on Essence rating than on splats (I fully endorse flattening the gaps between splats) and to see more differences in <i>potential</i> rather than raw power.</div> </div> </div> </div>You. I like you. I literally deleted a part of the last post I made on the Limit Break post that I made because I felt like &quot;Everyone was too much on the best-ever solar trope&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T06:19:44-08:00","id":1366540,"title":"","content":"I tend to agree. An Essence 5 Solar could make a claim to being the best X in Creation, but definitely not an Essence 2 Solar only a few sessions into the campaign-- Supernal or no. Solars are fabulously powerful, but that doesn't mean they <i>should </i>be able to auto-win against anyone they run into. If five low-Essence Solars can curb-stomp a Deathlord, I have trouble believing that a few dozen Dragonblooded couldn't do the same thing, and part of the point of the setting (at least as I understand it) is that the world is in trouble because it's being threatened by things that are too damn big for any number of Dragonblooded. Stuff that <i>needs </i>powerful Solars to deal with, because nothing else in Creation has a shot at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T06:39:29-08:00","id":1366543,"title":"","content":"I think some of this shades into our previous discussion about how much progression Solar Exalted should have, whether they should start fairly near their peak, and be a break from the whole zero-to-hero thing in favour of players getting to start out playing &quot;Mightiest Returned Heroes... Right NOW!&quot; and dealing direct with being the strongest (which is what 3e devs thought would be a great USP for Exalted!). Or it is more satisfying to have them have a longer Hero's Journey with some degree of building up even before they can have much chance of deal with Second Circle Demons alone on an equal basis in an area of focus (DrLoveMonkey's example on first page being Octavian).<br /> <br /> I would tend see Solars as having to be the most generally *skilled* humans and the most *skilled* supernaturally empowered beings, and the magically the strongest of the Exalted. That's a pretty non-negotiable core part of the setting. But I don't tend to see them as requiring of being the strongest, as such, things in any category an absolute sense.<br /> <br /> Where there are beings flat out stronger than the Solar Exalted, though they probably should be constrained by being not able to apply it in an easy &quot;human hero&quot; esque manner of course, or a manner which is replicable or lends itself to massive coordination with other beings in the manner that the Exalted host can coordinate. Like, their power's confined to a particular lair or location, it is connected to destabilizing effects on reality (introduces baleful effects of the Wyld, etc), it requires mass sacrifice, they're a one-off behemoth / monster that has inhuman personality and can't be replicated, etc.<br /> <br /> But going back to my first paragraph, this topic is all bound up again with how much journey Solars should have, and how much focus is on them having individual power against power to lead a circle in a particular area. (The OP question - now and in pre modified form ; ) - is all kind of bound up in &quot;Which Solars?&quot;.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T07:20:38-08:00","id":1366548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366532#post1366532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I guess there are two discussions here which would be great to disentangle:<br /> <br /> 1. How powerful Solars should be, given their narrative role?<br /> 2. If we decide that a circle of 5 Solars should beatable by a single (human-type) foe, could we make such foes (possibly stepping outside the current design paradigm)?<br /> <br /> I think that the answer to (2) is simply &quot;yes&quot;. If you think that a group of five Abyssals can beat your Solars, then just make an elder Abyssal with five Initiative tracks and possibly some extra shenanigans with mitigating decisive damage by spending motes or Initiative. That's actually simple. I don't want to make too strong claims how it works, but I tried to prepare solutions in this vein and I intend to playtest it.<br /> <br /> The answer to (1), I guess, is an irreducible disagreement between us.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;problem&quot; is that there is no such thing as an &quot;Elder Abyssal&quot;. And even if there were, having five Initiative tracks is WAY out of scope for how any of the beings in Exalted are portrayed.<br /> <br /> You can say &quot;in my game Solars are not the best and Elder Abyssals with five Initiative tracks exist&quot;. And I hope you have fun with that. But that's a house-rule you've put into your game to make it more fun -- it's not how the actual setting works.<br /> <br /> The closest thing to what you're asking for is a Primordial. You can reasonably have a Primordial BBEG who needs an entire Solar Circle to take down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366543#post1366543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would tend see Solars as having to be the most generally *skilled* humans and the most *skilled* supernaturally empowered beings, and the magically the strongest of the Exalted. That's a pretty non-negotiable core part of the setting. But I don't tend to see them as requiring of being the strongest, as such, things in any category an absolute sense.<br /> <br /> Where there are beings flat out stronger than the Solar Exalted, though they probably should be constrained by being not able to apply it in an easy &quot;human hero&quot; esque manner of course, or a manner which is replicable or lends itself to massive coordination with other beings in the manner that the Exalted host can coordinate. Like, their power's confined to a particular lair or location, it is connected to destabilizing effects on reality (introduces baleful effects of the Wyld, etc), it requires mass sacrifice, they're a one-off behemoth / monster that has inhuman personality and can't be replicated, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366305#post1366305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ma-Ha-Suchi currently could [fight an entire Circle of Solars] but he'd need a battle group which might go against the premise of this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I'll bite:<br /> <br /> How?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-09-2020, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T09:22:06-08:00","id":1366572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366548#post1366548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, I'll bite:<br /> <br /> How?</div> </div> </div> </div>He uses Invincible Beast Warrior Empowerment to hit them with a Command Action augmented range attack. Even with the bodyguard he's got in his write-up that'll be able to get an average of +13 successes to their attack roll pretty easily. Your typical circle of Solars will have people whose defensive strategy counts on nobody being able to add 13 successes and some will end up in initiative crash with his opening move because of it.<br /> <br /> Now the ranged part was important. After his opening move the Solars now need to kill or crash Ma-Ha-Suchi (deactivating IBWE) or destroy the battle group otherwise some of them aren't going to survive another round. This probably wouldn't be all that hard for them if he'd just ran in and attacked them at close range but instead he's exploiting the fact he's blunted their offensive and making them come to him (or attack him from range, obviously that works too).<br /> <br /> He still loses the eventual melee but I'd probably be pretty satisfied with how it went down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T11:25:35-08:00","id":1366594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366548#post1366548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;problem&quot; is that there is no such thing as an &quot;Elder Abyssal&quot;. And even if there were, having five Initiative tracks is WAY out of scope for how any of the beings in Exalted are portrayed.<br /> <br /> You can say &quot;in my game Solars are not the best and Elder Abyssals with five Initiative tracks exist&quot;. And I hope you have fun with that. But that's a house-rule you've put into your game to make it more fun -- it's not how the actual setting works.<br /> <br /> The closest thing to what you're asking for is a Primordial. You can reasonably have a Primordial BBEG who needs an entire Solar Circle to take down.<br /> How?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, that modification would require explicitly stepping out of the current design paradigm.<br /> <br /> There are no elder Abyssals, but Elder Sidereals able to meaningfully oppose a circle of Solars used to be a thing. Or potentially elder Infernals (I know there are no such things at the exact point where the action takes place, but Infernals with that potential surely did exist).<br /> <br /> The previously mentioned five Initiative tracks are obviously only an abstraction of that ability. It's meaningless to ask whether or not a thing with five Initiative tracks exists in the setting. What could potentially exist are elder exalted with the ability to defeat a whole circle (represented, for instance, by combatants with five Initiative tracks).<br /> <br /> So, is such an ability totally out of the scope of Exalted? Sure, currently, it's not a thing, but this is more or less clear in this discussion. I understand that it's not the intent of the current developers.<br /> <br /> However, for many years, in both previous editions, elder Sidereals or Deathlords were portrayed exaclty like that. And arguably, Deathlords were on a similar power level as first-age elder Solars. I know, more powerful, but it's really not a difference of orders of magnitude. At least they are explicitly something a Solar <i>could</i> become.<br /> <br /> I believe it is reasonable to assume that if something popped up in two editions (or really was mentioned more than once in a single book), then it qualifies, as a thing that could reasonably exist in Exalted. So powerful elder exalted, even if we don't have them as of now, and probably won't see them anytime soon, are not something totally out of scope of how setting works in Exalted broadly construed.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just as an illustration: I could easily imagine that developers decide that in the Exalted: fourth edition there will be no such thing as Caul. If someone were homebrewing a continent-size island at roughly the same place, I would never say that big landmasses on the Western Ocean are completely out of the scope of Exalted. Hypothetically, I could dislike it personally. I could even point out that it distorts the pure symbolism of map-as-governed-by-elements. (Hypothetically. Caul is cool!) But since we've definitely seen such things at some point (actually in two editions), it wouldn't automatically be out of the scope of the game.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> Neat!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-09-2020, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T12:11:37-08:00","id":1366603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366548#post1366548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;problem&quot; is that there is no such thing as an &quot;Elder Abyssal&quot;. And even if there were, having five Initiative tracks is WAY out of scope for how any of the beings in Exalted are portrayed.<br /> <br /> You can say &quot;in my game Solars are not the best and Elder Abyssals with five Initiative tracks exist&quot;. And I hope you have fun with that. But that's a house-rule you've put into your game to make it more fun -- it's not how the actual setting works.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where Lanic's first point comes into play-- how powerful, exactly, should Solars be relative to everything else that exists? What does an endgame challenge look like for a group of Solars? The lore says it has to be something truly impressive, but that could be anything from &quot;a thousand year-old Lunar gone mad&quot; to the Ebon Dragon itself-- and I don't think there's a definite answer anywere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T12:49:50-08:00","id":1366612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366572#post1366572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He uses Invincible Beast Warrior Empowerment to hit them with a Command Action augmented range attack. Even with the bodyguard he's got in his write-up that'll be able to get an average of +13 successes to their attack roll pretty easily. Your typical circle of Solars will have people whose defensive strategy counts on nobody being able to add 13 successes and some will end up in initiative crash with his opening move because of it.<br /> <br /> Now the ranged part was important. After his opening move the Solars now need to kill or crash Ma-Ha-Suchi (deactivating IBWE) or destroy the battle group otherwise some of them aren't going to survive another round. This probably wouldn't be all that hard for them if he'd just ran in and attacked them at close range but instead he's exploiting the fact he's blunted their offensive and making them come to him (or attack him from range, obviously that works too).<br /> <br /> <b>He still loses the eventual melee </b>but I'd probably be pretty satisfied with how it went down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so.<br /> <br /> Turn 1 Aim.<br /> Turn 2 Crash all the Solars.<br /> Turn 3 the Battlegroup acts before the Crashed Solars and attacks again, this time applying their attack to the Solar's Health Track.<br /> There is no Turn 4.<br /> <br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi is hard as nails.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366594#post1366594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I said, that modification would require explicitly stepping out of the current design paradigm.<br /> <br /> There are no elder Abyssals, but Elder Sidereals able to meaningfully oppose a circle of Solars used to be a thing. Or potentially elder Infernals (I know there are no such things at the exact point where the action takes place, but Infernals with that potential surely did exist).<br /> <br /> The previously mentioned five Initiative tracks are obviously only an abstraction of that ability. It's meaningless to ask whether or not a thing with five Initiative tracks exists in the setting. <b>What could potentially exist are elder exalted with the ability to defeat a whole circle</b> (represented, for instance, by combatants with five Initiative tracks).</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there elder exalted who can defeat a whole circle? (Well, there's Ma-Ha-Suchi.)<br /> <br /> From what book are you getting this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366594#post1366594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, for many years, in both previous editions, elder Sidereals or Deathlords were portrayed exaclty like that. And arguably, Deathlords were on a similar power level as first-age elder Solars. I know, more powerful, but it's really not a difference of orders of magnitude. At least they are explicitly something a Solar <i>could</i> become.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are you OK with your Solar PCs <i>eventually </i>gaining five Initative tracks themselves, once they are thousand year old elder Solars?<br /> <br /> Or are you inventing a Super-Special-NPC Tier just to out-class the PCs?<br /> <br /> Either is fine, but they both carry issues which you'll need to address at your table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366594#post1366594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So powerful elder exalted, even if we don't have them as of now, and probably won't see them anytime soon, are not something totally out of scope of how setting works in Exalted broadly construed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only we do have powerful elder Exalted. They don't have five Initiative tracks. Not even Ma-Ha-Suchi, who <i>can </i>take on five Solars at once (with twenty-ish mortal buddies).<br /> <br /> The elder Exalted we do have, do not even <i>remotely </i>work as if they had five Initative tracks. Mnemon doesn't work like that. Raksi doesn't work like that. Ma-Ha-Suchi doesn't work like that.<br /> <br /> The current design paradigm is that Essence 5 represents the most powerful effects possible for the Exalted. Essence 6+ is about customising your Essence to your personal nature.<br /> <br /> If you want to explicitly step out of the current design paradigm to make this happen anyway, then more power to you. But canonicly, I can't think of any examples in the fiction where a single elder takes on an entire Solar Circle single-handedly. The only example I can think of is Night Caste Akuma Assassin Gorol who killed the other four Solars in his Circle (who were at least 157 years younger than him), but there's no mention of whether he fought them all at once or assassinated them one at a time (before he got killed by two different Solars who ganged up on him).<br /> <br /> And the mechanics of the game (which, I concede, are explicitly not the physics of the universe) also don't support this.<br /> <br /> In fact the entire theme of Exalted (from Divine Rebellion to Usurpation) is that a big crowd of weaker beings can mob and kill anyone, no matter whether they're the Elder Gods who created existence, or the most powerful of the Exalted.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you can't homebrew your own mechanics to fit your head-canon: that's what Exalted is all about. And if you want to have an epic Nemesis Boss Fight, then Two-Snaking it (or Five-Snaking it) is probably the cleanest solution.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> How powerful should Solars be, given their narrative role?<br /> <br /> In my opinion: A Circle of Solars should be powerful enough to be able to challenge their elders. Not ridiculously curb stomp, but challenge.<br /> <br /> An elder (whether Solar, Sidereal, Lunar or Other) should be wary about taking on an entire Circle of fresh Solar Exalts (or experienced Dragon-Blooded), but should be able to beat them if they employ a clever strategy (like enlisting the help of a bunch of mortals, or practicing a specific type of Martial Art, or investing in Charms for fighting groups).<br /> <br /> Is giving an elder five Initiative tracks a good way of doing this?<br /> <br /> That depends entirely on your game and your expectations. But nothing in the current paradigm works like this, and I would be wary of giving NPCs that are supposed to be &quot;of a kind&quot; with the PCs powers which are far outside of what the PCs can achieve.<br /> <br /> If you want an elder Exalted who can take on an entire Circle, then you absolutely may use ST perrogative to &quot;cheat&quot;. I do. I don't make entire NPCs built like PCs, and I don't have to: I make Quick Characters with easy to use, thematic powers.<br /> <br /> If you want to run the Unconquered Sun as a boss fight, then giving him four Initiative tracks (one per arm) might be a good way of doing that. If you want to run a Primordial as a boss fight, then multiple Initative tracks is a good idea. Or a unique Behemoth.<br /> <br /> But if you want to give an elder Exalt extra Initative tracks, I suggest looking at stuff like Single Point and giving them actual abilities which the PCs can copy, or at least imitate. I don't suggest that you actually use the Single Point charms in the book as written (simplfy them for NPC use), but use them as a base so that when a PC turns around and says &quot;how do I get cool powers like that?&quot;, then you can flip open the book and tell them to go nuts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-09-2020, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T13:18:33-08:00","id":1366614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366612#post1366612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is giving an elder five Initiative tracks a good way of doing this?<br /> <br /> That depends entirely on your game and your expectations. But nothing in the current paradigm works like this, and I would be wary of giving NPCs that are supposed to be &quot;of a kind&quot; with the PCs powers which are far outside of what the PCs can achieve.<br /> <br /> If you want an elder Exalted who can take on an entire Circle, then you absolutely may use ST perrogative to &quot;cheat&quot;. I do. I don't make entire NPCs built like PCs, and I don't have to: I make Quick Characters with easy to use, thematic powers.<br /> <br /> If you want to run the Unconquered Sun as a boss fight, then giving him four Initiative tracks (one per arm) might be a good way of doing that.<br /> <br /> But if you want to give an elder Solar extra Initative tracks, I suggest looking at stuff like Single Point and giving them actual abilities which the PCs can copy, or at least imitate. I don't suggest that you actually use the Single Point charms in the book as written, but use them as a base so that when a PC turns around and says &quot;how do I get cool powers like that?&quot;, then you can flip open the book and tell them to go nuts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the whole point is rather simple : People want to do asymmetric gameplay like in DD to do some specific cool battle, and they try to find way to do it. I think it's fair and simple, and asking &quot;I should make NPC's that behave mechanically like the players, so I can't give them multiple initiative tracks/special powers/whatever because it doesn't work like the players do&quot; is a nonsense, because the core purpose of wanting to do asymmetric gameplay in order to do the trope of &quot;The old master taking everyone at the same time&quot;. <br /> <br /> So you're gonna say &quot;Yes but Exalted is not asymmetric gameplay&quot;, and I will answer &quot;Yes sadly this is the saddest thing that ever happened to the world&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T13:34:08-08:00","id":1366619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366612#post1366612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think so.<br /> <br /> Turn 1 Aim.<br /> Turn 2 Crash all the Solars.<br /> Turn 3 the Battlegroup acts before the Crashed Solars and attacks again, this time applying their attack to the Solar's Health Track.<br /> There is no Turn 4.<br /> <br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi is hard as nails.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm working under the assertion that some of the Solars won't be crashed in Turn 2 due to a combination of soak defence, extremely high initiative, making themselves invalid targets in turn 1 and pure dumb luck but yes, there's absolutely TPK potential here.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T13:38:50-08:00","id":1366620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366540#post1366540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I have trouble believing that a few dozen Dragonblooded couldn't do the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a few dozen powerful combat focused DBs absolutely could fight the Mask of Winters. The thing is, the Mask isn't some lone dude sitting in his house out in the middle of nowhere. For space I've spoiled just an example of what might await you in Thorns.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Close Allies/Pets</span><br /> <br /> <b>Mask of Winters</b><br /> An incredibly powerful Void Circle necromancer, and former First Age Solar ghost. Wearing a cape weighted down heavily by the hearthstones embedded into it, wearing ancient armor known as Grieving Shelter, and wielding the relic blade Frigid Razor he is a terrifying opponent. On his face he wears the Mask of Winters, depending on the side either enchantingly beautiful or sickeningly terrifying. Most deadly of all, the memory of his Solar life allows him, along with his fellow Deathlords, access the dark mirrors of Solar charms.<br /> <br /> <b>Juggernaut</b><br /> A behemoth of mind-boggling size, able to crush fortresses and armies with a single swipe of its massive hand. The beast is surrounded by a miasma of disease and rotting death, powerful enough to sicken and kill any living creature within days of exposure. A creature so large that the Mask of Winters constructed his primary fortress upon its back. Its legacy stretching back to the dawn of time, where it used to wrestle the great Elemental Dragons. Even the mighty Exalted of the First Age were unable to slay it, merely crippling the monster and forcing it to drag it's colossal broken limbs across the earth. It is said, indeed, that it can never be killed, save for one fated moment in time.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow of Ration Wings</b><br /> A Nephwrack who's company the Mask of Winters keeps. Part advisor, part sorcerous partner, part insane ally. The Shadow of Ration Wings dwells most commonly in the fortress upon the Juggernaut. It has spent the last several decades meticulously weaving it's dark necromancy into every bone and fiber of the behemoth. A powerful sorcerer as well as defender of Juggernaut, it commands the forces defending the fortress whenever the Mask is unable to do so himself.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Abyssals</span><br /> <br /> Below are examples of some of the Mask of Winters Abyssal Exalted. There are several more.<br /> <br /> <b>Apostate in Tatters</b><br /> Midnight caste Abyssal Exalted. A preacher of doom who wanders the streets of Thorns, twisting the minds and hearts of the mortals who still dwell there.<br /> <br /> <b>The Seven-Degreed Physician of Black Maladies</b><br /> Daybreak caste Abyssal Exalted. Apprentice necromancer to the Mask of Winters, the Physician has most recently been put to work devoting all of his time to mass summoning and animation. Sewing together twisting spine chains, summoning legions of undead, and effecting repairs upon the masks necromantic engines off war.<br /> <br /> <b>Typhon</b><br /> Dusk caste Abyssal Exalted. A deadly and stealthy archer in the service of the Mask of Winters. Used during the Mask's wars of conquest as a deadly warrior, but during the lulls in between battles he is sent out to hunt the Mask's enemies abroad.<br /> <br /> <b>Prince Respendant</b><br /> Daybreak caste Abyssal Exalted. A collector of art and artiface from the First Age and before. The Prince is the Mask's personal retriever, scouring the world for the deadliest and most potent ancient spells and devices to bring back to the vaults of Thorns. After years of his work they now burgeon with wonders of the lost ages.<br /> <br /> <b>Artist in Azure Blood</b><br /> Dusk caste Abyssal Exalted. The Mask's great champion. Rather than command troops in battle the Mask directs her to weave a tapestry of screams and blood through his foes. If any adversary is daring enough to challenge the Mask of Winters to single combat, he first requires that they beat his champion the same way. When he is inclined to oblige such a request, anyway.<br /> <br /> <b>Acrid Mist of the Moor</b><br /> Moonshadow caste Abyssal Exalted. The Mask's primary diplomat. One who's silver knives are only matched by her silver tongue. In truth Mist of the Moor is equal parts diplomat and assassin, sent as an envoy to neighboring kingdoms, and in her wake accidents seem to befall all those who would oppose the Mask's whims in that area.<br /> <br /> <b>Perfected tears Upon Alabaster Sorrow</b><br /> Day caste Abyssal Exalted. A special agent of the Mask of Winters, one who partakes in his most underhanded and ambitious schemes. Where most of the Mask's other agents have specific duties, Sorrow embodies the Masks will and whims at the time. A wildcard that the Mask may add to any of his other ventures.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Engines of War</span><br /> <br /> <b>Razor Ivory Tangle</b><br /> A construct of necromancy, a bonestrider. Towering above the battlefield, Eternal Ivory Pillar has been the end off hundreds, perhaps thousands, of the Mask's enemies. Able to gesture towards a group of soldiers and bid their bones to shatter, the shards flinging forth from their bodies and impaling their fellows as they do.<br /> <br /> <b>Eternal Frozen Pillar</b><br /> A warstrider made of soulsteel inlaced with blue jade. It wields the power of cold death. It wields a scythe in battle, one with an ethereal blade. It passes through flesh and steel without leaving a mark, but drags the souls of the living with it as it does. If it should ever need to destroy a solid object, the haft proves more than up to the task.<br /> <br /> <b>Doom of Black Skies</b><br /> A Soulsteel Warstrider with the rare ability to take flight. Shrouded, as it is, by shadow and smoke it can move silently over land or through the air, landing among it's prey like an enormous raptor and also silencing them, forever.<br /> <br /> <b>Siege Weapons</b><br /> Having looted Thorns and taken what the Prince Resplendent could give him from the surrounding area, the Mask's fortresses are equipped with all manner of first age weapons. Lightning Ballista, Implosion Bows, sorcerous tablets that explode in great firestorms when activated, and Sky Mantis Towers which bend the weather to his needs. The Mask also has a few weapons stored in his vaults that seldom been seen in Creation for the last two thousand years.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Forces</span><br /> <br /> <b>Ghostly Agents</b><br /> The Mask commands dozens, or perhaps hundreds, of ghosts from the Underworld. Mortwrights, Nemissaries, Barrow Hound hunters, and other, stranger things. These creatures watch over the lands and buildings of the Mask off Winters. Invisibly they haunt roads and forests, and when he commands it they surge forth on missions of assassination or information gathering.<br /> <br /> <b>War Ghosts</b><br /> Entire legions of ethereal warriors serve the Mask of Winters. Inhabiting and animating suits of armor, and plunging their ghostly blades into living foes, rending flesh as well as spirit as they do.<br /> <br /> <b>Bone Siders</b><br /> Born from the Puppeteer's Plauge, these animated skeletons are walking vectors for that supernatural disease. Even a small band of them is enough to kill an entire village, as their claws infect the living, who then tear their flesh off and cause the plague to erupt anew.<br /> <br /> <b>Giant Maggots</b><br /> Infesting the corpse-body of the Juggernaut are thousands of squirming fat white maggots. Growing to the size of elephants, and equipped with rending maws of razor sharp shredding fangs, they attempt to devour any creature not under the protection off the Mask's invitation.<br /> <br /> <b>Zombies</b><br /> Near endless tides of once human citizens, now turned into shambling corpses. Fodder for the Mask's wars. Their tireless limbs and gut-wrenching stench overpower most foes. Even those that can boast defeating a horde of the Mask's zombies almost never do so without becoming exhausted. Completely drained from hours of hewing undead limbs, they're easy prey for the Deathlord's other forces. When lead by Shadow of Ration Wings, the zombies become far deadlier. Empowered by the Dawn of Dead Stars they often overpower even trained soldiers.<br /> <br /> <b>Human Forces</b><br /> After subjugating Thorns the Mask of Winters has had his pick of loyal human warriors. Their souls worn down to surrender and rebuild by the Mask and his Abyssal Exalted. Legions of trained and equipped former soldiers of Thorns now serve him. In addition to their battlefield roles they often act as spies or traitors to any resistance force attempting to overthrow the Mask's rule.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's not everything the Mask has, and a lot of those headings were abbreviated. Fighting the Mask of Winters is way WAY more than just beating up the Mask in his throne room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T13:40:58-08:00","id":1366621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366614#post1366614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the whole point is rather simple : People want to do asymmetric gameplay like in DD to do some specific cool battle, and they try to find way to do it. I think it's fair and simple, and asking &quot;I should make NPC's that behave mechanically like the players, so I can't give them multiple initiative tracks/special powers/whatever because it doesn't work like the players do&quot; is a nonsense, because the core purpose of wanting to do asymmetric gameplay in order to do the trope of &quot;The old master taking everyone at the same time&quot;.<br /> <br /> So you're gonna say &quot;<b>Yes but Exalted is not asymmetric gameplay</b>&quot;, and I will answer &quot;Yes sadly this is the saddest thing that ever happened to the world&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted is about you playing some of the most powerful beings in existence. Not the most powerful, but among the most powerful.<br /> <br /> It's about you being able to save, or at least <i>change</i>, the world.<br /> <br /> I have no issue with asymetric gameplay if you're doing stuff like fighting Primordials, or the Celestines, or a Greater Elemental Dragon, or a massive Behemoth.<br /> <br /> But your PCs are Exalted. And if you start handing out Mega-Charms to <i>the Exalted</i> then your PCs are going to want those Charms for themselves.<br /> <br /> And that's a perfectly reasonable expectation for your PCs to have. Because you are playing <b>Exalted</b>.<br /> <br /> Plus, you are playing Exalted -- that's a sword which cuts both ways. Open your Corebook to page 444: there's a Charm that means you get to Counterattack every single time you are attacked (Withering or Decisive, your choice). Flip to 434: there's a Charm that gives you an extra Initative track. Page 348: Ignore all Onslaught penalties. Page 353: Launch a Withering attack against ALL foes (and if you Crash one, launch a Decisive Attack against all foes). You want Reflexive Clashes? Sure you do. Page 352 has you covered.<br /> <br /> These effects all exist. Already. In canon.<br /> <br /> Simplfy them for your QC elders -- just like all the published QC elders have a simplified array of Charms.<br /> <br /> You explicitly do not have to use the same rules that the PCs use. But you also don't have to reinvent the wheel by giving NPCs untouchable superpowers.<br /> <br /> If you're fighting something that is supposed to be of a kind with the PCs, then it should be of a kind with the PCs.<br /> If you're doing asymmetric gameplay against anything else, then it should be a suitably epic, world-ending threat - not Jim-Bob the Random Raksha Noble (which, I acknowledge, no-one is suggesting anything contrary to this).<br /> <br /> I would find it <i>deeply </i>unsatisfying if I went to fight Ma-Ha-Suchi (or Mnemon, Raksi, Lethiathan or CK) and found that they just ignored the rules and got to take five actions each round &quot;because they're an elder&quot;.<br /> <br /> Whereas if that elder were using some version of Charms that I could buy (if I invested the XP), even if they didn't work <i>exactly </i>the same way, then that would feel a lot &quot;fairer&quot; to me (even though being able to Reflexively Clash five times a round AND then take your combat action is probably more powerful than &quot;just&quot; having five Initative tracks).<br /> <br /> And I explicitly reject the idea that an elder Exalt should be <i>qualitiatively</i> more powerful than the PCs. Quantitively, sure. Socially? Of course. But this is Dragon Ball Z.<br /> <br /> I think the worst thing you can do is get in an arms race with your players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-09-2020, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T13:50:02-08:00","id":1366623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366612#post1366612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only we do have powerful elder Exalted. They don't have five Initiative tracks.<br /> [...]<br /> The current design paradigm is that Essence 5 represents the most powerful effects possible for the Exalted. Essence 6+ is about customising your Essence to your personal nature.<br /> [...]<br /> [T]he mechanics of the game (which, I concede, are explicitly not the physics of the universe) also don't support this.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, I understand the current paradigm. We are now discussing whether we like it or not, so invoking that paradigm completely misses the point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366612#post1366612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there elder exalted who can defeat a whole circle? (Well, there's Ma-Ha-Suchi.)<br /> From what book are you getting this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chejop Kejak, Deathlords (It's not entirely clear how powerful they should vs, say, Merela). More generally: do you honestly think that I would have the same complaint in Second or First edition? Because looking at the rules back there, it's really easy to build and opponent who will just stomp over a circle of Essence 2 Solars sticking to the book. I mean, to me, elders are now clearly and intentionally weaker. They used to be stronger. Do you disagree about that?<br /> <br /> And I would say that if at some point many people thought that it's good to have elders who function like that it's simply not totally outside of the scope of Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366612#post1366612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is giving an elder five Initiative tracks a good way of doing this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I think that you are focusing too much on this specific example (which we of course can discuss!). My point was this: everyone here agrees that there is some arrangement of enemies which can take down five Solars. If this is the case, a single enemy can do the same: just let them act mechanically as that arrangement.<br /> <br /> Of course, this has to be carried out carefully and with attention paid to details and playtested. Sure. I think that in practice, probably some stronger charms plus two-three Initiative tracks would be enough for Essence 1-2 Solars, but I'd like to first check it. This sounds scary, but remember that it's strictly weaker than simply pitting your players against two or three opponents with the same stats and I believe that 2 Essence 4 Abyssals would not be overwhelming against 5 Essence 2 Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366612#post1366612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are you OK with your Solar PCs <i>eventually </i>gaining five Initative tracks themselves, once they are thousand year old elder Solars?<br /> <br /> Or are you inventing a Super-Special-NPC Tier just to out-class the PCs?<br /> <br /> Either is fine, but they both carry issues which you'll need to address at your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that's a very good point and I was thinking a lot about it. I guess at the end of the day I would be fine with making a Super-Special NPC Tier.<br /> <br /> However, I agree with the sentiment you expressed. I also don't like NPC-only powers if PCs are roughly of the same kind. So my preferred solution is that the powers that make elder stronger are accessible to PCs but they are prohibitive: you need to wait a long time (i.e., it's not accessible via Supernal). You have to be somehow unusually combat-focused to really access them. You get them gradually.<br /> <br /> Of course, this generates an arms' race, so you want to balance everything so that if some players finally got this power, there's still something that can defeat them without things getting totally out of control.<br /> <br /> I proposed one solution in this thread. It does involve extra Initiative tracks. I tried to balance that idea around the assumption that an Essence 3 Solar should be a serious challenge to 2-3 Essence 1 Solars and Essence 5 Solar should be a serious challenge to 2-3 Essence 3 Solars (and probably so on). Moreover, a fight of two combat-oriented Solars of the same Essence rating should not result in a rocket tag.<br /> <br /> I think that some sort of extra Initiative tracks is the cheapest way to do it, but I'm not overly attached to this particular solution.<br /> <br /> EDIT: By the way, I explicitly discussed with the players that they shouldn't feel overly attached to the charms introducing extra Initiative tracks, because it's still work in progress and very likely to change.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-09-2020, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T13:59:47-08:00","id":1366626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366614#post1366614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're gonna say &quot;Yes but Exalted is not asymmetric gameplay&quot;, and I will answer &quot;Yes sadly this is the saddest thing that ever happened to the world&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Only for Solars though, and part of that is the on the players...kind of. I'm with John, I can't blame players for wanting to take awesome charms if you give them awesome charms, but in the Tomb of Dreams quickstart there's an example of what a starting group of Solars <i>could </i>look like, and it's absolutely able to lose to a powerful elder exalt in a straight fight.<br /> <br /> It's true that the characters don't quite have full starting character stats, but it's also true that they've spent bonus points, and the only thing most of them are missing is some charms and merits. With that here are their stats.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Volfer<br /> 8 attack dice<br /> 8 defense dice<br /> Light armor<br /> <br /> Fire Orchid<br /> 7 attack dice<br /> 7 defense dice<br /> Medium Armor<br /> <br /> Iay<br /> 4 attack dice<br /> 4 defense dice<br /> Light Armor<br /> <br /> Faka<br /> 10 attack dice<br /> 10 defense dice (Thumbs up, you're built like a normal PC)<br /> NO armor (And you ruined it)<br /> <br /> Mirror Flag<br /> 5 attack dice<br /> 6 defense dice<br /> Medium Armor<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T14:06:06-08:00","id":1366630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366623#post1366623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chejop Kejak, Deathlords (It's not entirely clear how powerful they should vs, say, Merela). More generally: do you honestly think that I would have the same complaint in Second or First edition? Because looking at the rules back there, it's really easy to build and opponent who will just stomp over a circle of Essence 2 Solars sticking to the book. I mean, to me, elders are now clearly and intentionally weaker. They used to be stronger. Do you disagree about that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but also in Second Edition players used to be able to start the game at Essence 5. Normal Solars? Oh yeah, Essence 2, maybe 3. Player Characters? Essence 4-5 almost always.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366623#post1366623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I think that you are focusing too much on this specific example (which we of course can discuss!). My point was this: everyone here agrees that there is some arrangement of enemies which can take down five Solars. If this is the case, a single enemy can do the same: just let them act mechanically as that arrangement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you might run into issues because almost any enemy like that in Exalted also has innumerable incredibly powerful forces at their command as well. If the Mask of Winters can beat a full circle of Solars on his own, what happens when you fight the Mask, 3 of his Abyssals, and a battlegroup of ghosts all at once? Or even just one after the other, when the circle of Abyssals wore you down, the Nephwrack took almost everything you had left, and then the Mask comes in with his personal guard?<br /> <br /> There's very very few major foes in Exalted who act alone like that, most of them are Behemoths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T14:09:31-08:00","id":1366632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366623#post1366623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, I understand the current paradigm. We are now discussing whether we like it or not, so invoking that paradigm completely misses the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, in that case: I like the current paradigm.<br /> <br /> You're playing Exalted. If you want to play a peasant who gets beaten up, play D&amp;D and start at level 1.<br /> This is Exalted, where you play the champions of the gods, returned to conquer/save the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366623#post1366623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chejop Kejak, Deathlords (It's not entirely clear how powerful they should vs, say, Merela).</div> </div> </div> </div>And can you cite a single instance where CK or the Deathlords fought an entire Circle of Solars? They don't even have to have won, just give me a book and page reference for when the fight happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366623#post1366623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More generally: do you honestly think that I would have the same complaint in Second or First edition? Because looking at the rules back there, it's really easy to build and opponent who will just stomp over a circle of Essence 2 Solars sticking to the book. I mean, to me, elders are now clearly and intentionally weaker. They used to be stronger. Do you disagree about that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if you would have had that complaint in Second Edition. Ever fight Kejak in 2.5? (2.0 Kejak was a beast, no bones about it. 2.5... not so much.)<br /> <br /> The power curve is flatter now. I'll give you that. I'd posit that this is desirable - the PCs are supposed to matter, not be playing &quot;race to Essence 6&quot; or sitting on the sidelines whilst the untouchable elders duke it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366623#post1366623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I think that you are focusing too much on this specific example (which we of course can discuss!). My point was this: everyone here agrees that there is some arrangement of enemies which can take down five Solars. If this is the case, a single enemy can do the same: just let them act mechanically as that arrangement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically, I think you have to be very careful doing this.<br /> <br /> Just because there is some combination of enemies that can defeat Superman, that does not mean it's a good idea to forge them into a single gestalt entity to fight Superman one-on-one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366623#post1366623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, that's a very good point and I was thinking a lot about it. I guess at the end of the day I would be fine with making a Super-Special NPC Tier.<br /> <br /> However, I agree with the sentiment you expressed. I also don't like NPC-only powers if PCs are roughly of the same kind. So my preferred solution is that the powers that make elder stronger are accessible to PCs but they are prohibitive: you need to wait a long time (i.e., it's not accessible via Supernal). You have to be somehow unusually combat-focused to really access them. You get them gradually.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's between you and your players: I think this is a good approach FWIW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366623#post1366623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, this generates an arms' race, so you want to balance everything so that if some players finally got this power, there's still something that can defeat them without things getting totally out of control.<br /> <br /> I proposed one solution in this thread. It does involve extra Initiative tracks. I tried to balance that idea around the assumption that an Essence 3 Solar should be a serious challenge to 2-3 Essence 1 Solars and Essence 5 Solar should be a serious challenge to 2-3 Essence 3 Solars (and probably so on). Moreover, a fight of two combat-oriented Solars of the same Essence rating should not result in a rocket tag.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, here I disagree.<br /> <br /> The Solars fight a Super-Solar at Essence 3. Ok, fair enough, there's not a lot (by intentional design choice) that can challenge an Essence 3 Solar (but you don't like the design so have home-brewed something more fun).<br /> Then the PCs fight an Ascended-Super-Solar at Essence 5... and at this point I'd be suggesting we pack up Exalted and give Gloomhaven a go. But lets say your players are into that.<br /> Then you scale up to Super-Solar-God-Super-Solars... and it just begs the question, &quot;where were these Super Special NPCs when the world was in danger three stories ago, man?&quot;<br /> <br /> The default setting has a power ceiling. It's there for a reason. Solars intentionally start near that ceiling. That's a core game assumption. (And change it if you will, but really: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366621#post1366621\">take a good long look at all the powerful things Solars can do in canon</a> and ask yourself if this is REALLY a ceiling that you want to raise.)<br /> <br /> You have every right to homebrew and golden rule the game the way you want it to be, but you're changing a feature, not a bug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-10-2020, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T14:12:43-08:00","id":1366633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366626#post1366626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only for Solars though, and part of that is the on the players...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is still one of the points of the debate (I know I'm repeating myself, but I also know that some people will read this thread only from page 4+). It is clear that some people here would like Solars not to be <i>literally</i> the most powerful human-sized agents in the world. You can want them to be extremely powerful returning rulers of the worlds, while still keeping some decent margin in power levels. Other splats simply don't support the same (iconic!) narrative.<br /> <br /> And it's not exactly something unusual in other media. You may want to play Aang from the Last Airbender, be constantly reminded how powerful you are, and eventually getting exactly that powerful, without casually mowing through any opposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-09-2020, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T14:45:46-08:00","id":1366637,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366632#post1366632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're playing Exalted. If you want to play a peasant who gets beaten up, play D&amp;D and start at level 1.<br /> This is Exalted, where you play the champions of the gods, returned to conquer/save the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh, you know it's not exactly an honest argument. There is a lot of room for players to be champions of goods without eliminating totally a room for their nemesis. For what it's worth, my favourite handling of power levels is Mage: the Awakening, 2 ed, followed by Mage: the Ascension (pre-Revised) or, recently, Trinity: Aeon.<br /> <br /> As a matter of fact, the protagonists in these setting don't really strike me as any weaker than Solar Exalted in terms of their actual capabilities, despite the &quot;hype&quot; surrounding the latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366632#post1366632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The power curve is flatter now. I'll give you that. I'd posit that this is desirable - the PCs are supposed to matter, not be playing &quot;race to Essence 6&quot; or sitting on the sidelines whilst the untouchable elders duke it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I often meet this sentiment (mostly, I remember it from discussions about Vampire: the Masquarade). I have to admit that to me that position is almost a cultural shock. I think that there is some deep difference in expectations and experiences.<br /> <br /> For me elder-like beings were always a kind of plot devices. As plot devices, they should be handled with care. You take active measures to make sure that they don't invalidate the struggles of your players. Something that player characters may <i>potentially</i> become, in distant horizon. They are mostly there to be cryptically mentioned and to remind the players that setting is overwhelmingly vast with stories going back to the past millenia. And, incidentally, to be to your players, what Darth Vader was in Star Wars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366632#post1366632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a core game assumption. You have every right to homebrew and golden rule the game the way you want it to be, but you're changing a feature, not a bug.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really think it's questionable whether it's <i>the</i> core assumption. When I read the first edition corebook, the pcs are clearly not handled by default as the main shakers and rulers of the world. There is even an explicit advice to that effect. I don't see that assumption when I look at the list of references. I think part of this assumption really stems from the Internet culture surrounding Exalted.<br /> <br /> (However, you definitely know Exalted better and from the longer time than I do.)<br /> <br /> You know, you can be Neo, the Chosen One in the original Matrix and you can be Neo from further two sequels. I believe that both characters realise the premise of Exalted, but only the second version really reaches the ceiling. (It's slightly dishonest argument, since the two latter movies are bad. They could be good, but they are bad partly because it's hard to build proper drama with such a powerful character). Honestly, if I were to play with characters so close to the ceiling, I'd probably prefer some more narrative game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-09-2020, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T15:22:46-08:00","id":1366641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366637#post1366637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really think it's questionable whether it's <i>the</i> core assumption. When I read the first edition corebook, the pcs are clearly not handled by default as the main shakers and rulers of the world. There is even an explicit advice to that effect. I don't see that assumption when I look at the list of references. I think part of this assumption really stems from the Internet culture surrounding Exalted.<br /> <br /> (However, you definitely know Exalted better and from the longer time than I do.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't claim to be an expert on Exalted. I'm an expert on the Exalted games <i>which I have played</i>. That's very different.<br /> <br /> But if we're talking 1E, flip open your corebook to Chapter 1: Setting and read the first paragraph under the subheading &quot;The Exalted&quot; for me. Then read the &quot;High and Low&quot; sidebar on the next page.<br /> <br /> Solars are described as being above the greatest paragons of the human race, &quot;unexcelled&quot; in their area of focus and &quot;excellent&quot; in all things. &quot;Cosmic beings&quot; able to go toe-to-toe with other Celestial Exalted, able to &quot;bring the Realm to its knees&quot;.<br /> <br /> The very next page has this exact line: &quot;The Solar Exalted are the mightiest of the Exalted&quot;. The Antagonists chapter states &quot;The most dangerous foe an Exalted can face is one of her own kind&quot;.<br /> <br /> I will give you that Chapter 7 states &quot;don't confuse power level with drama&quot; and &quot;your PCs are not necessarily the most important people in the world&quot;. But it also (literally) states the PCs &quot;<i>can</i> be the most important people in the world&quot; and &quot;there's no such thing as 'over the top'&quot;. And the section on genre convetions begins with &quot;large scale&quot; and &quot;epic&quot;.<br /> <br /> The most important thing in the 1E rulebook is this line: Nobody - not us, not gaming magazines, not other gamers on the Internet - can tell you that the way you're playing is wrong.<br /> <br /> If you want to play that there are man-sized foes who can beat down Solars five-to-one, then I'm not being sarcastic when I say to enjoy yourself. I genuinely want you to have fun. And you're right, when you watch Ninja Scroll or Crouching Tiger Hidden Dragon the protagonists aren't unstoppable. And if what your gaming group wants is to wail on a Darth Vader five-on-one then you don't need my blessing (but you have it anyway).<br /> <br /> But Solars being powerful* isn't a meme. It's not &quot;Internet culture&quot;. It is, and always has been, a default assumption of the game.<br /> <br /> In 3E Solars can (already, in canon) attack everyone who attacks them, then either [make three seperate single attacks on their turn / or attack all foes within Close range at least once, and potentially an infinite number of times until out of motes / or attack once with an un-Clashable attack outside of Initiative order] then take a single extra attack (but not really, because every time I've said &quot;single attack&quot; that could be something like Tripple Attack Technique or Iron Whirlwind Technique and thus be three to five attacks). And you're talking about adding homebrew powers on top of that to create new power tiers. I'm not saying &quot;don't do it&quot;: if you're going to have fun with this then you definitely should do it. All I'm saying is &quot;approach with caution&quot;.<br /> <br /> *In Universe. Other settings have characters WAY more powerful than Second Age Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-10-2020, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T15:43:40-08:00","id":1366647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366641#post1366641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The Solar Exalted are the mightiest of the Exalted&quot;<br /> [...]<br /> [I]t also (literally) states the PCs &quot;<i>can</i> be the most important people in the world&quot; and &quot;there's no such thing as 'over the top'&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with all these claims, I just tend to interpret them differently. I think they might be, and partially were, understood in terms of raw potential: up to literally cosmic scale in the high Essence rating.<br /> <br /> We clearly won't reach agreement any soon on this topic, but I'm happy we can disagree in a friendly atmosphere. I'm also positive that you have great fun with your game an how you play it. So do enjoy it!<br /> <br /> (I'm mostly so militant about this, because a couple of years ago, the atmosphere on this forum seemed to be rather unpleasant towards the kind of tropes that were dismissed in the transition to the third edition. I think it's important to at least present these views here, since most people with such sentiments simply expressed their frustration, sometimes in somewhat aggressive tone, and left the forum.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-09-2020, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T17:44:18-08:00","id":1366665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366633#post1366633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is still one of the points of the debate (I know I'm repeating myself, but I also know that some people will read this thread only from page 4+). It is clear that some people here would like Solars not to by <i>literally</i> the most powerful human-sized agents in the world. You can want them to be extremely powerful returning rulers of the worlds, while still keeping some decent margin in power levels. Other splats simply don't support the same (iconic!) narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be a bit confused here so I'm not quite sure how to respond. What is the narrative that you're wanting to tell that other splats can't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T17:52:04-08:00","id":1366666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366633#post1366633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is still one of the points of the debate (I know I'm repeating myself, but I also know that some people will read this thread only from page 4+). It is clear that some people here would like Solars not to by <i>literally</i> the most powerful human-sized agents in the world. You can want them to be extremely powerful returning rulers of the worlds, while still keeping some decent margin in power levels. Other splats simply don't support the same (iconic!) narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars don't need to be the best at everything forever to carry out the iconic narrative. <br /> Solars don't even need to be the best at more than a handful of things to carry out the iconic narrative. <br /> Solars certainly neither need to blow every other splat out of the water nor reach near-full potential in their specialty from day zero to carry out the iconic narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T18:07:20-08:00","id":1366669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366666#post1366666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars don't need to be the best at everything forever to carry out the iconic narrative.<br /> Solars don't even need to be the best at more than a handful of things to carry out the iconic narrative.<br /> Solars certainly neither need to blow every other splat out of the water nor reach near-full potential in their specialty from day zero to carry out the iconic narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think maybe Lanic is saying that he wants to tell a campaign with returning lawgivers, who also aren't the people who have the most potential for personal power in the setting. Which Exalted doesn't really do that well as a default, much like it doesn't do the DnD druid style character who's the iconic shapeshifter but also wielder of the natural elements. You can be a DB and be an element wielder, or a Lunar and be a beastial shapeshifter, but not both at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T18:08:50-08:00","id":1366670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366665#post1366665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might be a bit confused here so I'm not quite sure how to respond. What is the narrative that you're wanting to tell that other splats can't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the standard stuff: you are the returning ruler of the world who now can deal with its problems. I didn't mean anything complicated.<br /> <br /> With Lunars, with Dragon-Blooded, or with Sidereals, the central premise is fundamentally different. You are a warewolf/a twisted crazy witch; you are a member of the ruling class of superpowered individuals who are explicitly not the strongest in the world; you are a kung-fu agent secretely controlling the world.<br /> <br /> If you play these splats, you naturally tell different stories, even when the plot is similar. There is something very unique in Solars, even if you completely ignore their power-level. I think that Aang from <i>The Last Airbendender</i> perfectly fits into the Solar archetype, and yet, he isn't automatically winning every fight until he reaches his full potential.<br /> <br /> @vwlls trnt prncss I'm weirdly confused, because I absolutely agree with what you wrote, and I think I was trying to say similar things. And yet, your post seems somehow polemic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I explicitly meant that other splats are not well suited for telling &quot;Solar-like&quot; stories not because they are not as powerful as Solars, but because they are not the returning rightful heroes.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366665#post1366665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[H]e wants to tell a campaign with returning lawgivers, who also aren't the people who have the most potential for personal power in the setting. Which Exalted doesn't really do that well as a default[.]</div> </div> </div> </div>That's almost exactly my position. I'm totally ok with the <i>potential</i> for being the most powerful agent in the setting. I'm really ok, with being pretty much the most powerful agent you will meet. I simply think there should be more space for people who still are more powerful than you, as you start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-09-2020, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T18:53:01-08:00","id":1366678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366670#post1366670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's almost exactly my position. I'm totally ok with the <i>potential</i> for being the most powerful agent in the setting. I'm really ok, with being pretty much the most powerful agent you will meet. I simply think there should be more space for people who still are more powerful than you, as you start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's something you're going to have to homebrew away, unfortunately. Divorcing Solars from that is like divorcing them from the fact that they glow with the colours of the sun when they spend lots of essence.<br /> <br /> That being said, I'm not saying that any Solar automatically wins against whatever they might come across. Just that Solars are strong enough that nothing else in the setting is really five times as strong as they are. Which is the real hurdle that's almost impossible to get over. It doesn't really matter even if you made a Solar who's not living up to your full potential and the antagonist actually IS stronger than your Dawn. He might be solidly stronger than your Dawn, but he's definitely not five times stronger.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think you might be pidgeonholing the non-Solar Exalted a bit though. You can definitely play Dragonblooded Aang. He's an Immaculate of Air, one who's part of an ancient sect that wants to see the Empire stop invading other countries. He was frozen in ice, and the rest of his fellows were killed 1,000 years ago, but now he's back. He's going to go through and learn the wisdom of the other five elements, growing as he masters the Dragon styles until the point where he can challenge the next Emperor to a duel, and defeat him, proving the righteousness of his cause.<br /> <br /> Also, since he's not a Solar he won't be instantly murdered by the other people in the world, and can actually challenge the emperor to a duel without it becoming a massacre. If a Solar showed up to challenge Emperor Cathak Ozai and flared golden that's instantly every DB with their weapons out trying to kill you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T19:32:03-08:00","id":1366682,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a><br /> <br /> I think you're exaggerate how much Solars are <i>supposed </i> to dominate the rest of the setting (as opposed to how they actually dominate it under the current game mechanics). One of the examples of Solar-type hero given in the first edition core book is Conan. So apparently not some portrayed to be unbeatable (I haven't read it, so maybe it feels different than a layman would guess.)<br /> <br /> I also think that you're somewhat exaggerating how my position differs from the premises of the game. A possibility of a single human-type opponent confronting the whole circle isn't something particularly new. It simply was made much harder in third edition. On purpose. By the way, I understand the purpose, but we really don't have to reinvent the wheel here. Just make the power curve in the Essence progression somewhat steeper, given elder higher numbers and some significantly more powerful charms.<br /> <br /> And &quot;five-times more powerful&quot; than a Solar might seem radical, but mostly due to the fact that design trends in rpg generally went into direction of making game mechanics more tightly balanced. Meanwhile, many games in '90s to early '00s could easily handle such power gaps so that a whole party can loose to a single more experienced opponent. I understand the current design principles and the purpose of tightly designed games, adhering to principles of good board-game design, but I strongly believe that in this particular case of Exalted, current design principles are detrimental to the game.<br /> <br /> And I don't think that these power gaps could not be transplanted to example. There were simple design elements that enable it: mostly just a bit wider spread of numbers and fiddling with the action economy. Multiple actions and wider spreads of numbers were present in DnD, especially 3-4ed., Shadowrun, Warhammer, Burning Wheel, Earthdawn to name just a few of them (ok, in this case people didn't like it and it seemed to be poorly executed, but power gaps were very strongly present),<br /> <br /> Well, I just hope this will change. 15 years ago no one could guess that we will have both Vampire: Requiem and Vampire: the Masquarade, and the latter will be an intimate game of personal horror and the former will have no problem with elders and cosmic plots. I would pay any money for a game with the design quality that martial arts have in Exalted, third edtion and power gaps of Mage.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you might be pidgeonholing the non-Solar Exalted a bit though. You can definitely play Dragonblooded Aang. He's an Immaculate of Air, one who's part of an ancient sect that wants to see the Empire stop invading other countries. He was frozen in ice, and the rest of his fellows were killed 1,000 years ago, but now he's back. He's going to go through and learn the wisdom of the other five elements, growing as he masters the Dragon styles until the point where he can challenge the next Emperor to a duel, and defeat him, proving the righteousness of his cause. </div> </div> </div>Mhm, but <i>this</i> Aang will not be able to eventually become the completely dominating power, destroying whole fleets, like the Avatar used to be. You are giving up on a half of this narrative somewhere anyway.<br /> <br /> If there was a splat starting at the power level of Dragon-Blooded and dominating everyone else by Essence 5, I'd probably not be complaining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-09-2020, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T22:00:04-08:00","id":1366695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366682#post1366682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're exaggerate how much Solars are <i>supposed </i> to dominate the rest of the setting (as opposed to how they actually dominate it under the current game mechanics). One of the examples of Solar-type hero given in the first edition core book is Conan. So apparently not some portrayed to be unbeatable (I haven't read it, so maybe it feels different than a layman would guess.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, of course. If you're just one Solar warrior who's out in the wastes somewhere, Conan style, your impact on the setting is likely to be almost nil. If you venture close to a population center there's a real good chance you're going to call down a Wyld Hunt and be unceremoniously murdered out on some dusty road somewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366682#post1366682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that you're somewhat exaggerating how my position differs from the premises of the game. A possibility of a single human-type opponent confronting the whole circle isn't something particularly new. It simply was made much harder in third edition. On purpose. By the way, I understand the purpose, but we really don't have to reinvent the wheel here. Just make the power curve in the Essence progression somewhat steeper, given elder higher numbers and some significantly more powerful charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if it was just Deathlords? Incarna, Ishvara, Yozi, Primordials, Neverborn, Directional Dragons, Behemoths, Greater Elemental Dragons, Third Circle Demons, and Directional War Gods can all put up a fight against a circle of Solars, depending on the circle. If everyone will full hog combat Alhat might not do so well, but the other ones sure. Deathlords are kind of in a weird space where they have legions of nations that serve them, but they're also lumped in with Incarna and Primordials and stuff for some effects. Maybe on the low-side, like Alhat style?<br /> <br /> <br /> A kind of problem that I DO have with Exalted, even 3e, is that it's way too easy to make your character amazing at combat. Or most things really, but we're talking about combat. Like I said previously if only the Dawn was a great fighter and everyone else was kind of middling, you could do it. That's not how it's set up though, and I'm not sure if that's a good thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366682#post1366682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a>Mhm, but <i>this</i> Aang will not be able to eventually become the completely dominating power, destroying whole fleets, like the Avatar used to be. You are giving up on a half of this narrative somewhere anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, even if you're a Solar you're not going to do that. You're one Solar among 300, even if we say that Solars are so beyond all the other exalted that even Lunars and the like don't matter.<br /> <br /> Also, for what it's worth, Essence 5 Dragonblooded can absolutely destroy entire fleets of ships with a single action, and even have charms that, at Storyteller discretion, seal away even beings the likes of Deathlords and Yozi into colossal earthen tombs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366682#post1366682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there was a splat starting at the power level of Dragon-Blooded and dominating everyone else by Essence 5, I'd probably not be complaining.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could always just make an exigent that does that, although without houserules he won't end up more powerful than the theoretical Solars around the same level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T22:08:05-08:00","id":1366697,"title":"","content":"This is all so muddled because &quot;Solars&quot; mean such an incredible wide range of things. I think to have a meaningful discussion tomorrow night I'm going to have to stat up two full chargen Solar circles and reference them as like &quot;Punchface Circle&quot; and &quot;Other Circle&quot; or something.<br /> <br /> 'cause like Alhat WRECKS the Tomb of Dreams guys, but doesn't stand much of a chance against a circle otherwise built to fight him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T22:15:37-08:00","id":1366700,"title":"","content":"See here, Volfer from Tomb of Dreams should not be used to benchmark Dawn Solar anything. I recall him being chunked by JohnDoe\u2019s Deeb in two rounds.<br /> <br /> Granted, JohnDoe\u2019s Deeb is a mass murdering conglomerate of interlocking mechanics, but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T22:46:28-08:00","id":1366701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366700#post1366700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See here, Volfer from Tomb of Dreams should not be used to benchmark Dawn Solar anything. I recall him being chunked by JohnDoe\u2019s Deeb in two rounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but JohnDoe's DB was just about as powerful as DBs get, and was Essence 3 to boot. Volfer himself isn't <i>really </i>that bad, he's just not as good as he could be. He's missing six charms, but he's got seven combat charms already, so you might only give him one or two more.<br /> <br /> That's the thing though, do you do this:<br /> <br /> Thunderclap Rush<br /> Stubborn Boar<br /> Excellent Strike<br /> Fire and Stones<br /> One Weapon Two Blows<br /> Tiger's Dread Symmetry<br /> Durability of Oak Meditation<br /> Spirit Strengthens Skin<br /> Fists of Iron<br /> Food Gathering Exercise<br /> Friendship with Animals Approach<br /> Drifting Leaf Elusion<br /> Dipping Swallow<br /> Sensory Acuity Prana<br /> Ox Body<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Or do you do this?<br /> <br /> Excellent Strike<br /> Fire and Stones Strike<br /> Rising Sun Slash<br /> Divine Executioner Stance<br /> One Weapon Two Blows<br /> Peony Blossom Attack<br /> Iron Whilrwind Attack<br /> Invincible Fury of the Dawn<br /> Dipping Swallow Defense<br /> Bulwark Stance<br /> Fivefold Bulwark Stance<br /> Hail Shattering Practice<br /> Perfect Strike Discipline<br /> Gleaming Sever<br /> Heavenly Guardian Defense<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> One of those guys can easily take on all three of the corebook Immaculates at the same time, the other definitely can't. That's also just the Dawn, who's supposed to be fighty. The other characters get far, far more swingy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T01:33:16-08:00","id":1366714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366700#post1366700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See here, Volfer from Tomb of Dreams should not be used to benchmark Dawn Solar anything. I recall him being chunked by JohnDoe\u2019s Deeb in two rounds.<br /> <br /> Granted, JohnDoe\u2019s Deeb is a mass murdering conglomerate of interlocking mechanics, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the nicest thing anyone has ever said to me.<br /> <br /> BTW <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1366712#post1366712\">it takes 4 rounds for a starting level Dragon-Blooded to chunk Volfer</a>.<br /> <br /> (But DrLoveMonkey is correct, give him six Charms and the Artifact you get at the end of Tomb of Dreams and Volfer isn't <i>that</i> bad.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T01:49:46-08:00","id":1366715,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit sad because I seem to arrive after the war, but I'll post some of my comments on the discussion nonetheless.<br /> <br /> \u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> I don't think we agree on what is asymmetric gameplay ? (I'm not saying I have the good definition, just we don't seem to think about it in the same way). To me, asymmetric is when the ST doesn't work the same way as the PC's. It doesn't mean the ST is stronger, or the ST is weaker, just that they are different, and use different tools to function and represent their action on the game. The games of the Apocalypse have asymmetric gameplay because the ST rolls no dice and only functions through narrative opposition and calling rolls on the players. DD is actually mainly symmetric because most NPC's have the same functioning as the PC's (AC, HP, scores based on their statistics, spells, etc ...) but have asymmetric elements as well (DD5 has lair actions, epic actions, powers recharging on a d6).<br /> <br /> In this perspective, to take an example (that I don't think this is necessarily the best one as said Lanic, but it's just an example), what are these X tracks of initiative per turn ? Should the PC's be angry because Deathlord Kejak of the Changing Moon do it and the PC's don't ? The answer is no, and here is why : it's not a &quot;Charm&quot; in the game, it's game mechanic of making Kejak works to explicitly portray the &quot;long complicated battle against a master that can challenge 5 heroes alone&quot; (if you buy into that trope). This does not mean that Kejak always has 5 initiative tracks, this means the way of representing his prowess through this fight against the PC's, and make it closer to the mentioned trope, is through this mechanic. Why the players do not need it ? Because when the players are masters at Essence 5, and they want to crush some newbie, the system already supports that : they play normally and crush them, because they are master at Essence 5, and with the Core Rules, except if the ST is an asshole that makes the &quot;newbie&quot; be 5 Dawn supernal in brawl, they do it.<br /> <br /> Then your next line is &quot;But there is already a way to abstract the power of the characters in the setting and these are Charms why invent something that does the same thing but different&quot; and I will answer, as usual, by &quot;Yeah but symmetric gameplay is bad and asymmetric gameplay is good&quot; (personal opinion of course).<br /> <br /> Concerning the example with Aang : The only difference between a DB or a Solar would be the narrative. I think the trope that Aang is a Solar is the most obvious one because he is literally the chosen one of the prophecy that will bring balance and peace to the earth by overthrowing the Evil Empire that rule the world with an Iron Fist, returning from a slumber of a hundred years. You can't make it more Solar than that. Even if Aang didn't have any superpower, you can't make it more Solar Exalted than that. We could of course think of Aang like another splat (a Lunar rallying different frightened faction against the Empire around Creation, a lost egg that rebels against the unfair new order of the Empire, etc ...) and it would be just as interesting, I just think it's less obvious at first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 02-10-2020, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T02:36:24-08:00","id":1366718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366714#post1366714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(But DrLoveMonkey is correct, give him six Charms and the Artifact you get at the end of Tomb of Dreams and Volfer isn't <i>that</i> bad.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You could certainly make a far worse Dawn. There's like, worse than Volfer, which is if you spread yourself even between Brawl, Melee and Archery, and also took Dodge. Maybe make Physical your secondary stat. Then there's actually just trying to be bad, with physical tertiary (no bonus points spending to bring it up) and intentionally taking unrelated abilities and charms and stuff up.<br /> <br /> The non-Dawns is where it gets really wonky though. I have only once seen a PC Eclipse like Mirror Flag, maybe. Mirror Flag doesn't even have an excellency for her two dots of unfavoured thrown. On the other hand her three dex and 2 thrown mark her as having the same statline as a professional assassin. So what's the deal here? Are we saying that Iay is actually a pretty damn solid fighter because, in spite of being a sorcerer, he's got the stats of a professional regular soldier? Or are we saying that he sucks because he's got 2s in those abilities and like one charm?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366715#post1366715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this perspective, to take an example (that I don't think this is necessarily the best one as said Lanic, but it's just an example), what are these X tracks of initiative per turn ? Should the PC's be angry because Deathlord Kejak of the Changing Moon do it and the PC's don't ? The answer is no, and here is why : it's not a &quot;Charm&quot; in the game, it's game mechanic of making Kejak works to explicitly portray the &quot;long complicated battle against a master that can challenge 5 heroes alone&quot; (if you buy into that trope). This does not mean that Kejak always has 5 initiative tracks, this means the way of representing his prowess through this fight against the PC's, and make it closer to the mentioned trope, is through this mechanic. Why the players do not need it ? Because when the players are masters at Essence 5, and they want to crush some newbie, the system already supports that : they play normally and crush them, because they are master at Essence 5, and with the Core Rules, except if the ST is an asshole that makes the &quot;newbie&quot; be 5 Dawn supernal in brawl, they do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't feel right to me. If I'm fighting Kejak one on one, and then four of my friends join in later I would hope that the fight becomes a lot easier, rather than stays the same.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm also MUCH more okay with it not coming from some kind of Exalt that you might theoretically play as. Like maybe Luna just has 5 initiative tracks because she's Luna, or even has as many tracks as people she's fighting. Especially since Exalted, and Solars in particular, is billed as the RPG setting that doesn't do that. It doesn't have special NPCs that are way better than you could ever be. If you're a Solar and you want to be Laeral Silverhand, you can damn well be Laeral Silverhand.<br /> <br /> It's also, admittedly less commonly, billed as a setting which is big enough and epic enough that just because you're Laeral Silverhand doesn't mean you're just going to roll over everyone you come across.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T02:55:25-08:00","id":1366723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366718#post1366718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't feel right to me. If I'm fighting Kejak one on one, and then four of my friends join in later I would hope that the fight becomes a lot easier, rather than stays the same.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm also MUCH more okay with it not coming from some kind of Exalt that you might theoretically play as. Like maybe Luna just has 5 initiative tracks because she's Luna, or even has as many tracks as people she's fighting. Especially since Exalted, and Solars in particular, is billed as the RPG setting that doesn't do that. It doesn't have special NPCs that are way better than you could ever be. If you're a Solar and you want to be Laeral Silverhand, you can damn well be Laeral Silverhand.<br /> <br /> It's also, admittedly less commonly, billed as a setting which is big enough and epic enough that just because you're Laeral Silverhand doesn't mean you're just going to roll over everyone you come across.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this hypothetical scenario, the one where The Big Bad Guy is supposed to be a challenge to the whole group, you are not supposed to win alone. The fight just goes from &quot;almost unwinnable&quot; alone to &quot;Real challenge&quot; when your friends come in. <br /> <br /> I know the common disagreement is that a part of the people want the Solars to be the top unbeatable from the start if they chose to, and I respect that, and other people want a place where the most promising Solar can lose to Kejak, ducking train like the badass Solar than he is through cool narrative arc where he discovers his inner self and his purpose in Creation, and come back against Kejak to do a fair 1 on 1 and win almost every time because, yes he might have lost once, but he is still the best Solar on swordsmanship, so in the end he is meant to win. <br /> <br /> I feel like there really is a divide between us, but not that wide : You seem mainly ok with the idea that some things can be bosses, and function mechanically like bosses, for example in the thread made by Grod_The_Giant I didn't see any of you complain, but your specific point is that you don't want to apply this to other kind of Exalted, because it would make feel like the order of power between some of the Exalted would be changed. But I don't think this what we intend to do by designing a &quot;Boss system&quot;, it's more about this peculiar individual encounter between the Elder master and the fresh challengers, all mighty as they would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T03:47:36-08:00","id":1366731,"title":"","content":"Let's put this another way.<br /> <br /> Blind Frog is a 70 year old, blind begger. He is and old and infirm mortal. With one leg. He has never been trained in any combat abilities. He has no supernatural powers or aid.<br /> <br /> Would you give him twelve Initative tracks and blanket immunity to Decisive damage so he can fight Volfer one-on-one? I sure as hell wouldn't, because mortals do not work that way -- either in fluff or crunch.<br /> <br /> &quot;But John, I want to tell a story about how one of the greatest warriors in Creation gets laid low by a random no-body because of pure dumb luck.&quot;<br /> <br /> OK... sure. If you want to use ST fiat to ensure that Volfer definitely loses, but you don't want to just narrate the session then I guess you could do that.<br /> <br /> Likewise if you want to make elder Exalts VASTLY more powerful than they already are, then you can represent that via changing the design paradigm. Elder Exalts don't work like that -- in the fluff or crunch -- but you can make them work like that if you don't have narrative concerns. (If Solars can't individually challenge Celestial elders like the sidebar from 1E explicitly states, the why does the Wyld Hunt exist at all when a couple of Sidereal elders can match upto ten Solars at once?)<br /> <br /> The most promising Supernal Melee Solar does lose to Kejak, one-on-one &quot;rules as written&quot;. Kejak doesn't actually have a statline and I am explicitly not saying to build him like a PC -- build him like a QC, using the rules for building NPCs and give him powers <i>based on</i> but <i>different from</i> the powers the PCs have access to.<br /> <br /> But FIVE optimized Solars can beat Kejak. This was the case in 1E and 2.5 (not 2E). Five Solars are supposed to be able to defeat Kejak if ganging up five on one. Just like five Deebs are supposed to be able to defeat one Solar. (Not always, I can see CK beating 5 Solars who aren't combat optimized, like the Tomb of Dreams crew, just as a rule of thumb.)<br /> <br /> If you want to make something that isn't anything like a PC -- a living volcano, a Primordial, a sentient emotion -- then that thing should be completely assymetric to how a PC works.<br /> <br /> If you want to make something which is like a PC but older and with more experience, then they should work (more or less) like a PC who is older with more experience.<br /> <br /> You absolutely can make elders more powerful than they should be. Just be aware, you are house-ruling these elders to be more powerful than they actually are in canon.<br /> <br /> Would you run Mnemon as a boss fight and have a Terrestrial solo five Solars at once? If not, why not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-10-2020, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T04:36:08-08:00","id":1366737,"title":"","content":"I believe we are kind of discussing in the void. (I don't know how to say in in English it's a literal translation from French). <br /> <br /> Yes, I want to make some strong elder Exalt from the perspective of the PC. Is this non canon ? I don't know, I've read only 3e Core, 3e Dragon-Blooded and a part of 3e Lunar, so maybe, maybe not. A part of this discussion is about what kind of mechanic would allow this. I think this question, at least the one about making a Big Bad Boss, whatever his form is, is common enough on this forum that it's only fair to try and design answers for that (far more common than &quot;I want to design a system about a random disabled beating a Solar&quot;, which is the difference between the two questions). I think we all agree to a certain extent that this is a form of houserule or non-canonicity. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to make something which is like a PC but older and with more experience, then they should work (more or less) like a PC which is older with more experience. </div> </div> </div>I think, as I said, that this is our fundamental disagreement, and I think that's fine to not agree on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T04:55:30-08:00","id":1366741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366737#post1366737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A part of this discussion is about what kind of mechanic would allow this. I think this question, at least the one about making a Big Bad Boss, whatever his form is, is common enough on this forum that it's only fair to try and design answers for that (far more common than &quot;I want to design a system about a random disabled beating a Solar&quot;, which is the difference between the two questions). I think we all agree to a certain extent that this is a form of houserule or non-canonicity. <br /> <br /> I think, as I said, that this is our fundamental disagreement, and I think that's fine to not agree on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agreee that we're &quot;talking past each other&quot; (as the saying is in English) and that it's fine to disagree.<br /> <br /> But why should Kejak get to be a Big Bad Boss who can fight five Solars at once, but Blind Frog <b>not</b> get to be a Big Bad Boss?<br /> <br /> Why is it ok for Kejak to break the rules, but not a mortal?<br /> <br /> Is it ok for a Terrestrial to break the rules?<br /> <br /> I say that it <b>is</b> ok for a Primordial or an Unshaped Raksha or a Greater Elemental Dragon to break the rules because these Big Bad Bosses are materially different to the PCs, and within the constraints of the setting, plausibly strong enough to take on five Solars at once single-handedly. Primordials can have five Initiative tracks because they can fight five Solars at once.<br /> <br /> Mortals and Sidereals can't (without great personal danger) fight five Solars at once. They just can't. And it's bad for the setting if they can. And, fundementally, that's not what Exalted is about. They can fight Solars 5 on 5. They can fight Solars One on One. Some elders, geared to the teeth can fight an entire Circle of Five Solars (like Ma-Ha-Suchi) -- but they do it by engaging with the rules as written and specailizing. They don't just get to beat five Solars because they are elders.<br /> <br /> A normal Solar can't beat three Dragon-Blooded at once. But (just like Ma-Ha-Suchi) if you specailize then it is possible to build a Solar who can reliably beat 3 DBs. But Solars definitely shouldn't just get an extra two Initiative tracks so they can fight three DBs at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-10-2020, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T04:56:41-08:00","id":1366742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366723#post1366723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like there really is a divide between us, but not that wide : You seem mainly ok with the idea that some things can be bosses, and function mechanically like bosses, for example in the thread made by Grod_The_Giant I didn't see any of you complain, but your specific point is that you don't want to apply this to other kind of Exalted, because it would make feel like the order of power between some of the Exalted would be changed. But I don't think this what we intend to do by designing a &amp;quot;Boss system&amp;quot;, it's more about this peculiar individual encounter between the Elder master and the fresh challengers, all mighty as they would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, like for example in DnD. If you start out as fresh level one characters playing Dragonheist. You\u2019re in Waterdeep, and there\u2019s people in Waterdeep like Manshoon, the Blackstaff, Xanathar, Laeral Silverhand, Elminster, Mordenkainen, Jarlaxle. Those guys should look at the kind of monsters that can wipe out your whole party and just shrug, smiting them with a single action. Sometimes a bonus action even. Unless you have some knowledge they want, you don\u2019t even factor into their day planner. Which is pretty cool, you\u2019re starting out lowly heroes, but then as you progress from there and through the Dungeon of the Mad Mage you grow and learn and eventually become a power that can rival those titans who\u2019s shadow you used to stand in. That\u2019s not what I want from my Solar campaigns in Exalted, for the most part.<br /> <br /> When I made my first ex3 character, he was an intentionally bad fighter, but a legendary sorcerer. He was someone that even the greatest sorcerers in the world had to take seriously. Not quake in fear and surrender to, but somebody who would definitely factor into their plans. If there\u2019s a big meeting of the south-eastern sorcerers, I get an invite, and when I speak at it, the people present listen because I am a Solar who has poured his soul into the occult, and that makes me their equal. Or at least almost their equal. It\u2019s not like I can cast Burning Hands and they can cast Meteor swarm, so I have to sit at the kids table for now.<br /> <br /> So I guess part of the reason I\u2019d rather not have Exalted as the big boss characters is because the Exalted get involved in the politics and running nations and forming groups, human stuff. Which for DnD or even other Exalt types is fine. I\u2019m good with being granted an audience with the Blackstaff and have her just totally not care about us at all really, just offhandedly dealing with us as she goes about her day. If I\u2019m playing Solars it\u2019s because I don\u2019t want that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T05:48:27-08:00","id":1366746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366741#post1366741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortals and Sidereals can't (without great personal danger) fight five Solars at once. They just can't. And it's bad for the setting if they can. And, fundementally, that's not what Exalted is about. They can fight Solars 5 on 5. They can fight Solars One on One. Some elders, geared to the teeth can fight an entire Circle (like Ma-Ha-Suchi) can fight five Solars -- but they do it by engaging with the rules as written and specailizing. They don't just get to beat Fice Solars because they are elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't want your Elder Exalted to fight a circle of Exalted with house rules to make the fight resort to a certain trope some of the other players want to, it's fine. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agreee that we're &quot;talking past each other&quot; (as the saying is in English) and that it's fine to disagree.<br /> <br /> But why should Kejak get to be a Big Bad Boss who can fight five Solars at once, but Blind Frog <b>not</b> get to be a Big Bad Boss?<br /> <br /> Why is it ok for Kejak to break the rules, but not a mortal? </div> </div> </div>Because the rules represent a certain narrative. Kejak is a Big Bad Boss because he is literally a TV Trope (<a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/OldMaster\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/OldMaster</a>) that totally fits the genre, and so we try to find tools to do it in different ways because a lot of people has not been convinced in practice by the functioning of fights against a Single Big Boss (see this thread for example). Blind Frog could I guess as well be a TV Trope (The lucky guy that beats the odds), and if you want to houserule for him go do it, but you'll notice I haven't seen tons of threads on this forum about &quot;How do I make a fight against 1 very lucky guy ???&quot;, but I have seen quite a few &quot;How do I make a Big Boss that challenge a group of Solar ?&quot; and so we are looking for solution for this. It happens that a lot of these solutions comes from different other RPGs, because they have been tested and useful over the years, like for example multi-actions from DD. It doesn't mean the character is &quot;beyond the power ceiling of the world&quot;, it means that the way of representing his power through a specific encounter against the PC is through this mechanic, to give a different dynamic to the fight. <br /> <br /> To took one of your good examples : You taught me (truly a good advice) to ignore enemies that were useless in fights when they were not good enough for fight, in order to simplify combat. It's a good advice, and I take it. It's of course inspired, for example, from the rule that says &quot;If a character is too weak just make a roll of (Dexterity + brawl) against him and be done with it&quot;. So obviously, when a Solar optimized PC encounter a DB freshman with 7 in fighting abilities, I won't spend my time doing a real fight and apply your advice. But what happens the way around ? Would you just look at a player with a freshman DB encountering a Solar that wants to fight him, tell the player &quot;Ok roll (Brawl + Dexterity) ? 6 successes ? Well you're dead you can roll a new character.&quot; I tend to think you wouldn't do that, and instead try to let player escape or find a way around his imminent death, because the narrative is not the same from the player perspective (disposing of weak enemies vs surviving a killing machine). Does it mean that suddenly &quot;You broke the rules and the setting doesn't make sense anymore ?&quot;. Well obviously no, you just adapted the mechanic at your disposal to fit the narrative going on. <br /> <br /> So as I said, if you don't want the narrative to represent of the Old Master Sideral challenging a group of Solar, then don't adapt the rules to the narrative, it's fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T05:52:26-08:00","id":1366748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366742#post1366742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, like for example in DnD. If you start out as fresh level one characters playing Dragonheist. You\u2019re in Waterdeep, and there\u2019s people in Waterdeep like Manshoon, the Blackstaff, Xanathar, Laeral Silverhand, Elminster, Mordenkainen, Jarlaxle. Those guys should look at the kind of monsters that can wipe out your whole party and just shrug, smiting them with a single action. Sometimes a bonus action even. Unless you have some knowledge they want, you don\u2019t even factor into their day planner. Which is pretty cool, you\u2019re starting out lowly heroes, but then as you progress from there and through the Dungeon of the Mad Mage you grow and learn and eventually become a power that can rival those titans who\u2019s shadow you used to stand in. That\u2019s not what I want from my Solar campaigns in Exalted, for the most part.<br /> <br /> When I made my first ex3 character, he was an intentionally bad fighter, but a legendary sorcerer. He was someone that even the greatest sorcerers in the world had to take seriously. Not quake in fear and surrender to, but somebody who would definitely factor into their plans. If there\u2019s a big meeting of the south-eastern sorcerers, I get an invite, and when I speak at it, the people present listen because I am a Solar who has poured his soul into the occult, and that makes me their equal. Or at least almost their equal. It\u2019s not like I can cast Burning Hands and they can cast Meteor swarm, so I have to sit at the kids table for now.<br /> <br /> So I guess part of the reason I\u2019d rather not have Exalted as the big boss characters is because the Exalted get involved in the politics and running nations and forming groups, human stuff. Which for DnD or even other Exalt types is fine. I\u2019m good with being granted an audience with the Blackstaff and have her just totally not care about us at all really, just offhandedly dealing with us as she goes about her day. If I\u2019m playing Solars it\u2019s because I don\u2019t want that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is a gap between &quot;I want my characters to have a Big Boss Fight against the mastermind old master of mystic kung fu behind the killing of my past lives&quot; and &quot;I want my character to be totally ignored and irrelevant to the setting because they are too weak&quot;, and I certainly think it's possible to make the first happen without falling on the second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T06:30:19-08:00","id":1366757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366731#post1366731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...] FIVE optimized Solars can beat Kejak. This was the case in 1E and 2.5 (not 2E). Five Solars are supposed to be able to defeat Kejak if ganging up five on one. Just like five Deebs are supposed to be able to defeat one Solar. (Not always, I can see CK beating 5 Solars who aren't combat optimized, like the Tomb of Dreams crew, just as a rule of thumb.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently, at some point, the developers of Exalted thought that it would be a good idea for Kejak to defeat a circle of Solars. At the same time, they never thought that a beggar could. So there is clear difference with respect to which one of these is canonical. I understand that you may not like their decision from that time, but, well, it is a part of Exalted's legacy.<br /> <br /> By the way, canonical Deathlords <i>are</i> something that player characters could become in-setting (by a specific combination of events, but still, I could imagine a pc becoming a deathlord in a course of ten years of campaign), so if you think that they PCs shouldn't be undermined by things they can personally become, then you shouldn't place Deathlords next to third-circle demons.<br /> <br /> Third circle-demons are assets that players can reliably control, so you wouldn't like them to completely overshadow the combatants, because then only the sorcerer matters in the circle. (In my games, if you summoned a demon/have a familiar/command a battle group, that usually, you, the player, control it mechanically.) <br /> <br /> Canonically, Merela was fighting a Primordial one-on-one. So elder Solars of first-age and Primordials do not canonically land in totally different categories. I understand, she was punching above her weight class, but still, at some point she was able to defeat a Primordial in direct confrontation. <br /> <br /> Of course: if we stick to third edition and current design paradigm, then sure, what I'm proposing and doing is clearly outside of this paradigm. If we treat Exalted broadly, taking as possible anything that happened in some edition, then gaps between low Essence Solars and elder Solars are potentially obviously huge. If you don't think they were, would you agree to reintroduce high-essence charms from previous editions? (Let's say those charms that had purely narrative effects, so that we don't have compatibility issues.) Would you allow in your games an Essence 6 charm that lets you punch your enemies so hard that they will end up in Malfeas or speak a curse so compelling that the whole cities are wiped out of existence and never were?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> Dnd is constantly invoked here and I think it is a serious strawman. No one here proposes dnd-like progression. As far as I know, Dnd 5ed flattened things out, but I think that what I, probably <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24291\" data-vbnamecard=\"24291\">Chausse</a> and possibly other people are suggesting here is more like starting with a 15th level character in DnD. Already very competent, very well known, invited to sorcerous councils, listened there. Simply, still with some nontrivial room for developement and still possibly challenged by some more powerful foes (human-type).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> One last question, not purely rhetorical. Are you ok with sorcery being gated behind Essence ratings?<br /> <br /> Because that's exactly the kind of progression I would like to see. As you said: you start as a competent powerful sorcerer. But then, you can still become a super-sorcerer, matched only by strange legendary witches from deep jungles. But then, you can still become something more, a sorcerer straight from a different era. You already have these power gaps, but strangely concentrated in one place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T06:46:34-08:00","id":1366759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366757#post1366757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and possibly other people are suggesting here is more like starting with a 15th level character in DnD. Already very competent, very well known, invited to sorcerous councils, listened there. Simply, still with some nontrivial room for developement and still possibly challenged by some more powerful foes (human-type).</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s really nobody in the world of DnD that can solo fight five level 15 characters without being themselves a demon lord or some kind of god like Tiamat. A level 15 Wizard, Sorcerer, cleric, fighter, rogue party annihilates a level 20 anything. The only hope of not dying is if they\u2019re a level 20 wizard and they have a clone which activates. If any 5-person level 15 party had trouble with a level 20 antagonist, it\u2019s not because that antagonist could take them all in a fair fight.<br /> <br /> Level 15 DnD characters are definitely Solar style feels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366757#post1366757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> One last question, not purely rhetorical. Are you ok with sorcery being gated behind Essence ratings?<br /> <br /> Because that's exactly the kind of progression I would like to see. As you said: you start as a competent powerful sorcerer. But then, you can still become a super-sorcerer, matched only by strange legendary witches from deep jungles. But then, you can still become something more, a sorcerer straight from a different era. You already have these power gaps, but strangely concentrated in one place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m good with sorcery being that because, mostly, sorcery is a game changer in ways that other charms and abilities aren\u2019t. You can summon and bind Ligier, somebody who actually can fight a whole circle of Solars and win. That\u2019s beyond just the power to wipe out a city, it\u2019s like your own personal city wiper for a year and a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T07:26:50-08:00","id":1366770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366741#post1366741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why should Kejak get to be a Big Bad Boss who can fight five Solars at once, but Blind Frog <b>not</b> get to be a Big Bad Boss?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Kejak is a thousand year-old badass who's practically in charge of heaven. He gets crazy-ass mechanics because he's mastered, like, every Sidereal Martial Art and has learned to combine them in ways that should be impossible, and he's called in centuries worth of favors from war gods, and he's armed himself with some of the greatest weapons ever created. If the players manage all that, they can get multiple turns too.<br /> <br /> Speaking of talking past each other, though... Supernals or no, there's a very big difference between a being who can stand up to a circle of Essence 1 Solars and one who can stand up to a circle of Essence 5. I would absolutely expect Kejak to kick the asses of the former single-handedly, and I'd expect the latter to make him look like a fool if he tried to fight them all by himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T07:45:16-08:00","id":1366776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366757#post1366757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Canonically, Merela was fighting a Primordial one-on-one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a meme. Merela defeated a Primordial with her bare hands i.e. brawl charms, Stephen Lea Sheppard who created the version of Queen Merela that we're familiar with has said he didn't intend for it to be a solo feat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T08:30:16-08:00","id":1366782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366770#post1366770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Kejak is a thousand year-old badass who's practically in charge of heaven. He gets crazy-ass mechanics because he's mastered, like, every Sidereal Martial Art and has learned to combine them in ways that should be impossible, and he's called in centuries worth of favors from war gods, and he's armed himself with some of the greatest weapons ever created. If the players manage all that, they can get multiple turns too</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, what about five Essence 1 Dawns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T08:39:42-08:00","id":1366783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366782#post1366782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm, what about five Essence 1 Dawns?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think usuallu they have the same curriculum, neither the same character development at this point.<br /> <br /> Do we agree that we agree on the fact that an elder Exalted is a cool challenge for a young circle of Solar, and than our only disagreement is about how to handle this challenge mechanically or am I missing something ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T09:03:08-08:00","id":1366788,"title":"","content":"Personally speaking, I'm less in favour of elder power and more dangerous/forbidden power, there's overlap but I wouldn't like to confuse the two.<br /> <br /> Lets look at Filial Wisdom the Dawn Caste who first appeared in Ruins of Rathess. I'm cool with the idea that all the time he's spent with Han-Tha has given him access to dark power that could give him an unfair advantage in a fight. However, I actively resent the idea that spending the last 109 years in a jungle ruin being forgotten by the rest of the world makes him a better Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T09:33:10-08:00","id":1366791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366746#post1366746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To took one of your good examples : You taught me (truly a good advice) to ignore enemies that were useless in fights when they were not good enough for fight, in order to simplify combat. It's a good advice, and I take it. It's of course inspired, for example, from the rule that says &quot;If a character is too weak just make a roll of (Dexterity + brawl) against him and be done with it&quot;. So obviously, when a Solar optimized PC encounter a DB freshman with 7 in fighting abilities, I won't spend my time doing a real fight and apply your advice. But what happens the way around ? Would you just look at a player with a freshman DB encountering a Solar that wants to fight him, tell the player &quot;Ok roll (Brawl + Dexterity) ? 6 successes ? Well you're dead you can roll a new character.&quot; I tend to think you wouldn't do that, and instead try to let player escape or find a way around his imminent death, because the narrative is not the same from the player perspective (disposing of weak enemies vs surviving a killing machine). Does it mean that suddenly &quot;You broke the rules and the setting doesn't make sense anymore ?&quot;. Well obviously no, you just adapted the mechanic at your disposal to fit the narrative going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference here is that the optimized Solar will win the fight against the DB freshman if you play the fight out fairly using the full combat rules.<br /> <br /> So if you simplfy that to a single dice roll... nothing has changed. Either way the Solar wins.<br /> <br /> If you fight five Solars against a single Sidereal, the Sidereal <i>loses</i>.<br /> <br /> If you complicate the rules so that the Sidereal wins, then you've <i>changed the outcome.</i> Changing the outcome breaks the setting.<br /> <br /> What you're proposing when you say &quot;give elders five Initative tracks&quot; is exactly the same <i>mechanically</i> as saying &quot;Because a Freshman DB with dice pools of 7 can't beat an Optimized Solar in a fair fight, you should let <i>the <u>DB</u> </i>roll (Dexterity+Brawl) to automatically win the fight.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which... does not make sense to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366783#post1366783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we agree that we agree on the fact that an elder Exalted is a cool challenge for a young circle of Solar, and than our only disagreement is about how to handle this challenge mechanically or am I missing something ?</div> </div> </div> </div>A single elder Exalt fighting solo against a young Circle of Solars is explictly <u><b>NOT</b></u> a cool challenge for a young Circle of Solars. The Circle should pound that Elder into the ground.<br /> <br /> An elder Exalt who leverages her control over mortals, allies both Exalted and Divine, sorcerously bound demons, powerful war manse full of traps, thousand year daiklave to manipulate the Circle into fighting at night, in the rain, whilst poisoned, and up against the clock as an army marches on their home town... now that is a cool challenge for a young Circle of Solars.<br /> <br /> Which is why when you look at the write up for any of the published elders, they all say &quot;this elder can usually be found with at least one of their prot\u00e9g\u00e9s and a massive bunch of mortal troops&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366770#post1366770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Kejak is a thousand year-old badass who's practically in charge of heaven. He gets crazy-ass mechanics because he's mastered, like, every Sidereal Martial Art and has learned to combine them in ways that should be impossible, and he's called in centuries worth of favors from war gods, and he's armed himself with some of the greatest weapons ever created. If the players manage all that, they can get multiple turns too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why isn't all that enough? Why isn't mastering every Sidereal Martial art and having centuries worth of favors and the greatest weapons created <i>enough</i> so that you have to add on extra Initative tracks?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366757#post1366757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently, at some point, the developers of Exalted thought that it would be a good idea for Kejak to defeat a circle of Solars. At the same time, they never thought that a beggar could. So there is clear difference with respect to which one of these is canonical. I understand that you may not like their decision from that time, but, well, it is a part of Exalted's legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still waiting on a citation for that. If you're just going by unErrata'd statlines... then at some point the devs thought the Mask of Winter's couldn't read.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366757#post1366757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, canonical Deathlords <i>are</i> something that player characters could become in-setting (by a specific combination of events, but still, I could imagine a pc becoming a deathlord in a course of ten years of campaign), so if you think that they PCs shouldn't be undermined by things they can personally become, then you shouldn't place Deathlords next to third-circle demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, you could become a Third-Circle Demon too...<br /> <br /> Heck, you can become a new breed of Titan or the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> But these are qualitively different to just growing in power as an Exalt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366757#post1366757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course: if we stick to third edition and current design paradigm, then sure, what I'm proposing and doing is clearly outside of this paradigm. If we treat Exalted broadly, taking as possible anything that happened in some edition, then gaps between low Essence Solars and elder Solars are potentially obviously huge. If you don't think they were, would you agree to reintroduce high-essence charms from previous editions?</div> </div> </div> </div>So I love 2E. But 3E is not 2E. (I also love 1E.)<br /> <br /> The gap between Essence 6+ and Essence 1-5 Exalts of any kind was huge. Absolutely.<br /> <br /> An Essence 10 Solar could walk over a dozen Essence 5 Solars. Without breaking a sweat.<br /> <br /> 3E getting rid of that power disparity was an important themeatic and mechanical change.<br /> <br /> And, I have nothing against you house-ruling that change back in. I won't be, but you can if you like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366757#post1366757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> One last question, not purely rhetorical. Are you ok with sorcery being gated behind Essence ratings?<br /> <br /> Because that's exactly the kind of progression I would like to see. As you said: you start as a competent powerful sorcerer. But then, you can still become a super-sorcerer, matched only by strange legendary witches from deep jungles. But then, you can still become something more, a sorcerer straight from a different era. You already have these power gaps, but strangely concentrated in one place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcery (and Evocations and Eclipse Charms) aren't Solar Charms.<br /> <br /> Just like I'm ok with Primodials having five Initative tracks, I'm ok with Solars not having Supernal access to powers which are not Solar powers.<br /> <br /> Likewise I'm ok with Solars not having Supernal access to Essence 6+ Charms because they represent a personal refinement of power not an increase in power.<br /> <br /> (DrLoveMonkey raises a valid point about the scope of Sorcery, and I &quot;get&quot; that you want more power tiers and don't want Solars to start near the top of their area of expertise, but it's not really the same thing. A Solar Occultist who wants to start play as the best Occultist in Creation, can do so.)<br /> <br /> If we're going by anything that ever got published under the Exalted name ever... have you considered *shudders* starting play as Dragon-Blooded then Exalting again as Solars? That'd give you a pretty clear power up and preserve the whole &quot;returning heroes&quot; themes.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> For clarity there are 3 things I object to in Exalted:<br /> <br /> 1. This NPC is more special than you.<br /> 2. The Exalted aren't powerful enough, let's buff them.<br /> 3. The Exalted are too powerful, let's nerf them.<br /> <br /> In Exalted you play an amazingly powerful demi-god. Embrace the awesomeness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-10-2020, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T09:44:46-08:00","id":1366795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366783#post1366783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we agree that we agree on the fact that an elder Exalted is a cool challenge for a young circle of Solar, and than our only disagreement is about how to handle this challenge mechanically or am I missing something ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It really depends how you build it up. If you build the Solars a certain way, not a \u201cbad\u201d way or the \u201cwrong\u201d way, maybe even the most \u201cright\u201d way, then Kejak doesn\u2019t need any fancy tricks to win. Just give him White Reaper, maybe Wood Dragon or something, and the Sidereal excellency. Added help from any sidereal resistance charms or Citroen Poxes, the SMA is just racking up the score. I think that\u2019s just fine.<br /> <br /> On the other hand what I usually see is that the twilight bureaucrat has Dex 5, melee 5, specialty in swords, Awareness 5, specialty in ambushes, a daiklave, artifact heavy plate, and spells like Invulnerable Skin of Bronze stacked on top of that. If every character is built like that, and then the Dawn just has 18 melee charms, the 18 best ones, then Kejak needs to bring in reinforcements to win that fight. The one Dawn there might be Essence 1 but yes poised to be a warrior who is legendary even among the ranks of the Dawn caste, and everyone else there is a world class fighter who\u2019ve honed their Solar Essence to break far beyond mortal limits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T10:53:36-08:00","id":1366808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366795#post1366795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It really depends how you build it up. If you build the Solars a certain way, not a \u201cbad\u201d way or the \u201cwrong\u201d way, maybe even the most \u201cright\u201d way, then Kejak doesn\u2019t need any fancy tricks to win. Just give him White Reaper, maybe Wood Dragon or something, and the Sidereal excellency. Added help from any sidereal resistance charms or Citroen Poxes, the SMA is just racking up the score. I think that\u2019s just fine.<br /> <br /> On the other hand what I usually see is that the twilight bureaucrat has Dex 5, melee 5, specialty in swords, Awareness 5, specialty in ambushes, a daiklave, artifact heavy plate, and spells like Invulnerable Skin of Bronze stacked on top of that. If every character is built like that, and then the Dawn just has 18 melee charms, the 18 best ones, then Kejak needs to bring in reinforcements to win that fight. The one Dawn there might be Essence 1 but yes poised to be a warrior who is legendary even among the ranks of the Dawn caste, and everyone else there is a world class fighter who\u2019ve honed their Solar Essence to break far beyond mortal limits.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A single elder Exalt fighting solo against a young Circle of Solars is explictly <u><b>NOT</b></u> a cool challenge for a young Circle of Solars. The Circle should pound that Elder into the ground. </div> </div> </div>I mean I like you both really, but I don't think our discussion is leading anywhere. We don't want the same thing apparently, so we won't have the same thing. It's fine, but I don't believe this discussion has any purpose except showing we have different expectations about the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T10:55:32-08:00","id":1366809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366791#post1366791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why isn't all that enough? Why isn't mastering every Sidereal Martial art and having centuries worth of favors and the greatest weapons created <i>enough</i> so that you have to add on extra Initative tracks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the system as written makes being outnumbered an enormous disadvantage, and &quot;giving the boss an extra turn&quot; is a really simple and straightforward way to address the imbalance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T11:39:48-08:00","id":1366819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366809#post1366809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the system as written makes being outnumbered an enormous disadvantage, and &quot;giving the boss an extra turn&quot; is a really simple and straightforward way to address the imbalance.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s an enormous but not insurmountable disadvantage. Revolving Crescent Defense from White Reaper cancels all onslaught penalties and instead turns them into a parry bonus. That\u2019s pretty damn good, it just doesn\u2019t mean much if all five incoming attacks are 23-28 dice backed by a charm that rerolls 1s and another that gives non-charm automatic successes. Especially when your attacks back are all met with super heavy artifact plate. Which is a thing Solars can do, but they don\u2019t have to.<br /> <br /> I won\u2019t have the time to run it tonight but I bet if I made a pretty conservative Kejak using only one or two martial arts from the current published material he could beat a circle of Solars. He just won\u2019t beat a circle of Solars who\u2019ve all got max combat stats and as many combat charms as they can grab at their essence.<br /> <br /> This is also why I said yesterday that if we don\u2019t pin down what we mean by that this discussion is pointless. The difference between Essence 5 and Essence 1 is insignificant compared to the difference between Melee 5 and Melee 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T12:07:19-08:00","id":1366824,"title":"","content":"Just to illustrate my point. Who wins in a fight? The Essence 5 guy with 1s in all his combat abilities, or the Essence 1 guy with 5s in all his combat abilities?<br /> <br /> Assuming no shenanigans like \u201cwell is resistance technically a combat ability? And what about occult for combat sorcery?\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T13:45:59-08:00","id":1366847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366809#post1366809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the system as written makes being outnumbered an enormous disadvantage</div> </div> </div> </div>The system or <i>the setting</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T15:20:20-08:00","id":1366869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366809#post1366809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the system as written makes being outnumbered an enormous disadvantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being Outnumbered kind of works out that way in real life too, regardless of skill. Amazing, that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T15:35:57-08:00","id":1366874,"title":"","content":"Are there any game systems out there that convincingly and elegantly make 5 opponents piling in against 1 small opponent *not quite* as good as you might expect?<br /> <br /> You often see this trope in movie fights (if maybe not reality) where you have 5 guys piling in against &quot;the hero&quot; or some badass villain, and they are not that effective, not much more effective than one-on-one, as the more skilled party is able to turn the confusion of close battle and their superior spatial and combat awareness to their advantage. <br /> <br /> Does Ex3 have the kind of tools in its system to make this happen? (Even if it does not, as base written).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T17:31:27-08:00","id":1366886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366874#post1366874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any game systems out there that convincingly and elegantly make 5 opponents piling in against 1 small opponent *not quite* as good as you might expect?<br /> <br /> You often see this trope in movie fights (if maybe not reality) where you have 5 guys piling in against &amp;quot;the hero&amp;quot; or some badass villain, and they are not that effective, not much more effective than one-on-one, as the more skilled party is able to turn the confusion of close battle and their superior spatial and combat awareness to their advantage. <br /> <br /> Does Ex3 have the kind of tools in its system to make this happen? (Even if it does not, as base written).</div> </div> </div> </div>You can always battlegroup enemies who are mobbing somebody if you want them to be ultimately not very effective. On the other hand multiple people all attacking from different angles is handled by onslaught penalties. Powerful exalted can generally ignore these for some kind of cost though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T19:00:43-08:00","id":1366904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366874#post1366874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any game systems out there that convincingly and elegantly make 5 opponents piling in against 1 small opponent *not quite* as good as you might expect?<br /> <br /> You often see this trope in movie fights (if maybe not reality) where you have 5 guys piling in against &quot;the hero&quot; or some badass villain, and they are not that effective, not much more effective than one-on-one, as the more skilled party is able to turn the confusion of close battle and their superior spatial and combat awareness to their advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, of course it depends what you mean by &quot;convincingly and elegantly&quot;, but yes, many system in the '90s used to embrace power gaps enabling the single fighter not to be overwhelmed by five opponents. DnD 3rd edition did that. Warhammer did that. Old World of Darkness games did that, Earthdawn did that, Shadowrun I guess did that (I own 3ed and 5 ed rulebooks but I never happened to play them), Burning Wheel did that. Honestly, it was a pretty normal thing. Arguably, systems back then were generally not &quot;elegantly&quot; designed going by current standards, but I wouldn't say there were bad.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> As I said, I think it's good to break discussion in two points:<br /> <br /> 1. What relative power levels we want to have in Exalted,<br /> 2. If we want a circle of five Solars to be beatable by a single opponent, how can we reach it.<br /> <br /> Let me resume your points, to see whether we are not talking past each other. We were essentially completely ignoring point 2. and focusing completely on point 1. You're saying this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No one actually</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The essential feature of Exalted is that a Solar character, right after being created can be literally the top warrior in the world. If you gather five such Solars, any enemy of roughly human type should be beaten by them, because otherwise the statement that Solar can be really top warriors becomes meaningless. This feature is so fundamental to Exalted that changing it completely changes the basic premise of the game (say, like getting rid of the Masquarade in Vampire).</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that an accurate summary of your opinion?<br /> <br /> Now, my point is this: It's clear that the game mechanic of Exalted, the third edition supports your opinion. It is really how developers tend to depict things. Everyone agrees with that. What you say is the core feature of Solars in the current edition. We know that we are explicitly goldruling away something that really is a premise of Exalted: Third Edition.<br /> <br /> What I don't agree with is that this feature is somehow indeed fundamental to Exalted:<br /> - I don't see it really in the first edition rulebook. The tone seem to be rather sword and sorcery adventure;<br /> - I don't really see it really in the second edition rulebook; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a>, you yourself agreed that elders were so powerful in 2e as to completely dominate starting characters, even combat-optimised.<br /> <br /> Now, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> you said that in fact that feature was present in first edition. I went to the passages you hinted at and honestly, none of them seems to support the view that Solars should start near the top. We can discuss concrete passages, but reading the ones you already suggested, I remain unconvinced.<br /> <br /> Second edition was changed in the Scroll of Errata, ok. I understand. It was changed even more in third edition. But we are now discussing whether it is completely out of tone for Exalted to have powerful elders. My argument is: no. At some point, quite a few developers thought that it was a cool idea to have elders who completely dominate everyone else in the setting. You can argue that they were fundamentally wrong about what game Exalted should be, but this really requires some very strong arguments.<br /> <br /> For quite a few years, going by published charms, elders were vastly more powerful than the fresh Exalts. Therefore it's not contrary to the core premises of the game. I get that you may not like it, but what criterion do you even propose then of what is and what is not the essence of Exalted? What does it even mean to be the core premise in the game if it can change? The core premise in Exalted as such, not Exalted: third edition. We explicitly don't want to stick to premises of third edition in some respects. In my opinion, you are treating some features of Solars which you obviously enjoy and which clearly hold in current edition as the central premise of that splat.<br /> <br /> I would never claim that Lunars being twisted Wyld monsters is somehow the core premise of Lunars, precisely because it changes from edition to edition. Their being shapeshifers definitely is. It never changed and it's not likely to ever change.<br /> <br /> Learning Exalted, it never occurred to me that Solars starting <i>literally </i>at the top is the core premise of the setting and, judging by the number of threads that ask the precise same question, some people also don't see that as something obvious.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I tend to see the core premises of Solars as:<br /> - absurdly high power level (in the terms of narrative powers. You can shoot exploding arrows, because you're such a great archer. Doesn't mean that no one is better);<br /> - shiny heroes;<br /> - reborn rulers of the world;<br /> - chased by usurpers.<br /> <br /> Building on the tropes on which Exalted is partially built: mostly that of anime or wuxia stories, I would like to see more room for characters honing their skills and truly becoming a cosmic power.<br /> <br /> That was longish. I think that it's maybe pointless to discuss what the core premise of Solars is, because we obviously disagree about that and I couldn't possibly imagine what criteria can we apply to settle this issue (we could do deep exegesis of Exalted books, but honestly, it doesn't seem worth the effort).<br /> <br /> EDIT: One disclaimer. I know about Exalted definitely much less than you, and in this discussion, it's actually very relevant. However, I really think that with this experience comes certain baggage, as the impression of fresh reading becomes deeply entangled with numerous recollections from sessions, Internet discussion etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-10-2020, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T21:27:08-08:00","id":1366918,"title":"","content":"I'm going to respond by saying not why IS it like that, but why it should be like that.<br /> <br /> 1. It gives Solars a really cool and unique place, not just among the Exalted, but even among Tabletop RPGS in general. Not utterly unique, but pretty unique. If your whole circle wants to be warriors, then the five of you combined can fight literal mile-high behemoths, or the elder rulers of the world. Chejop Kejak doesn't get to look down his nose at you and scatter you to the winds like trash all on his own.<br /> <br /> In so many other settings, and so many other systems, you start out weak with major players totally beyond you in scope. Almost any WoD game, DnD, Shadowrun, Warhammer, Edge of Empire, Dark Heresy, all that is great for being awesome heroes that actually still don't hold a candle to the people really in charge, until you've reached the endgame and actually stand with them. It's nice for that not to be the case, for a change.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2. It helps to counterbalance the crazy disadvantages that Solars start with. They have no infrastructure in place to catch them as they exalt like the Lunars, Sidereals and Dragonblooded do. A Sidereal is scooped up and flown in to Heaven to become enlightened and part of the workings of Heaven itself, Lunars are rescued from the jaws of the Wyld Hunt and taken to fortress-nations outside the easy grasp of the realm to learn in schools from their Shahan-ya, and their peers. Dragonblooded are raised from birth to grasp the helm of the greatest empire in the world, and exalted as elemental saints by the worlds greatest religion.<br /> <br /> Solars don't have any of that, or anything like it. They even suffer more than any other Exalted from the Great Curse on top of it all. The only thing they have is their personal strength. Even then, it's no match for the forces arrayed against them. They still need allies, they still need more experience and to grow in power as they adventure. Maybe not in martial power if they just dumped all 15 of their starting charms into combat right away. Nobody but a Dawn can do that anyway though. Everyone else is going to have to get theirs the slow way.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3. Decentralizing the power of major NPCs outside of making them personally invincible lets the Storyteller and the Players better able to deal with them in a variety of ways and using a variety of characters, and lets the storyteller tailor the experience more. This is the only one that doesn't apply to just Solars. The Mask of Winters as he was in 2e was not able to be fought by almost any group of Solars. If you had a balanced circle of Solars, with maybe a pretty powerful Dawn, and everyone getting a bit involved in combat, they would still get destroyed by the Mask. Just the Mask, nevermind his Abyssals and other minions that you'd have to find some way to also deal with.<br /> <br /> He was beatable by some very specific Solars in some very specific ways, but that's about it. Even then step one of making those Solars was &quot;Start the game at Essence 5&quot;. It's always a really hard balance point in any RPG, but it gets blown to absurdity in Exalted. In 5e DnD you can at least expect that everyone in a level 17 party can fight really well, there's no such thing as a class that can't put the hurt on people. Also DnD is pretty easy to optimize for, and doesn't require to to optimize that much. Your wizard with 18 intelligence is just fine.<br /> <br /> Exalted is not that at all. it's got a huge variety of characters, and a lot of them just can't fight. If your circle consists of the Warrior (Dawn), the Preacher (Zenith), the Messenger (Night) the Tinkerer (Twilight) and the Diplomat (Eclipse) then it really helps if you don't absolutely require five really epic warriors in the final conflict.<br /> <br /> <br /> 4. Shouldn't really be in this list but I kind of don't understand why a Third Circle Demon or an epic Fey lord, doesn't fit the bill for a nemesis. They're not human, sure, but that doesn't make them not characters. Like what's wrong with <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/15/b1/64/15b1643f423a02d4d5361baa8dec2bf6.png\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> guy? He even has a convenient excuse as to why he doesn't just teleport over to the pathetically weak PCs and slay them. He's also powerful enough to fight the Unconquered Sun to a standstill, which is definitely powerful enough to fight a whole Solar circle.<br /> <br /> From the Compass of Celestial Directions: Malfeas: He relishes the attention given to him for his station, arrogant, an adept sorcerer and smith. He'll even do commission work for the right price, whatever that is. When you need something from him he invites you into one of his seven decadent parlours to treat with you, he'll even treat with mortals if they offer him a legitimate request. He rules one of the largest and most powerful feifdoms in Malfeas,<br /> <br /> He's not like a xenomorph or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T01:00:21-08:00","id":1366923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366869#post1366869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being Outnumbered kind of works out that way in real life too, regardless of skill. Amazing, that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to be mean but you can't really argue that in one of the rare fantasy non-narrativist game where one person can defeat 1000 enemies abstracted in a single entity almost right from the start. <br /> <br /> Edit : Awesome my first part of the answer was deleted when I decided to quote someone else.<br /> <br /> I just wanted to say I think my position is a little different from Lanic : I don't want &quot;elders to all be stronger than Solar forever&quot;, I want tools to &quot;sometimes make a fight against an elder a long trial for a group of Solars without having to learn 15 Charms for 1 NPC&quot;. This same elder might not have these same mechanics when they encounter him later, or if he is deemed unimportant to the story. I don't believe consistency on this kind of things is the most important thing. I guess my point ultimately comes back to a well discussed topic on this forum &quot;How do you make strong and simple NPC's that can pose a challenge to the players.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 02-11-2020, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T05:18:24-08:00","id":1366949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366904#post1366904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, of course it depends what you mean by &quot;convincingly and elegantly&quot;, but yes, many system in the '90s used to embrace power gaps enabling the single fighter not to be overwhelmed by five opponents. DnD 3rd edition did that. Warhammer did that. Old World of Darkness games did that, Earthdawn did that, Shadowrun I guess did that (I own 3ed and 5 ed rulebooks but I never happened to play them), Burning Wheel did that. Honestly, it was a pretty normal thing. Arguably, systems back then were generally not &quot;elegantly&quot; designed going by current standards, but I wouldn't say there were bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOK, but I'm not talking about if it does so by making a single fighter specifically generally and generically strong, but by emulating a specific fictional trope. One where strong, skilled fighters actually do not face as much of a disadvantage as thought, because their skill allows them to exploit the chaos of a multiple enemy chaotic melee much better than their less skilled opponents. <br /> <br /> Are you talking about that same thing when you say that Warhammer, oWoD, Shadowrun etc did?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366886#post1366886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can always battlegroup enemies who are mobbing somebody if you want them to be ultimately not very effective. On the other hand multiple people all attacking from different angles is handled by onslaught penalties. Powerful exalted can generally ignore these for some kind of cost though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, battlegroups sprung to mind as arguably an abstract emulation of the trope I'm talking, but they aren't very useful for situations where players won't want or characters can't be abstracted into them. Yeah, also under Exalted can negate onslaught penalties, though that's more of a &quot;remove disadvantage&quot; rather than &quot;gain a new advantage&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Fictive example of specific trope with a reference that is less manky and decrepit than most I go to: Opening episode of &quot;The Witcher&quot;, where you see Geralt's skill against a bunch of mooks come out in that they are confused and uncoordinated in the big brawl, *less* than the sum of their parts, while he knows exactly where to move and how to be effective. That could be played as removing an onslaught penalty, but I also think you could go beyond that.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T05:49:15-08:00","id":1366952,"title":"","content":"Anyway my issue with multiple initiative tracks is simply the standardised nature of it.<br /> <br /> I don't mind if a boss breaks the rules enemies normally follow if the result is interesting, but if all bosses break the rules in the same way I'm not sure that interest will be sustained especially since it partially mitigates the opportunity for the boss to be clever about this on their own terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T05:50:59-08:00","id":1366954,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a><br /> Ok. For the completeness of the discussion let me just briefly say what is my personal preference as to power-levels. I played rather little DnD and I know that in the US gaming community comparisons to DnD are very natural for the US rpg community and I think that this comparison slightly blurs the picture.<br /> <br /> My reasons why I want potentially powerful elders:<br /> <br /> 1. First and the most important for me, personally: if you start near the ceiling, then this makes your ceiling not so impressive. You want your game to be manageable, so you'll be afraid for the powers near the ceiling to break the game. You will not hand powers that completely change the game. You will not have an Awarness charms that, say, lets you eavesdrop conversations anywhere in Creation. You won't have a version of Hypnotic Tongue that lets you affect the whole court. You won't have a Brawl charm that lets you send someone to Malfeas.<br /> <br /> I loved that in Mage games, they would never shy away from giving your players really narrative-breaking capabilities. In Exalted, I would probably make them more restrictive, say once per story, but other than that -- I just love that you actually don't handwave the category of plot devices, but you hand them to your players.<br /> <br /> However, I wouldn't like to start any campaign that high, because then the use of these powers lack appropriate gravity. You want to build up to that moment. It's something completely different when you do it after two years of weekly play. There are NPCs you care about, places in the game you care about. You are extremely powerful and yet deeply anchored.<br /> <br /> There are <i>some</i> powers in Exalted 3ed which really feel that powerful. But incidentally, what really stands out, is Solar Circle sorcery. I think that the reasons why I would like to gate more powerful charms behind more experience points, is that I would like them to be similarly powerful.<br /> <br /> 2. I like to introduce such grandiose effects as plot devices in my games. Often they appear just as hints, legends, stories of unclear source. It introduces a deep atmosphere of mystery that I also love. Moreover, these stories involve <i>Exalted</i>, not otherworldly beings. That's because it brings certain promise: you can play in the same category as these creatures of cosmic myth. If the players start near the ceiling, these plot devices and legends feel simply fake, a pure decoration. And if these stories involve, say, demons, then, honestly, this makes me feel players are even less important. It's a very different and powerful message, when you say: &quot;some day, you can be a part of cosmic myth.&quot;<br /> <br /> The bottom line is this: if either me or my players would play literally the best X in the world, then we wouldn't feel great. The world would feel small. (Half-jokingly, it feels like our discussion might be related to some deep cultural differences. In the US, you can really see that people have this deep feeling of agency.)<br /> <br /> 3. The tropes that Exalted invokes: that of great reborn heroes, just scream to me &quot;stories of personal growth&quot;. Finding your mentor, overcoming your pride, growing up to your role, and finally overcoming the foe who killed your past incarnation.<br /> <br /> Ok, just to finish: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> I think I now really better understand your position. I think that when we think of Solars' power, we tend to think of two distinct things: absolute and relative power.<br /> <br /> I am very attached to the idea that Solars are, in principle, powerful in the absolute sense. Essentially, I view them as a splat that realises crazy cosmic tropes of Mage, but in a fantasy setting, and with a wider arrange of possible roles.<br /> <br /> As far as I understand, you really mostly want Solars to be simply the best and it's less important what the actual power levels are. Let's take this to extreme: if we tell a story about a boxer, or a physicist who is literally and by far the best in the history, but set in the real world, where the said boxer can be gunshot and the physicist will simply not be able to build time machine, then nevertheless, these are deeply &quot;Solar&quot; characters and right inspirations of how Solars should function.<br /> <br /> Am I right? I'm asking, because this seems a good test case: I would distinctly not tend to think of these characters as essentially Solar. For me, Solar phycisist is the one who actually managed to build a time-machine, even if his main competitor did that already 20 years ago and better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-11-2020, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T05:54:18-08:00","id":1366957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366949#post1366949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you talking about that same thing when you say that Warhammer, oWoD, Shadowrun etc did?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I actually meant just general power levels.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> I actually tend to think of these as of &quot;boss-level&quot; excellencies. But I can see where you're coming from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T06:51:36-08:00","id":1366964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366957#post1366957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> I actually tend to think of these as of &quot;boss-level&quot; excellencies. But I can see where you're coming from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be useful to give a more specific example. There's been some straw manning of your approach with giving a blind beggar extra initiative tracks to fight Volfer etc it could help people understand each other better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T07:57:04-08:00","id":1366976,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m Canadian, not American, but close enough I guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019m not personally much of a fan of Solars reaching the kind of cosmic heights that other people are. Partially I think because I just can\u2019t figure out how to adjudicate those games. Like if two nations are fighting and a player wants to stop them by removing the concept of conflict from reality...I\u2019m lost and I don\u2019t know how to progress.<br /> <br /> Like if cosmic power we\u2019re talking about this kind of thing: <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CosmicEntity\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.p...n/CosmicEntity</a><br /> <br /> So for my games it\u2019s probably a lot more reasonable for Solars to start much closer to the top, if they try hard enough. Even if they\u2019re only halfway there, five times 50% of an elder is overwhelming to the elder. <br /> <br /> \u201c 3. The tropes that Exalted invokes: that of great reborn heroes, just scream to me &quot;stories of personal growth&quot;. Finding your mentor, overcoming your pride, growing up to your role, and finally overcoming the foe who killed your past incarnation.\u201d<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t disagree with this is any way whatsoever though. My epic spirit shackling occultist that I mentioned started that campaign really meek, afraid of everything, very dependant on others, and ended the campaign riding a soulbreaker orb into the maw of a ravenous world eating monster.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s lots of personal growth that doesn\u2019t necessarily translate directly to power. Also on top of that you go from having nothing to, maybe, leading the entire world as a single nation or something, which is massive growth as far as power is concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T16:00:28-08:00","id":1367115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366976#post1366976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m Canadian, not American, but close enough I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see that my post could come off as borderline offensive. I'm sorry if it was.<br /> <br /> I mostly meant that (at least in some places) in US, you really have this feeling of history being done just right now, just right here, and I think that this experience really might transfer to the habits we have in our hobby.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> You stated previously (also in different threads) that you don't personally enjoy &quot;cosmic heights&quot;. I know it, and I think that this difference in preferences is largely the cause of different preference as to the role of &quot;elders&quot;, broadly understood.<br /> \u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> You,re right. I posted previously in this thread one mechanical solution which we're currently playtesting in our campaign. I planned it to be handed in some splat-adjusted version to other kinds of Exalts, much like excellencies are roughly the same across splats and abilities. (I know, Sidereals. Roughly.) After some time, maybe I'll post on the forum how the playtest went and propose some actual homebrew for the interested. <br /> <br /> I didn't want to focus overly on the particular implementation, since I wouldn't bet my money on whether it works fine. Additionally, there many parametres we should take into account. For example, we should decide first whether we are ok with asymmetric mechanic or not (I'm ok with it when necessary, but generally reluctant).<br /> <br /> But you're right, I should probably be more specific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T16:53:34-08:00","id":1367122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1367115#post1367115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see that my post could come off as borderline offensive. I'm sorry if it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah don't worry about it. Canadians are always &quot;On the contrary, we're more British than American, I think you'll find.&quot; or &quot;Yeah, crazy Europeans, am I right?&quot; when convenient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T12:08:59-08:00","id":1367277,"title":"","content":"Anyway, what I meant by this, because I think I could've been clearer in expressing the idea. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366305#post1366305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going past essence 6 it's not all that difficult. The charms that create extra actions become a game changer if there's a significant difference in mote pool sizes.</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory you could boost every attack a charm like Iron Whirlwind Attack gives you with a full excellency, it's just ruiniously expensive but if there's a significant essence pool disparity between you and the people you're fighting you can create cascades of attacks where the purpose isn't to kill or harm them but to grind them down to a point where their subsequent participation in the combat will be limited but yours won't be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-12-2020, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T14:19:07-08:00","id":1367304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366954#post1366954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I understand, you really mostly want Solars to be simply the best and it's less important what the actual power levels are. Let's take this to extreme: if we tell a story about a boxer, or a physicist who is literally and by far the best in the history, but set in the real world, where the said boxer can be gunshot and the physicist will simply not be able to build time machine, then nevertheless, these are deeply &amp;quot;Solar&amp;quot; characters and right inspirations of how Solars should function.<br /> <br /> Am I right? I'm asking, because this seems a good test case: I would distinctly not tend to think of these characters as essentially Solar. For me, Solar phycisist is the one who actually managed to build a time-machine, even if his main competitor did that already 20 years ago and better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nailed it.<br /> <br /> Being a Solar doesn't mean you get everything you want. No time machines.<br /> <br /> It means you're the best equipped to get what you want.<br /> <br /> I think your &quot;boxer getting shot&quot; and &quot;physicist who can't build a time machine&quot; are an excellent illustration, by the way.<br /> <br /> Reed Richards is a Solar.<br /> Viktor Von Doom is an Infernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T16:47:30-08:00","id":1367331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1367277#post1367277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, what I meant by this, because I think I could've been clearer in expressing the idea.<br /> In theory you could boost every attack a charm like Iron Whirlwind Attack gives you with a full excellency, it's just ruiniously expensive but if there's a significant essence pool disparity between you and the people you're fighting you can create cascades of attacks where the purpose isn't to kill or harm them but to grind them down to a point where their subsequent participation in the combat will be limited but yours won't be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate on that?<br /> <br /> If I undertand correctly, you say: even with RAW charms, an Essence 6 with multi-attack charms is a serious threat, since they can launch a series of decisive attacks with the purpose of inflicting wound penalties and this would work due to mote economy. (And this possibly could be amplified in presence of extra Initiative tracks.) Is that correct?<br /> <br /> From my limited experience, it seems to me that even if your are Essence 6, then mote economy is not really a game changer. You are at most ~50 motes ahead of Essence 1 characters. This means that if they are &gt;2 of them, the mote economy is on their side (by which I mean that they can freely spend as much motes boosting their Defense, as the opponent did boosting attack pool and some of them still will have reserves to boost their attacks).<br /> <br /> Do you find it different? Or did I miss your point?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> Yeah, that's the point at which we have agree to disagree <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-12-2020, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T18:51:41-08:00","id":1367354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1367331#post1367331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you find it different? Or did I miss your point?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Lioness might have been saying that even if you max out your defense an elder Exalt can still hit you, and doing so with a boosted decisive attack in the first turn of combat leaves you with either people down and out of the fight, or wound penalties.<br /> <br /> Depending, of course, on if the whole party picked up like 5 ox-bodies and the charms to ignore wound penalties. which again brings us back around to what kind of party is facing off against this elder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T20:29:44-08:00","id":1367384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1367331#post1367331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you elaborate on that?<br /> <br /> If I undertand correctly, you say: even with RAW charms, an Essence 6 with multi-attack charms is a serious threat, since they can launch a series of decisive attacks with the purpose of inflicting wound penalties and this would work due to mote economy. (And this possibly could be amplified in presence of extra Initiative tracks.) Is that correct?<br /> <br /> From my limited experience, it seems to me that even if your are Essence 6, then mote economy is not really a game changer. You are at most ~50 motes ahead of Essence 1 characters. This means that if they are &gt;2 of them, the mote economy is on their side (by which I mean that they can freely spend as much motes boosting their Defense, as the opponent did boosting attack pool and some of them still will have reserves to boost their attacks).<br /> <br /> Do you find it different? Or did I miss your point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, hang on.<br /> <br /> The purpose of the extra actions isn\u2019t to distribute the attacks <i>evenly</i> among combatants, it\u2019s to force the PC or PCs most likely to end the fight by round 2 onto the backfoot.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s either going to happen via wound penalties or because they spend so many motes on defence that it puts their doom combo off the table for a few rounds. Yes, certainly an exertion like that isn\u2019t nothing to the boss they\u2019ll come out of it way more ready to keep fighting than the characters they\u2019re doing it to because they have more motes.<br /> <br /> Now either someone else has to step up or at least hold off the boss while their heavy hitters adapt to compensate by idling long enough to regain motes and/or taking aim actions to offset wound penalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T09:25:38-08:00","id":1368310,"title":"","content":"Upon reflection, this actually highlights the main shortcoming I see of action economy as a solution.<br /> <br /> Giving the boss multiple initiative tracks because they're in a 5 on 1 fight comes with an expectation that they'll distribute the attacks fairly evenly when the PCs are almost certainly not contributing equally towards the potential curbstomping.<br /> <br /> The alternative strategy of frequently giving the Dawn Caste (or equivalent) the boss' undivided attention for however many attacks they make is its own potential problem because that highlights the disparity between prominent NPCs and the PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T10:29:49-08:00","id":1368321,"title":"","content":"Yes I think as well that multiple actions is the less elegant way to approach this problem. I for example line Grod' suggestion to give the ennemy bonus initiative each round propirtionnately to the number of enemies or something like that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T10:39:05-08:00","id":1368324,"title":"","content":"It's difficult to do other ways as well. If they don't have enough soak, and really with artifact weapons they also need post-soak damage reducers, they're going to be permanently crashed. On the other hand if you do give them enough Defense or damage reducers to weather those storms then most turns are going to end up being everyone attacking the big bad to no effect, which isn't really a fun way to play it.<br /> <br /> Especially with the disparity in combat power. I ran a 3e game with a Twilight artist, Eclipse bureaucrat, Night acrobat, and a Dawn MA-ist and Dawn Brawler. The big final fight I came up with there had a bunch of support for the Essence 5 Infernal that was facing off against them. It worked pretty well, unfortunately the party focused on taking out the support guys first after which there was about two rounds of the non-dawns doing basically nothing to the jacked up Infernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T11:04:54-08:00","id":1368332,"title":"","content":"Seems true that X initiative tracks for boss *wouldn't* in practice get dedicated each to X opponents.. But that's sort of true if you're fighting a group of enemies as well, isn't it? The group of enemies would try and go all-in against their best opponent too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T11:40:21-08:00","id":1368339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1357571-how-2-god-fite-making-single-enemies-work?p=1357579#post1357579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All good. I like Scene long Reflexive Clashes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I like Clashes. More dynamic than static Parry, get the whole party feeling like they're doing something without ganging up on one character.<br /> <br /> Reflexively Clashes are RAW a power available to the PCs so you don't need to bolt on a new powerlevel on the game.<br /> <br /> Reflexive counter attacks are also good for ebb and flow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-16-2020, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T11:46:42-08:00","id":1368341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1368332#post1368332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems true that X initiative tracks for boss *wouldn't* in practice get dedicated each to X opponents.. But that's sort of true if you're fighting a group of enemies as well, isn't it? The group of enemies would try and go all-in against their best opponent too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> I think that the problem is that whoever your circle is fighting, it is almost always the optimal solution to focus your fire and take them one by one. Of course, this holds both ways. It's almost always the optimal strategy focus your fire and make your hits actually influence your enemies' capabilities. <br /> <br /> In defense of Initiative Tracks as the solution, I would says this: If you think that n identical Abyssals is reasonable challenge to your circle, then one of these Abyssals with n Initiative Tracks should be generally <i>less </i>challenging. You now have the same base numbers of attacks, but dramatically fewer motes (so you cannot infuse your every attack with full excellency, and your players can), you have only one health track (so your players instead of killing one of n Abyssals could perform exactly the same actions and kill you instead).<br /> <br /> Of course, you could try to split said n Abyssals, but similarly, you can try to attacks your n-Abyssal-package-in-one-enemy from some distance, so it's not obvious to me that here you would get any advantage either.<br /> <br /> Generally, you also don't assume that all n tracks will act before your players (that would be equivalent to all n Abyssals acting before your players, so they would be pretty much hopeless). So, if your enemy's tracks and the players are reasonably interwoven, then the players will in general be able to empty a couple of them each round, so those n tracks are in general never <i>able</i> to concentrate on one player. I mean, you could put all your resources trying to kill one man, but in general you would also like to make sure that no one around sits on tons of Initiative, so you will spread out those attacks. <br /> <br /> Much depends on the specific implementation of multiple tracks, so let me stick to the one that I actually proposed here. These tracks are expensive to maintain. You commit motes to open them, you pay willpower to open them. Once you make them empty, they are closed and you need to pay once more to reopen them. If you make a decisive attack, you cannot combine this Initiative in one attack. You either make withering attacks or decisive, so in general you cannot sit on a ton of Initiative and repeat decisives.<br /> <br /> I believe that this is really reasonably balanced. I don't want to make strong claims because this solution needs clear playtest. But I don't think that trying to focus on one combatant would be close to the optimal strategy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T12:15:12-08:00","id":1368350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1368332#post1368332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems true that X initiative tracks for boss *wouldn't* in practice get dedicated each to X opponents.. But that's sort of true if you're fighting a group of enemies as well, isn't it? The group of enemies would try and go all-in against their best opponent too?</div> </div> </div> </div>The key difference is that X opponents are in fact X opponents. They don't normally have to worry about a single powerful opponent killing them all at once like the boss does because they have seperate health level tracks, there's a few exceptions such as Death of Obsidian Butterflies or Heaven Sword Flash but by crowding in on one character you would ironically create the situation where your group of enemies can all be targeted at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T12:28:48-08:00","id":1368355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1368341#post1368341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> I think that the problem is that whoever your circle is fighting, it is almost always the optimal solution to focus your fire and take them one by one. Of course, this holds both ways. It's almost always the optimal strategy focus your fire and make your hits actually influence your enemies' capabilities.<br /> <br /> In defense of Initiative Tracks as the solution, I would says this: If you think that n identical Abyssals is reasonable challenge to your circle, then one of these Abyssals with n Initiative Tracks should be generally <i>less </i>challenging. You now have the same base numbers of attacks, but dramatically fewer motes (so you cannot infuse your every attack with full excellency, and your players can), you have only one health track (so your players instead of killing one of n Abyssals could perform exactly the same actions and kill you instead).<br /> <br /> Of course, you could try to split said n Abyssals, but similarly, you can try to attacks your n-Abyssal-package-in-one-enemy from some distance, so it's not obvious to me that here you would get any advantage either.<br /> <br /> Generally, you also don't assume that all n tracks will act before your players (that would be equivalent to all n Abyssals acting before your players, so they would be pretty much hopeless). So, if your enemy's tracks and the players are reasonably interwoven, then the players will in general be able to empty a couple of them each round, so those n tracks are in general never <i>able</i> to concentrate on one player. I mean, you could put all your resources trying to kill one man, but in general you would also like to make sure that no one around sits on tons of Initiative, so you will spread out those attacks.<br /> <br /> Much depends on the specific implementation of multiple tracks, so let me stick to the one that I actually proposed here. These tracks are expensive to maintain. You commit motes to open them, you pay willpower to open them. Once you make them empty, they are closed and you need to pay once more to reopen them. If you make a decisive attack, you cannot combine this Initiative in one attack. You either make withering attacks or decisive, so in general you cannot sit on a ton of Initiative and repeat decisives.<br /> <br /> I believe that this is really reasonably balanced. I don't want to make strong claims because this solution needs clear playtest. But I don't think that trying to focus on one combatant would be close to the optimal strategy.</div> </div> </div> </div>N discrete Abyssals can be split up and forced to spread their attacks. An Abyssal who's really N Abyssalets in a Soulsteel trenchcoat can't. <br /> <br /> Warning: <b>Personal Opinions</b> follow! The idea of splitting fire like that also flies in the face of my personal sensibilities. I believe that it is my duty as GM to first establish a world that is suitable for the PCs to exist in (eg, the enemies likely to be fought aren't pushovers and aren't instant death) and then step from my fair-and-balanced chair over to my be-the-world chair. I believe that it's an outrage for me to deliberately do something a NPC wouldn't do, such as having a highly skilled combatant take deliberately bad actions. It makes me feel like I've crossed from &quot;role-playing game&quot; to &quot;roll-playing game&quot;, that I'm deliberately playing enemies &quot;dumb&quot; so they lose instead of playing enemies the way those enemies should act based on their personalities and experiences (ie, role-playing them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T12:40:57-08:00","id":1368359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1368341#post1368341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that this is really reasonably balanced. I don't want to make strong claims because this solution needs clear playtest. But I don't think that trying to focus on one combatant would be close to the optimal strategy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could run some fights like that in the Arena, but at initial glance you're still unprepared for 5 dedicated combat Solars. Even at Essence 2 and without a combat Supernal you can throw out attacks in the range of 30-35 dice, in combination with chaining attacks or multi-attacks. If you even want a hope of blocking that attack you need to spend a lot of Essence, which you need to do 4 times...and then the Dawn gets to go.<br /> <br /> So you're probably looking at giving it something like 300 motes, and something like Legendary Size, so immune to Onslaught penalties and not counting as Crashed unless all 5 of his initiative tracks are crashed. He'll also need...I'm gonna say at least 60-70 health levels. A very focused Dawn can easily dish out 30 damage in a single turn with his starting initiative, but if the enemy is going full excellency defense some of those attacks will end up missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T12:55:17-08:00","id":1368361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1368359#post1368359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could run some fights like that in the Arena, but at initial glance you're still unprepared for 5 dedicated combat Solars. Even at Essence 2 and without a combat Supernal you can throw out attacks in the range of 30-35 dice, in combination with chaining attacks or multi-attacks. If you even want a hope of blocking that attack you need to spend a lot of Essence, which you need to do 4 times...and then the Dawn gets to go.<br /> <br /> So you're probably looking at giving it something like 300 motes, and something like Legendary Size, so immune to Onslaught penalties and not counting as Crashed unless all 5 of his initiative tracks are crashed. He'll also need...I'm gonna say at least 60-70 health levels. A very focused Dawn can easily dish out 30 damage in a single turn with his starting initiative, but if the enemy is going full excellency defense some of those attacks will end up missing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I'd appreciate that, because I'm clearly biased. I'd sign up for two fights.<br /> <br /> 1) Say, an Essence 5 apocryphal Solar with the following apocryphals: Steel Faster Than Thought times 3, Master's Blade Strikes, Unsurpassed Battle Awarness, Finesse of Supreme Balance, some reasonable choice of regular Melee charms (definitely basic defense charms(, Thunderbolt Attack Prana, 3-4 Ox Bodies, maybe some Soak-adder vs 5 Essence 2 Solars, all of which have maxed out stats, two are combat optimised and one of the two is Melee-Supernal. I could bring you a specific list of charms on either side, since choosing them might be a big task in itself.<br /> <br /> 2) An Essence 3 apocryphal Solar with Steel Faster Thought + a standard choice of Melee charms + Thunderbolt Attack Prana vs two Essence 1 Solars, one of which is combat optimised and one of which ha maxed-out stats.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25764\" data-vbnamecard=\"25764\">vwllss trnt prncss</a> I think that in this case splitting fire would actually be optimal. And when fighting 5 Abyssals, you could theoretically split them, but how do you actually do that if they want to stick together and focus their fire? It's far from trivial. I mean, they will typically <i>want </i>to split and not let your archer sit on a pile of Initiative, but this is the exact same reason why a single opponent would like to split their attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-16-2020, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T13:06:30-08:00","id":1368362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1368361#post1368361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I'd appreciate that, because I'm clearly biased. I'd sign up for two fights.<br /> <br /> 1) Say, an Essence 5 apocryphal Solar with the following apocryphals: Steel Faster Than Thought times 3, Master's Blade Strikes, Unsurpassed Battle Awarness, Finesse of Supreme Balance, some reasonable choice of regular Melee charms (definitely basic defense charms(, Thunderbolt Attack Prana, 3-4 Ox Bodies, maybe some Soak-adder vs 5 Essence 2 Solars, all of which have maxed out stats, two are combat optimised and one of the two is Melee-Supernal. I could bring you a specific list of charms on either side, since choosing them might be a big task in itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do technically non-combat abilities like Survival count as a combat focused ability due to the familiar boosting? Also how un-focused are the ones who aren't combat optimised? Since they're Essence 2 with like 22-26 charms can I give them around 10 combat ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T13:16:35-08:00","id":1368367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1368362#post1368362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do technically non-combat abilities like Survival count as a combat focused ability due to the familiar boosting? Also how un-focused are the ones who aren't combat optimised? Since they're Essence 2 with like 22-26 charms can I give them around 10 combat ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take all liberties when thinking of the charms selection. I guess a regular circle would have:<br /> <br /> 1 combat monster Dawn<br /> 2 combat focused characters who also do something else (like a Night ninja or a Survival supernal with a buffed familiar)<br /> 2 combat-competent but not combat focused character (I guess up to ten combat related charms would be ok, my players have 5-7).<br /> <br /> Generally, whatever seems realistic to you. The opponent on the other hand, should also have all obvious choices: Fire and Stones Strike, Heavenly Guardian Defense, Peony Blossom Strike, multi attack charms (since you cannot otherwise make multiple decisives) and so on.<br /> <br /> By the way, I <i>expect</i> the circle to win. I hope that there will at least be the feeling that they were challenged indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-16-2020, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T13:32:30-08:00","id":1368376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1368341#post1368341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In defense of Initiative Tracks as the solution, I would says this: If you think that n identical Abyssals is reasonable challenge to your circle, then one of these Abyssals with n Initiative Tracks should be generally <i>less </i>challenging. You now have the same base numbers of attacks, but dramatically fewer motes (so you cannot infuse your every attack with full excellency, and your players can), you have only one health track (so your players instead of killing one of n Abyssals could perform exactly the same actions and kill you instead).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly my problem with it.<br /> Assuming 5 Solars vs. 5 Abyssals. The circle of Abyssals don't need to take the optimal strategy to be a threat if you set all 5 of them on one PC while ignoring everyone else their player would probably wonder how they'd personally wronged you. Meanwhile the Abyssal with 5 initiative tracks needs to be comparatively on their A game, the fact they don't have enough motes imo creates the incentive to &quot;dogpile&quot; their first target since the best use for those additional unaugmented attacks is against someone whose already spent essence on defence this round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T13:45:11-08:00","id":1368381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1368376#post1368376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly my problem with it.<br /> Assuming 5 Solars vs. 5 Abyssals. The circle of Abyssals don't need to take the optimal strategy to be a threat if you set all 5 of them on one PC while ignoring everyone else their player would probably wonder how they'd personally wronged you. Meanwhile the Abyssal with 5 initiative tracks needs to be comparatively on their A game, the fact they don't have enough motes imo creates the incentive to &quot;dogpile&quot; their first target since the best use for those additional unaugmented attacks is against someone whose already spent essence on defence this round.</div> </div> </div> </div>And unless each of those Initiative tracks comes with a health track, Five Corpses One Sword can't afford to get hit with a decisive. Ever! So he really can't afford to not alpha-strike anyone with enough accuracy to hit him and enough initiative to bypass Hardness. What's that you say, Solars get to ignore Hardness? Well, I guess he has to keep anyone who can hit him with a Decisive in crash and kill them before they 3-turn out. <br /> <br /> Playing such a character boils down to &quot;Here is the most pressing threat. I must focus on this threat <i>to the exclusion of all else</i> or I will die. Threat neutralized, 20 GOTO 10. <i>or</i> Threat not neutralized, I am about to die.&quot; which isn't really interesting. The more I look at the flow of numbers underlying the system, the more I realize that <b>Exalts are not solo bossfights</b>. It just don't work. Hit the party with a 2-3CD or Behemoth or Wyld thing or other such monster. Heck, give that murderbeing an Exalted ha- er, rider if you want a human face to the struggle. But accept that the Exalt's role there is &quot;Talking Hat&quot;, not &quot;Real Fight, just beat this big thing to end the warmup&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T13:57:35-08:00","id":1368385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1368381#post1368381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more I look at the flow of numbers underlying the system, the more I realize that <b>Exalts are not solo bossfights</b>. It just don't work. Hit the party with a 2-3CD or Behemoth or Wyld thing or other such monster. Heck, give that murderbeing an Exalted ha- er, rider if you want a human face to the struggle. But accept that the Exalt's role there is &quot;Talking Hat&quot;, not &quot;Real Fight, just beat this big thing to end the warmup&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that one actually doesn't follow from the rest of your post. In fiction, you could have single masters as bosses. So, if this particular mechanical representation doesn't achieve that goal, I would personally start to look for another mechanical implementation that <i>will</i> do that.<br /> <br /> As for the specific concerns, let's wait for a third-party playtest <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I mean, currently I think that your objections (plural &quot;your&quot;), really boil down to: against a whole circle suboptimal play of the ST doesn't look so awkward. If you would be playing multiple Abyssals in such a way as to really win, you would essentially have the same constraints: you want to eliminate heavy hitters, you never want to be hit by decisive, etc. I really don't see a difference in what you're writing thus far between a singular fight and a team fight (what you're righting is true and it applies equally well to both scenarios).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-16-2020, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T14:07:52-08:00","id":1368390,"title":"","content":"Prncess is right that the optimal antagonist strategy to win is to alpha strike kill as many PCs as possible in turn one. Should I do that or a more conventional fight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T14:28:41-08:00","id":1368397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1368390#post1368390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prncess is right that the optimal antagonist strategy to win is to alpha strike kill as many PCs as possible in turn one. Should I do that or a more conventional fight?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this pretty much<i> always</i> the optimal strategy. I think it's ok if some participants end up incapacitated (I assume that this is really the end of a big story arc).<br /> <br /> But most of all, play to test it. Imagine that you are playtesting Ahlat fighting against a circle of Solars and you want to see whether he has any chance against them. Play with the same premises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T14:40:13-08:00","id":1368400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1368341#post1368341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> I think that the problem is that whoever your circle is fighting, it is almost always the optimal solution to focus your fire and take them one by one. Of course, this holds both ways. It's almost always the optimal strategy focus your fire and make your hits actually influence your enemies' capabilities.<br /> <br /> In defense of Initiative Tracks as the solution, I would says this: If you think that n identical Abyssals is reasonable challenge to your circle, then one of these Abyssals with n Initiative Tracks should be generally <i>less </i>challenging. You now have the same base numbers of attacks, but dramatically fewer motes (so you cannot infuse your every attack with full excellency, and your players can), you have only one health track (so your players instead of killing one of n Abyssals could perform exactly the same actions and kill you instead).<br /> <br /> Of course, you could try to split said n Abyssals, but similarly, you can try to attacks your n-Abyssal-package-in-one-enemy from some distance, so it's not obvious to me that here you would get any advantage either.<br /> <br /> Generally, you also don't assume that all n tracks will act before your players (that would be equivalent to all n Abyssals acting before your players, so they would be pretty much hopeless). So, if your enemy's tracks and the players are reasonably interwoven, then the players will in general be able to empty a couple of them each round, so those n tracks are in general never <i>able</i> to concentrate on one player. I mean, you could put all your resources trying to kill one man, but in general you would also like to make sure that no one around sits on tons of Initiative, so you will spread out those attacks.<br /> <br /> Much depends on the specific implementation of multiple tracks, so let me stick to the one that I actually proposed here. These tracks are expensive to maintain. You commit motes to open them, you pay willpower to open them. Once you make them empty, they are closed and you need to pay once more to reopen them. If you make a decisive attack, you cannot combine this Initiative in one attack. You either make withering attacks or decisive, so in general you cannot sit on a ton of Initiative and repeat decisives.<br /> <br /> I believe that this is really reasonably balanced. I don't want to make strong claims because this solution needs clear playtest. But I don't think that trying to focus on one combatant would be close to the optimal strategy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the main problem is not &quot;efficacy&quot; per se, but rather fun and ease of play. I may repeat myself, but the advantage of Grod's suggestion (for example) that the enemy gains automatically initiative proportionately to the number of players he is facing is 1) Automatic, 2) Simple and 3) Direct. I'm obviously not saying this is perfect, but I believe the problem of the multi initiative track solution is that it is neither 1) Automatic (you have to make multiple attacks), 2) Simple (You have to account for Charms and stuff on every attack) and is only 3) Direct (you gain initiative which already exists in the game). I believe any solution for the ST to handle complex fights that is neither Automatic nor Simple will make for a complicated solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T21:38:29-08:00","id":1368459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1368397#post1368397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that this pretty much<i> always</i> the optimal strategy. I think it's ok if some participants end up incapacitated (I assume that this is really the end of a big story arc).<br /> <br /> But most of all, play to test it. Imagine that you are playtesting Ahlat fighting against a circle of Solars and you want to see whether he has any chance against them. Play with the same premises.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I did it. For reference this fight took six hours to run a week before midterms, so think about that before suggesting &quot;Oh okay run it again with this little tweak, if you please.&quot;<br /> <br /> I also went pretty easy on the combat efficiency of the characters, mostly because I don\u2019t have the brainpower to do more. Real PCs will have artifact evocations, multiple Martial Arts and all sorts of things. Maybe.<br /> <br /> Maybe.<br /> <br /> Or maybe most of them don\u2019t even have artifact armor or 5s in combat abilities and they die to this guy 100% of the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1368381#post1368381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playing such a character boils down to &quot;Here is the most pressing threat. I must focus on this threat <i>to the exclusion of all else</i> or I will die. Threat neutralized, 20 GOTO 10. <i>or</i> Threat not neutralized, I am about to die.&quot; which isn't really interesting. The more I look at the flow of numbers underlying the system, the more I realize that <b>Exalts are not solo bossfights</b>. It just don't work. Hit the party with a 2-3CD or Behemoth or Wyld thing or other such monster. Heck, give that murderbeing an Exalted ha- er, rider if you want a human face to the struggle. But accept that the Exalt's role there is &quot;Talking Hat&quot;, not &quot;Real Fight, just beat this big thing to end the warmup&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted are meant to fight monsters, not be them. That's both an in-universe distinction and a mechanical one. The Exalted punch UP to fight big things that no man could ever possibly imagine facing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 02-17-2020, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T21:54:29-08:00","id":1368461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1368459#post1368459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I did it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T22:14:58-08:00","id":1368462,"title":"","content":"So having reviewed the fight: I feel that'd be a pretty lousy climax to a game. Motes went flying, the BBEG ate a bunch of hits, two PCs died when the BBEG blew all his motes on his first turn, the BBEG was helpless due to no motes and died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T00:05:32-08:00","id":1368471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1368385#post1368385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, currently I think that your objections (plural &quot;your&quot;), really boil down to: against a whole circle suboptimal play of the ST doesn't look so awkward.</div> </div> </div> </div>If &quot;awkward&quot; also includes suboptimal play potentially getting the soloboss killed in the first or second round. Then yes.<br /> <br /> Please remember. I don't object to bosses or multiple initiative tracks on principle I don't doubt you could have fun with this and benefit hugely from the 'fog of war' where your players don't quite know what they're dealing with*, my problem is with a one size fits all solution.<br /> <br /> *I could absolutely make an Abyssal last a few rounds with some groups simply because the PCs would be like &quot;this mofo's crazy enough to take us all on? that can't be right! what are they planning?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-17-2020, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T06:04:23-08:00","id":1368518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1368459#post1368459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I did it. For reference this fight took six hours to run a week before midterms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you and I appreciate that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T08:29:37-08:00","id":1368940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1366620#post1366620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a few dozen powerful combat focused DBs absolutely could fight the Mask of Winters. The thing is, the Mask isn't some lone dude sitting in his house out in the middle of nowhere. For space I've spoiled just an example of what might await you in Thorns.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Close Allies/Pets</span><br /> <br /> <b>Mask of Winters</b><br /> An incredibly powerful Void Circle necromancer, and former First Age Solar ghost. Wearing a cape weighted down heavily by the hearthstones embedded into it, wearing ancient armor known as Grieving Shelter, and wielding the relic blade Frigid Razor he is a terrifying opponent. On his face he wears the Mask of Winters, depending on the side either enchantingly beautiful or sickeningly terrifying. Most deadly of all, the memory of his Solar life allows him, along with his fellow Deathlords, access the dark mirrors of Solar charms.<br /> <br /> <b>Juggernaut</b><br /> A behemoth of mind-boggling size, able to crush fortresses and armies with a single swipe of its massive hand. The beast is surrounded by a miasma of disease and rotting death, powerful enough to sicken and kill any living creature within days of exposure. A creature so large that the Mask of Winters constructed his primary fortress upon its back. Its legacy stretching back to the dawn of time, where it used to wrestle the great Elemental Dragons. Even the mighty Exalted of the First Age were unable to slay it, merely crippling the monster and forcing it to drag it's colossal broken limbs across the earth. It is said, indeed, that it can never be killed, save for one fated moment in time.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow of Ration Wings</b><br /> A Nephwrack who's company the Mask of Winters keeps. Part advisor, part sorcerous partner, part insane ally. The Shadow of Ration Wings dwells most commonly in the fortress upon the Juggernaut. It has spent the last several decades meticulously weaving it's dark necromancy into every bone and fiber of the behemoth. A powerful sorcerer as well as defender of Juggernaut, it commands the forces defending the fortress whenever the Mask is unable to do so himself.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Abyssals</span><br /> <br /> Below are examples of some of the Mask of Winters Abyssal Exalted. There are several more.<br /> <br /> <b>Apostate in Tatters</b><br /> Midnight caste Abyssal Exalted. A preacher of doom who wanders the streets of Thorns, twisting the minds and hearts of the mortals who still dwell there.<br /> <br /> <b>The Seven-Degreed Physician of Black Maladies</b><br /> Daybreak caste Abyssal Exalted. Apprentice necromancer to the Mask of Winters, the Physician has most recently been put to work devoting all of his time to mass summoning and animation. Sewing together twisting spine chains, summoning legions of undead, and effecting repairs upon the masks necromantic engines off war.<br /> <br /> <b>Typhon</b><br /> Dusk caste Abyssal Exalted. A deadly and stealthy archer in the service of the Mask of Winters. Used during the Mask's wars of conquest as a deadly warrior, but during the lulls in between battles he is sent out to hunt the Mask's enemies abroad.<br /> <br /> <b>Prince Respendant</b><br /> Daybreak caste Abyssal Exalted. A collector of art and artiface from the First Age and before. The Prince is the Mask's personal retriever, scouring the world for the deadliest and most potent ancient spells and devices to bring back to the vaults of Thorns. After years of his work they now burgeon with wonders of the lost ages.<br /> <br /> <b>Artist in Azure Blood</b><br /> Dusk caste Abyssal Exalted. The Mask's great champion. Rather than command troops in battle the Mask directs her to weave a tapestry of screams and blood through his foes. If any adversary is daring enough to challenge the Mask of Winters to single combat, he first requires that they beat his champion the same way. When he is inclined to oblige such a request, anyway.<br /> <br /> <b>Acrid Mist of the Moor</b><br /> Moonshadow caste Abyssal Exalted. The Mask's primary diplomat. One who's silver knives are only matched by her silver tongue. In truth Mist of the Moor is equal parts diplomat and assassin, sent as an envoy to neighboring kingdoms, and in her wake accidents seem to befall all those who would oppose the Mask's whims in that area.<br /> <br /> <b>Perfected tears Upon Alabaster Sorrow</b><br /> Day caste Abyssal Exalted. A special agent of the Mask of Winters, one who partakes in his most underhanded and ambitious schemes. Where most of the Mask's other agents have specific duties, Sorrow embodies the Masks will and whims at the time. A wildcard that the Mask may add to any of his other ventures.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Engines of War</span><br /> <br /> <b>Razor Ivory Tangle</b><br /> A construct of necromancy, a bonestrider. Towering above the battlefield, Eternal Ivory Pillar has been the end off hundreds, perhaps thousands, of the Mask's enemies. Able to gesture towards a group of soldiers and bid their bones to shatter, the shards flinging forth from their bodies and impaling their fellows as they do.<br /> <br /> <b>Eternal Frozen Pillar</b><br /> A warstrider made of soulsteel inlaced with blue jade. It wields the power of cold death. It wields a scythe in battle, one with an ethereal blade. It passes through flesh and steel without leaving a mark, but drags the souls of the living with it as it does. If it should ever need to destroy a solid object, the haft proves more than up to the task.<br /> <br /> <b>Doom of Black Skies</b><br /> A Soulsteel Warstrider with the rare ability to take flight. Shrouded, as it is, by shadow and smoke it can move silently over land or through the air, landing among it's prey like an enormous raptor and also silencing them, forever.<br /> <br /> <b>Siege Weapons</b><br /> Having looted Thorns and taken what the Prince Resplendent could give him from the surrounding area, the Mask's fortresses are equipped with all manner of first age weapons. Lightning Ballista, Implosion Bows, sorcerous tablets that explode in great firestorms when activated, and Sky Mantis Towers which bend the weather to his needs. The Mask also has a few weapons stored in his vaults that seldom been seen in Creation for the last two thousand years.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Forces</span><br /> <br /> <b>Ghostly Agents</b><br /> The Mask commands dozens, or perhaps hundreds, of ghosts from the Underworld. Mortwrights, Nemissaries, Barrow Hound hunters, and other, stranger things. These creatures watch over the lands and buildings of the Mask off Winters. Invisibly they haunt roads and forests, and when he commands it they surge forth on missions of assassination or information gathering.<br /> <br /> <b>War Ghosts</b><br /> Entire legions of ethereal warriors serve the Mask of Winters. Inhabiting and animating suits of armor, and plunging their ghostly blades into living foes, rending flesh as well as spirit as they do.<br /> <br /> <b>Bone Siders</b><br /> Born from the Puppeteer's Plauge, these animated skeletons are walking vectors for that supernatural disease. Even a small band of them is enough to kill an entire village, as their claws infect the living, who then tear their flesh off and cause the plague to erupt anew.<br /> <br /> <b>Giant Maggots</b><br /> Infesting the corpse-body of the Juggernaut are thousands of squirming fat white maggots. Growing to the size of elephants, and equipped with rending maws of razor sharp shredding fangs, they attempt to devour any creature not under the protection off the Mask's invitation.<br /> <br /> <b>Zombies</b><br /> Near endless tides of once human citizens, now turned into shambling corpses. Fodder for the Mask's wars. Their tireless limbs and gut-wrenching stench overpower most foes. Even those that can boast defeating a horde of the Mask's zombies almost never do so without becoming exhausted. Completely drained from hours of hewing undead limbs, they're easy prey for the Deathlord's other forces. When lead by Shadow of Ration Wings, the zombies become far deadlier. Empowered by the Dawn of Dead Stars they often overpower even trained soldiers.<br /> <br /> <b>Human Forces</b><br /> After subjugating Thorns the Mask of Winters has had his pick of loyal human warriors. Their souls worn down to surrender and rebuild by the Mask and his Abyssal Exalted. Legions of trained and equipped former soldiers of Thorns now serve him. In addition to their battlefield roles they often act as spies or traitors to any resistance force attempting to overthrow the Mask's rule.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's not everything the Mask has, and a lot of those headings were abbreviated. Fighting the Mask of Winters is way WAY more than just beating up the Mask in his throne room.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. If the PCs are attacking somewhere like Thorns where the enemy enjoys an obvious home field advantage it's possible to have them basically wondering from one mini-boss fight to another. What follows is frankly lowballing things by assuming only 5 Abyssals and focusing on them.<br /> <br /> The Dusk Caste general is waiting with a well-calibrated battle group(s), keep going further in? (next scene)<br /> The Daybreak Caste necrosurgeon has some kind of legendary sized undead monster as backup, keep going further in? (next scene)<br /> The Day Caste archer has set themselves up with an impressive kill zone and traps, keep going further in? (next scene)<br /> The Midnight Caste has an unexpected ally that they've won over with their ideology maybe their Lunar mate or someone the PCs care about, keep going further in? (next scene)<br /> The Moonshadow Caste diplomat is the penultimate encounter, they saw what happened to the 4 other Abyssals and really don't want to die for this shit so there's a chance for them to social characters to gain a slightly unsavoury ally here but if they fear duplicity and scrutinise everything they do or pounce because they won't let this one get away it could be its own exhausting encounter, keep going further in? (next scene)<br /> Mask of Winters (final boss) you can make this a two stage encounter with Juggernaut smashing an enormous hand through the roof of his palace once he starts struggling.<br /> <br /> The rest of the city's undead presence is largely held in reserve for if the PCs dawdle to help them regain motes or get smart and start to circumvent the above encounters i.e. if a PC declares a fact Thorns has absurdly spacious sewers that will let them circumvent the open area with the Day Caste waiting to ambush them in a hail of arrows from long range. These substitute mini-boss squads will still play to their strengths so if we keep with the example of the PCs taking the sewer to avoid the Day Caste they might encounter fairly powerful war ghosts or nemissaries who- playing to their own strengths might have a number of spare bodies lying around so if Ghost Eating isn't employed against them they'll seemingly die then ambush a little later in new armour or meat suits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T17:53:23-08:00","id":1369063,"title":"","content":"May we try to make a catalog of mechanical devices for boss fights? Just to brainstorm some abstract ideas. So far, we seem to have:<br /> <br /> 1. Multiple Initiative tracks (less dynamic then I thought, probably better than in the most pessimistic scenarios. It would possibly go better, now that we know that Thunderbolt Attack Prana cannot be easily spammed; plus, I intended tracks to shut down when Initiative goes to zero, but this is absolutely the fault of my wording).<br /> <br /> 2. Scene-long reflexive clashes (possibly with twists, like clashing with grapples).<br /> <br /> 3. Multiple health tracks (possibly with regeneration, possibly with debilitating effects, when a health track closes).<br /> <br /> 4. Cap on the decisive damage (Legendary size, the charm that Octavian has).<br /> <br /> What other ideas do you have? I was thinking of <br /> <br /> 5. Some powers to forcefully isolate characters (some charms taking away their actions or relocating them multiple range bands). We have some precedents in published charms, but the risk here is that it's very unpleasant to players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T17:59:03-08:00","id":1369066,"title":"","content":"From the Mahicara fight I just ran it seems pretty good to be able to initiate multiple massive AoE environmental damage effects every turn. I also might suggest a range of abilities that target different defenses, like something that can attack through an enemy's resolve unmodified by intimacies.<br /> <br /> Especially when it takes no resources, like no action, no motes, ect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 02-19-2020, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T18:33:35-08:00","id":1369074,"title":"","content":"At least they got rid of the part about schlongs in the title of the question...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T00:08:58-08:00","id":1369101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369063#post1369063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May we try to make a catalog of mechanical devices for boss fights? Just to brainstorm some abstract ideas. So far, we seem to have:<br /> <br /> 1. Multiple Initiative tracks (less dynamic then I thought, probably better than in the most pessimistic scenarios. It would possibly go better, now that we know that Thunderbolt Attack Prana cannot be easily spammed; plus, I intended tracks to shut down when Initiative goes to zero, but this is absolutely the fault of my wording).<br /> <br /> 2. Scene-long reflexive clashes (possibly with twists, like clashing with grapples).<br /> <br /> 3. Multiple health tracks (possibly with regeneration, possibly with debilitating effects, when a health track closes).<br /> <br /> 4. Cap on the decisive damage (Legendary size, the charm that Octavian has).<br /> <br /> What other ideas do you have? I was thinking of <br /> <br /> 5. Some powers to forcefully isolate characters (some charms taking away their actions or relocating them multiple range bands). We have some precedents in published charms, but the risk here is that it's very unpleasant to players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Automatic initiative gain (Grod idea to gain depending on the number of PC or just a static gain) so the ennemy is always a threat<br /> <br /> Attack with fixed amount of damage (I believe the phenix like elemental in Ex3 Core got one) so you can always damage even with low initiative","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T06:08:19-08:00","id":1369125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369063#post1369063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May we try to make a catalog of mechanical devices for boss fights? Just to brainstorm some abstract ideas. So far, we seem to have:<br /> <br /> 1. Multiple Initiative tracks (less dynamic then I thought, probably better than in the most pessimistic scenarios. It would possibly go better, now that we know that Thunderbolt Attack Prana cannot be easily spammed; plus, I intended tracks to shut down when Initiative goes to zero, but this is absolutely the fault of my wording).<br /> <br /> 2. Scene-long reflexive clashes (possibly with twists, like clashing with grapples).<br /> <br /> 3. Multiple health tracks (possibly with regeneration, possibly with debilitating effects, when a health track closes).<br /> <br /> 4. Cap on the decisive damage (Legendary size, the charm that Octavian has).<br /> <br /> What other ideas do you have? I was thinking of<br /> <br /> 5. Some powers to forcefully isolate characters (some charms taking away their actions or relocating them multiple range bands). We have some precedents in published charms, but the risk here is that it's very unpleasant to players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seen in a <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/272809/The-Thousand-Sanctioned-Beasts--Martial-Artists\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Vault entry</a> : give the boss 1 free turn immediately after each of his non-trivial enemies' turns (these free turns never cause clashes for being on the same Tick). It's basically an action-economy equalizer, but without the multiple initiative tracks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T07:24:33-08:00","id":1369128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369125#post1369125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seen in a <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/272809/The-Thousand-Sanctioned-Beasts--Martial-Artists\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Vault entry</a> : give the boss 1 free turn immediately after each of his non-trivial enemies' turns (these free turns never cause clashes for being on the same Tick). It's basically an action-economy equalizer, but without the multiple initiative tracks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Has someone tested this in play? How was it?<br /> <br /> Additional actions was my first idea at shifting action economy, but I was afraid that in Exalted this can lead to an obnoxious amounts of Initiative on the enemy's side. Initiative tracks seemed more safe to me, since you're forbidden to use that Initiative in one powerful strike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T14:16:52-08:00","id":1369200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369063#post1369063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Multiple Initiative tracks (less dynamic then I thought, probably better than in the most pessimistic scenarios. It would possibly go better, now that we know that Thunderbolt Attack Prana cannot be easily spammed; plus, I intended tracks to shut down when Initiative goes to zero, but this is absolutely the fault of my wording).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this might work best as it is with the Fang Blossom, which is a published monster in Hundred Devil's Night Parade. It's an enormous carnivorous plant that when it feels threatened it activates a number of vine tendrils equal to twice the number of present combatants. They each have their own initiative tracks and health tracks separate from the main core, and the core itself is unkillable until all the vines have been destroyed.<br /> <br /> Also it has charms to grow more fanged blossoms and more vines as the combat progresses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369063#post1369063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Scene-long reflexive clashes (possibly with twists, like clashing with grapples).</div> </div> </div> </div>This could work, it might drain a single opponent of motes really quickly though, and making it scenelong might be a bit much. Having a charm activate until next turn might be better.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369063#post1369063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Multiple health tracks (possibly with regeneration, possibly with debilitating effects, when a health track closes).</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to work really well. Also it automatically puts a limit on how much damage can be done with a single attack. If you fire off a 38L decisive against a health track with only 2 boxes left to fill, that's not the best option.<br /> <br /> <br /> Most importantly I think using multiple techniques at once is helpful. Have an enemy with Legendary Size, <i>and </i>multiple health tracks, and AoE attacks, <i>and </i>a poison miasma surrounding it, <i>and </i>a swarm of tiny appendages that are treated as a battlegroup, <i>and </i>every time one of its health tracks gets killed have it explode with another AoE environmental effect, <i>and </i>have them slowly regenerate if it's still alive, <i>and </i>have the main health track be invulnerable until all its appendages are killed, <i>and</i> make sure that it's total health levels number in the triple digits.<br /> <br /> THAT'S a dominating adversary that even Solars will tremble at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T15:46:09-08:00","id":1369221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">give the boss 1 free turn immediately after each of his non-trivial enemies' turns (these free turns never cause clashes for being on the same Tick). It's basically an action-economy equalizer, but without the multiple initiative tracks.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369128#post1369128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Has someone tested this in play? How was it?<br /> <br /> Additional actions was my first idea at shifting action economy, but I was afraid that in Exalted this can lead to an obnoxious amounts of Initiative on the enemy's side. Initiative tracks seemed more safe to me, since you're forbidden to use that Initiative in one powerful strike.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't had the opportunity to test it myself. That said I think the way the boss's extra turns are spread out evenly in between the PCs' turns should give PCs a better chance to keep the boss's initiative from snowballing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T16:05:19-08:00","id":1369226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369221#post1369221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I haven't had the opportunity to test it myself. That said I think the way the boss's extra turns are spread out evenly in between the PCs' turns should give PCs a better chance to keep the boss's initiative from snowballing.</div> </div> </div> </div>My main worry would be that it can convert a combat-unfocused character from &quot;not helping much&quot; into &quot;actively unhelpful please leave the fight&quot;. <i>Especially</i> if multiple combat-unfocused characters wind up at the bottom of the initiative stack and the boss gets multiple effectively-unopposed turns in a row.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T16:47:52-08:00","id":1369230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369226#post1369226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My main worry would be that it can convert a combat-unfocused character from &amp;quot;not helping much&amp;quot; into &amp;quot;actively unhelpful please leave the fight&amp;quot;. <i>Especially</i> if multiple combat-unfocused characters wind up at the bottom of the initiative stack and the boss gets multiple effectively-unopposed turns in a row.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be a problem with abundant reflexive clashes too. Somebody wearing light armor throws out a 10 dice withering attack, gets reflexively clashed and instantly crashed, giving the big bad +15 initiative for the effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T17:13:50-08:00","id":1369234,"title":"","content":"Reflexive clashes and counterattacks are at least a little better than granting them extra actions from your mere presence because at least you have the option to take different actions.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=v-sgdj1Osrs\" data-code=\"v-sgdj1Osrs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/v-sgdj1Osrs/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T17:57:11-08:00","id":1369249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369234#post1369234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reflexive clashes and counterattacks are at least a little better than granting them extra actions from your mere presence because at least you have the option to take different actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those can have the problem of &quot;At least this good or don't try&quot; where if you're unlikely to win the clash it's better to not attack. Clashes in particular, since losing the clash means you cost them some motes and suffered horribly for it. <br /> <br /> Actually, this brings me to an interesting thought. How do you design a boss for the possibility that the PCs look at its combat abilities and just defend and throw the social system at it instead? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T17:59:16-08:00","id":1369252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369249#post1369249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, this brings me to an interesting thought. How do you design a boss for the possibility that the PCs look at its combat abilities and just defend and throw the social system at it instead</div> </div> </div> </div>Intended design? If the boss isn't also some kind of immutable being or social demi-god sitting back and trying to use the social system to persuade it to stop or something is legit.<br /> <br /> It works both ways though, an amazing social powerhouse can throw instill and persuade actions out in combat against the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T19:03:17-08:00","id":1369262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369252#post1369252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Intended design? If the boss isn't also some kind of immutable being or social demi-god sitting back and trying to use the social system to persuade it to stop or something is legit.<br /> <br /> It works both ways though, an amazing social powerhouse can throw instill and persuade actions out in combat against the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but it'll short-circuit a number of big-group-countermeasures. For example, if nobody's throwing attacks at the boss, it doesn't get any clashes or counters. <br /> I'm imagining a group (far more competent than mine was) that immediately realizes &quot;Hey, this guy only really hurts if we try to hurt him&quot; and throws a million social actions around while the Dawn spams Defend Other (WAR LION STANCE) because he no talk good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T19:26:53-08:00","id":1369267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369262#post1369262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but it'll short-circuit a number of big-group-countermeasures. For example, if nobody's throwing attacks at the boss, it doesn't get any clashes or counters.<br /> I'm imagining a group (far more competent than mine was) that immediately realizes &quot;Hey, this guy only really hurts if we try to hurt him&quot; and throws a million social actions around while the Dawn spams Defend Other (WAR LION STANCE) because he no talk good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you mean. It's probably a good idea to give the boss some powerful intimacies so that he doesn't instantly go down to Social influence, with maybe some charms to defend against it. Otherwise just sitting there taking his attacks should be tense enough.<br /> <br /> Mahicara has a charm that fills the area out to 3 range bands with a 6L/round, difficulty 5 magma hazard for three rounds, no reset, and its withering fist attacks strike everyone within 2 range bands. It has one defining principle, to walk from pole to pole, and if it has any other intimacies they're probably hatred for the Exalted. I'd say if your group is knee-deep in red hot lava and dodging* enormous fist swings every turn you're probably feeling the pressure. If you can even get it to hear you in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> *literally, the shockwave attack is unblockable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T19:33:51-08:00","id":1369268,"title":"","content":"To be fair, there\u2019s limits to what social influence can do to a character. Especially if they don\u2019t know what his Intimacies are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T01:50:15-08:00","id":1369305,"title":"","content":"There's also potentially relevant social penalties, for example it's -5 to try and get a favour from someone you're openly antagonising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T03:16:07-08:00","id":1369313,"title":"","content":"Yeah, my last couple game sessions involved negotiating with a series of Abyssals about whom our circle knew almost nothing. I\u2019m fairly certain that if I hadn\u2019t gone in openly as an Eclipse, they\u2019d have made mincemeat of my character. As it was, they probably still would\u2019ve killed him if he\u2019d persisted beyond their initial agreement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T08:42:34-08:00","id":1369844,"title":"","content":"Something I find useful for sourcing boss mechanics. Looking at 2nd edition charms (ideally 2.5 since it's mechanically much closer) which haven't been included in Ex3 or were changed significantly and trying to explore the though process of them not making the cut.<br /> <br /> i.e. Adamant Skin Technique (2.5 version) lets you reduce the damage of an attack to 0 <i>after it hits you </i>for 8 motes, it has a built in weakness that can shut down when you use the charm but it's a pretty permissive one. In a 3rd edition combat environment that's nuts because free excellencies are gone and damage is now built up via successive actions via withering attacks, the ability to just take a successful decisive to 0 after it hits is huge!<br /> <br /> So a character with this charm and no other considerations would have an absolute game changing power. You'd basically have to keep making cheap/low damage decisive attacks to try and mote tap them. There's two easy says to way to weaken a defensive charm from a previous edition, the first is to apply the Perilous keyword, which would kind of turn it into an all or nothing version of Heavenly Guardian Defence promising invulnerability when you had even 1i but vulnerable in initiative crash with no scope to add something like Protection of Celestial Bliss. I don't like it, there's too much incentive to crash your opponent and dismantle them and this makes it mandatory. The other would be to make it once per scene with a reset condition. I like this far more. Essentially the proposed charm would be the best parts of Ruin Abrasing Shrug and Seven Shadow Evasion (it's a bit stronger than that but we're still in broad strokes here).<br /> <br /> There's still good reasons to turn this down as a custom charm. It would fufill the role of two charms in different trees and notably stealing Dodge's big panic button charm for Resistance in the process.<br /> <br /> For a boss though? That's a handy way to condense their charms and reduce your mental load as a Storyteller. So I'll give it the same reset condition as Ruin Abrasing Shrug and since having no way to resist your initiative being rest to base is both really powerful and extremely annoying to the person you're doing it to I'll add the initiative loss clause from the Dragon-Blooded Resistance charm Perfected Scales of the Dragon.<br /> <br /> Perfected Skin of Adamant (8m; Reflexive; Instant; Decisive-only): After being hit by an attack, but before damage is rolled reduce all damage to 0. Attackers lose two Initiative instead of resetting to base. Once per scene, unless reset by taking no withering or decisive damage on three separate damage rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T18:59:18-08:00","id":1369946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369844#post1369844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's still good reasons to turn this down as a custom charm. It would fufill the role of two charms in different trees and notably stealing Dodge's big panic button charm for Resistance in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally agree with what you wrote, but I don't think that two panic buttons with slightly different functions are bad design (the hypothetical Resistance one doesn't prevent other possible effects of being hit, like flying a couple of range bands or being poisoned; the Dodge one doesn't protect you against Enviromental Damage), quite the contrary. I could easily imagine even five or six different panic buttons in different places. It shouldn't be to easy to get two of them. <br /> <br /> Generally, attrition gets boring mostly when the pattern is clear. If you can perfectly dodge an attack using willpower, you could easily skip next [willpower] attack and start watching the fight again when it gets interesting. On the other hand, <i>complicated</i> attrition in which you have several distinct factors to follow and individually they can go up and down (on of which is &quot;can I use my panic button&quot;) makes for a tactically deep game. <br /> <br /> Currently, we already have two different panic buttons; one in Dogde and one in Occult (that charm that makes you impossible to kill, unless you are at you last health level). I think that another one with Resistance with slightly different effects and rather deep in a tree could be an interesting addition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T20:07:24-08:00","id":1369957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369946#post1369946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could easily imagine even five or six different panic buttons in different places. It shouldn't be to easy to get two of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think that having too many of them would choke the combat 2e style, wouldn't it? 2e Perfect Defenses also had Flaws of Invulnerability, and things like Adamant Skin Technique were vulnerable to badtouch effects and flurries and stuff.<br /> <br /> Also...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369946#post1369946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dodge one doesn't protect you against Enviromental Damage</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it totally does. Two of the examples that you can dodge in the charm are a cyclone and an avalanche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T20:24:35-08:00","id":1369959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369957#post1369957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that having too many of them would choke the combat 2e style, wouldn't it? 2e Perfect Defenses also had Flaws of Invulnerability, and things like Adamant Skin Technique were vulnerable to badtouch effects and flurries and stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. I just think that two is quite far from too many. I think that a soft cap on what is too many is some function of how many <i>really</i> dangerous attacks can the opposition reliably make.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369957#post1369957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it totally does. Two of the examples that you can dodge in the charm are a cyclone and an avalanche.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess you're right. I misunderstood the description and thought that it prevents <i>either</i> an attack (in the technical sense) <i>or</i> uncountable damage, like Heavenly Guardian Defense does. The wording isn't crystal-clear though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-24-2020, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T21:03:04-08:00","id":1369961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369946#post1369946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I generally agree with what you wrote, but I don't think that two panic buttons with slightly different functions are bad design (the hypothetical Resistance one doesn't prevent other possible effects of being hit, like flying a couple of range bands or being poisoned; the Dodge one doesn't protect you against Enviromental Damage), quite the contrary. I could easily imagine even five or six different panic buttons in different places. It shouldn't be to easy to get two of them.<br /> <br /> Generally, attrition gets boring mostly when the pattern is clear. If you can perfectly dodge an attack using willpower, you could easily skip next [willpower] attack and start watching the fight again when it gets interesting. On the other hand, <i>complicated</i> attrition in which you have several distinct factors to follow and individually they can go up and down (on of which is &quot;can I use my panic button&quot;) makes for a tactically deep game.<br /> <br /> Currently, we already have two different panic buttons; one in Dogde and one in Occult (that charm that makes you impossible to kill, unless you are at you last health level). I think that another one with Resistance with slightly different effects and rather deep in a tree could be an interesting addition.</div> </div> </div> </div> My experience is that if it were introduced it would be more likely to learned instead of Seven Shadow Evasion (and Dodge as a whole) rather than used in conjunction with it. That doesn't exactly endear me to it, but there's a style of game and a sort of player where approving it for general use wouldn't be a potential problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-24-2020, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T21:31:39-08:00","id":1369964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369959#post1369959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely. I just think that two is quite far from too many. I think that a soft cap on what is too many is some function of how many <i>really</i> dangerous attacks can the opposition reliably make.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose as long as they're limited enough and costed appropriately. I just really, really don't want a return to 2e perfect spam. My group has kind of run up against it already in 3e when our whole circle fought an Essence 2-3 Resistance Supernal Solar, and the only reason the fight didn't last six hours is because Revolving Bow Discipline completely breaks Aegis of Invincible Might due to a messed up rules interaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T21:37:14-08:00","id":1369967,"title":"","content":"I think that one really basic criterion in the design, and, what, to me, was ultimately wrong with 2e-style perfect defenses is the following test: Realistically, is there any scenario in which I don't know whether to use this power or not? A bad situation would be when we would have so many panic buttons (or such abundance of really strong attacks) that I don't really hesitate whether or not to use one, either because I have plenty of them or that I can't hope surviving without them. <br /> <br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> noted, if I understand correctly, another question is whether it is even a meaningful choice whether or not to have this power in the first place, and Dodge tree seems &quot;safer&quot; as it's not as universally appealing as Resistance. Do I understand you correctly?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T22:04:50-08:00","id":1369971,"title":"","content":"There is the old 2e adage of &quot;Don't fuck with perfects until you fix lethality.&quot;<br /> <br /> One thing that I like about 3e that I wouldn't want to change is that, usually, an enormous effort brought into an attack requires a likewise enormous effort in defense. Either that or likely that it will still punch through and do something. If you get attacked by some giant enemy who's got 35 initiative and double 9s on the damage roll something is still going to happen. If you use Heavenly Guardian Defense to nullify it you spent some initiative to do it, if you use Adamant Skin Technique some of that damage is coming through, if you use Uncanny Shroud Defense you probably still lost some health levels from it.<br /> <br /> Seven Shadow Evasion is about as close as it gets, because for 4m 1wp you force them to waste all the motes that they put into the attack, but they also only count as having missed, and it's not really able to be spammed much. With really generous level-2 stunts I guess you could safely use it every fight, but that's about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T00:04:36-08:00","id":1369988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369964#post1369964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose as long as they're limited enough and costed appropriately. I just really, really don't want a return to 2e perfect spam. My group has kind of run up against it already in 3e when our whole circle fought an Essence 2-3 Resistance Supernal Solar, and the only reason the fight didn't last six hours is because Revolving Bow Discipline completely breaks Aegis of Invincible Might due to a messed up rules interaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd never put Aegis of Invincible Might on a boss character.<br /> The conditions of the invulnerability being maintained are heavily orientated towards the player who activated it and how they've built the character and less so any strategy from the people they're fighting. This is especially the case if Diamond Body Prana is involved because the random value soak means it's be difficult to do the math and know who among the PCs will be able to hurt the boss ahead of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T06:17:20-08:00","id":1370041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369988#post1369988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd never put Aegis of Invincible Might on a boss character.<br /> The conditions of the invulnerability being maintained are heavily orientated towards the player who activated it and how they've built the character and less so any strategy from the people they're fighting. This is especially the case if Diamond Body Prana is involved because the random value soak means it's be difficult to do the math and know who among the PCs will be able to hurt the boss ahead of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my sorcerer character was effectively completely useless, same with the Eclipse sea captain, the Zenith ex-soldier might have been able to do something on a lucky hit, but really the Dawn archer was our only hope.<br /> <br /> Even then he\u2019d normally be useless except he shot her literally 30-40 times in one action, and even dealing 0 damage every hit that\u2019s 1i for hitting each time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T17:17:54-08:00","id":1370187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1369967#post1369967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> noted, if I understand correctly, another question is whether it is even a meaningful choice whether or not to have this power in the first place, and Dodge tree seems &quot;safer&quot; as it's not as universally appealing as Resistance. Do I understand you correctly?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's two major factors here.<br /> #1 Supernal ability makes me wary of deliberate overlap.<br /> #2 In the context of this discussion disincentivising Dodge shackles yourself as a Storyteller. A player character without any investment in that ability tends to forget what retreating is and that can seriously get in the way if they're encountering antagonists strong enough to fight five Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-25-2020, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T19:50:37-08:00","id":1373312,"title":"","content":"Something, that I've used recently that might be helpful for people trying to create major antagonists.<br /> <br /> A plot level power that requires a successful gambit or succession of gambits in order to disable. You could do a comic book version of Corvus Glaive deal where the only way to truly defeat him is to disarm him and stab him with his own glaive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T20:14:05-08:00","id":1373317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1373312#post1373312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something, that I've used recently that might be helpful for people trying to create major antagonists.<br /> <br /> A plot level power that requires a successful gambit or succession of gambits in order to disable. You could do a comic book version of Corvus Glaive deal where the only way to truly defeat him is to disarm him and stab him with his own glaive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Exalted has done this before to some effect. Wasn't there a published adventure with a jade bull that was invincible except for one specific thing? Also there's an enemy in Hundred Devil Night Parade which is invulnerable to normal damage, so that checks out for 3e anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T07:54:47-08:00","id":1373378,"title":"","content":"Gambits do make this more significant than they used to be, in 2e I had a difficult time getting people to remember 'Called Shots' even existed because they were so much harder to pull off than just stabbing someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T04:14:24-07:00","id":1396345,"title":"","content":"wasnt there a heartstone in previous editions that made the bearer unable to be killed unless someone went on a quest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T10:08:38-07:00","id":1396421,"title":"","content":"Thanks for reposting your question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T12:15:54-07:00","id":1396443,"title":"","content":"I'm near positive there wasn't, otherwise somebody in one of the games I was in would have brought it up.<br /> <br /> There was a concept that the Deathlords couldn't be killed except in certain ways specific to the particular Deathlords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T12:39:26-07:00","id":1396449,"title":"","content":"It might be the Gem of Incomparable Wellness. A quest in the sense of going &quot;okay, you're immortal&quot; then weighing them down and throwing them in the ocean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T17:11:36-07:00","id":1396541,"title":"","content":"very rarely would I do something as simple as having the party fight a villain alone. I like to play my main big bads like they are pcs and will have them use tactics and such include escaping if at all possible, of course the big bad's lair had a back door silly pants","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T19:17:03-07:00","id":1397424,"title":"","content":"I always kinda wished that Exalted had started with Dragonblood as the &quot;Default&quot; Exalt in the core books. As they're a much more default RPG protagonist style group, with room to grow and lots of options for antagonists that are legit scary. So much so I struggled with Solars even being viable PCs until most of the Splat Books for others (AT LEAST DB, Lunars, and Abyssals) to make them even have some interesting, fun threats. Sure, I admit I'm a terrible GM too, so that's a different matter. But with DB as the default things scale so much better.<br /> <br /> That said, yeah. Single Bosses are such a staple in Gamer Culture. Probably blame video games. But I feel that's even more important in a game like this, which definitely has some video game inspirations. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T20:22:43-07:00","id":1397432,"title":"","content":"In my last Solar game (Modern) the last boss was essentially a superpowered Warstrider that was also infused with the power of the Neverborn then hijacked by the Neverborn. My PC's were not minmaxed but they were still no slouches to combat. It very easily engaged with all of them, and in the end they decided to banish the abomination back to the pit of the Labyrinth than fight it. Mainly because (1) They did not expect the BBEG would be stupid enough to do something to give the Neverborn control of an N/A Warstrider (he did) (2) The PC's were in no way equipped to deal with the literal manifestation of entropy and despair. One PC had to sacrifice themselves (along with a near-game long NPC) to seal the bastard.<br /> <br /> If it was an Exalt however, I'd make a boss group. The only way to make an Exalt into &quot;Boss mode&quot; is to either (a) give them plot specific and broken powers or increase their soak to disgusting heights. The latter makes the game a slog and makes me wonder if god abandoned me long ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T12:56:38-07:00","id":1398225,"title":"","content":"So video I want to share, spoilers for season 2 of Wakfu.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HjBuhFPRTO0\" data-code=\"HjBuhFPRTO0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/HjBuhFPRTO0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div> There's English subtitles if you're confused what's going on.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Qilby has the same basic moveset as Yugo which makes Adamai think he can win. Then Qilby starts spamming attacks in a way Yugo is simply incapable of. In Ex3 terms I consider it a good demonstration of how a significant disparity in essence to play around with can make a difference.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1397432#post1397432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it was an Exalt however, I'd make a boss group. The only way to make an Exalt into &quot;Boss mode&quot; is to either (a) give them plot specific and broken powers or increase their soak to disgusting heights. The latter makes the game a slog and makes me wonder if god abandoned me long ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with high soak as a solution is that it has the illusion of fairness since under that everyone's able to hit and do a little damage but it's likely to produce a by the numbers affair with no surprises what so ever. <br /> <br /> One of the most often overlooked parts when talking about encounter design is how different GMs and their groups measures success. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 06-25-2020, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T13:50:59-07:00","id":1399369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1398225#post1398225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with high soak as a solution is that it has the illusion of fairness since under that everyone's able to hit and do a little damage but it's likely to produce a by the numbers affair with no surprises what so ever.<br /> <br /> One of the most often overlooked parts when talking about encounter design is how different GMs and their groups measures success.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yea I'm against higher soaks as a solution as well. Really the only time I see it necessary is maybe if a player is using a legendary size DBT Lunar which is capable of a disgusting damage output, but unless the other players do something similar then you're really just hosing the other players.<br /> <br /> Also because it slows the game down to a slog, where unless you did a one true build of overwhelming/post-soak stackers than things just go on forever.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T06:23:57-07:00","id":1399582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1399369#post1399369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea I'm against higher soaks as a solution as well. Really the only time I see it necessary is maybe if a player is using a legendary size DBT Lunar which is capable of a disgusting damage output, but unless the other players do something similar then you're really just hosing the other players.<br /> <br /> Also because it slows the game down to a slog, where unless you did a one true build of overwhelming/post-soak stackers than things just go on forever.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I just realized that I think a part of the problem is Soak is a one size fit all solution (is that the correct expression ? I'm not sure). For a simple comparison, take DD : You usually will have some good defenses (for example AC and Fortitude if you are a tank), and you also will have some weaknesses. In Exalted, I'd say it's quite regular to have a character with no apparent fighting combat weakness, especially in the form of Soak. Considering it's not that hard to also raise your other defenses (for example I've almost never seen any character with less than 4 resolve), and that there are (I think I'm becoming senile because I've written this phrase so many times on this forum) not enough tools at the hands of the ST to suggest using special options (how good are undodgeable and unblockable attacks ? Should I give them often to enemies ? I've also tried to make enemies attack more targetted on abilities like Athletics or Resistance in the form of special attacks from the enemies), I think it makes Soak a too centralized option, where almost all ennemies will attack Soak, because it asks non trivial efforts from the ST to prepare something else, and so Soak becomes too polarized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T09:15:19-07:00","id":1399604,"title":"","content":"My experience with soak is that there's this perception that hitting and doing minimum damage is adequate for player engagement but there's an irrational fear of someone having a &quot;wasted turn&quot; because mid-round the boss has done something like moved out of engagement range or disappeared to try and re-establish surprise.<br /> <br /> A lot of interesting offensive options are also removed from the table for similar reasons out of fear that someone might feel &quot;singled out&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T09:37:05-07:00","id":1399608,"title":"","content":"I'm afraid I dont see the connection between soak and the wasted turn could you explain it again with more details ? Thank you for your time and sorry for bothering you","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T09:56:14-07:00","id":1399611,"title":"","content":"No problem.<br /> If the boss depends on high soak then the players are probably still at least getting to roll their overwhelming damage (unless the boss has charms which negate it) and for a lot of Storytellers that's sufficient to say that everyone at the table is engaged in the scene. If these blows were all being dodged, parried or inapplicable this wouldn't be the case.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 06-28-2020, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T12:33:29-07:00","id":1399636,"title":"","content":"Yeah okay I see your point. I think that's true to a certain extent, but some players (and the ST) tend to notice quickly that, when you throw 2-3 dice for Initiative damage, meanwhile other players regularly deals 10+, they are <i>useless</i> in the scene, which I feel is kinda bad for the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T15:58:58-07:00","id":1399685,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's the problem it overvalues minimal participation when really it's about how it makes players feel.<br /> <br /> There's a decent chance that the players who can't attack because the boss just disappeared and is about to ambush them are having way more fun, despite the fact they're technically doing less than they would be against the soakbeast boss because they're invested in what's going on. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T05:47:44-07:00","id":1400057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1399611#post1399611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No problem.<br /> If the boss depends on high soak then the players are probably still at least getting to roll their overwhelming damage (unless the boss has charms which negate it) and for a lot of Storytellers that's sufficient to say that everyone at the table is engaged in the scene. If these blows were all being dodged, parried or inapplicable this wouldn't be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true, and yet the soakbeast is also one of the iconic types of enemies. If you are going to use one I suggest one of two approaches. If your group is large enough (mine usually is), you can find a way to split the group having the mental and social characters doing something important that's more their thing, while sending the optimized combat terrors after your big bad soakbeast. This doesn't really solve your problem though, as all you're really doing is saying 'hey you're not tall enough to ride this ride, scram kid!' Still this is one way to have a soakbeast fight without alienating certain players if you're subtle enough.<br /> <br /> Second method requires you to have an excellent grasp of your players thought processes and their characters abilities. For instance, if one my players is a Twilight with excellent mental faculties and shattering grasp and craftsman needs no tools the could destroy the foundational support of something large enough to squish the big bad, damage at least enough to make it easier to fight, or knock it prone and pin it for a while. Or they could scream for the party to fall back as they destroy the supporting chain on a bridge over a chasm (the other destroyed earlier by the Night's cascade of cutting terror, thus did the brilliant Twilight hatch a plan for gravity, creation's deadliest weapon, to finish their nearly invincible foe).<br /> <br /> That's just one example but there are many, many ways clever players can participate in combat without throwing massive damage if their ST goes with the spirit of Exalted using it's stunt system and the rule of cool. And for those not so clever players you can give them a nudge with ability rolls to give them subtle or not so subtle hints on what they could do to impact the battle. The thing here is that I believe you have to cater to both the kill monsters and the much less combat capable characters. The badasses shouldn't go from essence 1 to 5 never seeing a soakbeast just because the eclipse is never going to take melee beyond 2, and the savants and healers shouldn't be punished for exploring excellence out side of combat. Both are capable of changing the world, because both are Exalted, the masters of creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T18:17:11-07:00","id":1400224,"title":"","content":"The main problem with the soakbeast is its over use.<br /> <br /> In the you mention context I'm probably going to be less worried with the Eclipse or the Twilight with little to no combat investment and more concerned about the Night with Thrown because they could be heavily invested in combat, but in a way that a soakbeast would shrug off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":".  inexplicable gap 06-30-2020, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T18:46:16-07:00","id":1400231,"title":"","content":"I have had great success with 2 tactics for Big Bads, the first is that they only drop 1 Initiative per wither attack (the attacker gains like normal, the Big Bad just doesn't lose more than 1), and the Two Snakes method: the Big Bad is modeled mechanically as if it were 2 creatures taking 2 turns, each has separate health pools. When the first &quot;snake&quot; dies then second snake can be attacked and the boss is down to one turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T19:50:32-07:00","id":1400235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1400224#post1400224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main problem with the soakbeast is its over use.<br /> <br /> In the you mention context I'm probably going to be less worried with the Eclipse or the Twilight with little to no combat investment and more concerned about the Night with Thrown because they could be heavily invested in combat, but in a way that a soakbeast would shrug off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point, and it's easier to justify high soak creatures being constantly used than it is high defense swordmasters. One has quite a few generic examples and the other should be fairly rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T00:55:56-07:00","id":1400260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1400231#post1400231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have had great success with 2 tactics for Big Bads, the first is that they only drop 1 Initiative per wither attack (the attacker gains like normal, the Big Bad just doesn't lose more than 1), and the Two Snakes method: the Big Bad is modeled mechanically as if it were 2 creatures taking 2 turns, each has separate health pools. When the first &quot;snake&quot; dies then second snake can be attacked and the boss is down to one turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your ideas seems interesting to me. How did it work so far ?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T21:53:21-07:00","id":1400455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1400260#post1400260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your ideas seems interesting to me. How did it work so far ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Great. The foe was the Big Bad of 2 real life years of campaign, so I wanted a suitably epic fight. One thing I've learned from DnD streams (specifically Matt Colville and Matt Mercer) is that you need to break the rules a little to make bosses feel threatening. The Big Bad of a 20+ session adventure has to be someone who cant be punked in 1 round by 5 solars going Nova. Here's what I did. <br /> <br /> <br /> First Round: Big Bad is literally invincible. The battle was in his dream realm, so it made narrative sense. The Solars quickly realized this. After everyone had a turn, a mini cutscene happened and some NPC favors took the invincibility from the boss. <br /> <br /> <br /> Round 2: Boss goes on initiative 20, and his Spear goes on Initiative 10 (i didn't roll for these, they were set). The spear can only do basic attacks, but its still an artifact spear weilded by Basically Octavian<br /> <br /> <br /> They fight. <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd like to tell you this was an epic match up where everyone gave all they could and barely toppled an incredible foe, but they didn't. They didn't work together well as a team, and the tanky party members weren't there for the glass cannons and it was basically fiat that they won at all. That may sound strange to admit after i explain how I made a tough boss, but these 4 Solars at Essence 3 could barely deal with Octavian's base statline (before charms) and the players were of mixed levels of invested or joyride. It was, honestly, a huge letdown to plan a 3 stage kaiju bossfight ultimate duel showdown only for people to still struggle with their charms and not have a battle plan or team tactics. <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly I don't think they would have beat plain old Octavian or Ahlat, who aren't slouches by any means but should never roll a 4 person crew of E3 Solars. <br /> <br /> The Single Pointer did his job but wasnt supported by the tanky Twilight and his Tyrant Lizard Survival Build, who both stayed in Medium plinking away. The Zenith tried her presence-fu but met the hard wall of Unacceptable Influence (she did succeed on the undead BG though). The Thrown using Bureaucrat hung out in Long but forgot his charms and isnt really invested as a player so did virtually nothing useful. <br /> <br /> They certainly could have won easily, but didnt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T23:18:56-07:00","id":1400462,"title":"","content":"Well that sucks. Sorry to hear that your battle didn't go as epic as you had planned. This was the 2 snake method, when did you use the other method and how did it go?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T02:39:46-07:00","id":1400482,"title":"","content":"I used it on a Fae Lord. That was interesting because the Fae was a Lord of Dance (and Storms) so the Initiative Trick was represented in-game as their belief in the Dance being hard to stop with their attacks. That fight was basically the Fae Lord summoning different Environmental Hazards and warping the actual ground beneath their feet to throw them all over the map. The players had a great time with that one because of how weird it was. Puzzle Bosses are great, definitely try them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T05:28:17-07:00","id":1400502,"title":"","content":"Yeah Octavian's probably not the best choice for this method. <br /> Since he's something of a soakbeast already and limiting the initiative the boss loses to 1 is just going to confound the sense of futility for characters with low damage (note this can also an issue with Legendary Size).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T05:49:09-07:00","id":1400506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1400502#post1400502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah Octavian's probably not the best choice for this method.<br /> Since he's something of a soakbeast already and limiting the initiative the boss loses to 1 is just going to confound the sense of futility for characters with low damage (note this can also an issue with Legendary Size).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also reducing his initiative is a pretty important strategy for keeping him from splatting your characters all over the room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T14:44:22-07:00","id":1400583,"title":"","content":"I didnt give him legendary size or his charms, just his statline. <br /> <br /> Honestly though, the subtle art if gauging difficulty can be a moot point when pcs don't work together and no one uses tactics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T17:31:41-07:00","id":1400602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1400583#post1400583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didnt give him legendary size or his charms, just his statline.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that him only losing 1i per successful withering attack as per your solution, is in some ways reminiscent of the issues caused by Legendary Size (though lesser) and Hardness.<br /> <br /> With his hardness rating you need either 11+ initiative, a charm which ignores hardness or for him to be in initiative crash (the one major advantage this has over Legendary Size) to make a decisive attack and with the wrong build that could be so fucking tedious.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly though, the subtle art if gauging difficulty can be a moot point when pcs don't work together and no one uses tactics.</div> </div> </div> </div> Was this something they could theoretically do based on their character sheets or unusually bad for them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 07-02-2020, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T22:57:56-07:00","id":1400638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1400602#post1400602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that him only losing 1i per successful withering attack as per your solution, is in some ways reminiscent of the issues caused by Legendary Size (though lesser) and Hardness.<br /> <br /> With his hardness rating you need either 11+ initiative, a charm which ignores hardness or for him to be in initiative crash (the one major advantage this has over Legendary Size) to make a decisive attack and with the wrong build that could be so fucking tedious.<br /> <br /> <br /> Was this something they could theoretically do based on their character sheets or unusually bad for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh they should have fucking steamrolled him. They have done similar things in the past. The Initiative Trick and 2 attacks were meant to make him a slugfest. Here's my group:<br /> <br /> Full Single Point Sail Supernal (about 20 health) and a ton of Brawl Grapple charms (inclides Dragon Coil Tech) <br /> Full Survival Twilight with ISoB and a lot of Resistance. 4 ox bodies @ Stam 5 Resistance 5<br /> A Tyrant Lizard enhanced by Baara-Unleashing Technique <br /> A Presence Zenith with no combat charms but unstoppable Terror Powers (she obliterated the undead BG) <br /> A Bureacrat Twilight with Thrown charms and Cirrus Skiff. <br /> <br /> Save for the non-com Zenith, each one has an artifact, and the Tyrant Lizard has some custom charms too (rp its an otter god, mechanically its a Tyrant Lizard). <br /> <br /> I thought the 2 fighters would enter melee with their literally unkillable TRex for a major 3 on 2 (boss and spear) brawl while the Zenith handled the BG and the flying sniper chose the best targets to kill. <br /> <br /> Instead the Survival Twilight Tank and the Unkillable Tyrant Lizard stayed at medium using some weak ranged charms leaving the Single Pointer by himself. <br /> <br /> Just the Tyrant Lizard was enough to keep the boss occupied, but keeping it in Medium was something I didnt consider and the boss wasnt going to ignore the Single Pointer he has rp reasons to hate so it went down like the titanic. The thrown user forgot his charms bc he doesnt really care about the game and i wanna kick him but hes moving soon so oh well. <br /> <br /> I dont know. Maybe my boss design was shit. This was the big event they worked towards for 2 years irl so i told them we we absolutely going to go hard and that they needed to be ready for the fight of the Century. <br /> <br /> I'll take responsibility for the failure as ST, since thats my job. I balanced around the Avengers but they held back the Hulk and Thor, leaving Cap to fight Thanos by himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T23:07:43-07:00","id":1400639,"title":"","content":"Well I'd say you're only partly to blame. True, you should never design an encounter with the thought that surely the players will act thusly, 'cuz that's when they do the exact opposite of what they've done the last 40 times. Still, if they have tanks with tanks, those damn tanks better be engaging if it's at all possible. And even if a player doesn't care for the game he or she have a responsibility to the other players and you as the ST to pull their wait as best they can in a major fight. I mean they could have opted out at any point, hanging out with my buddies is still not a great reason to potentially wreck a game. You probably should've gone with that instinct to kick them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T23:09:13-07:00","id":1400640,"title":"","content":"And how in the hell do you forget about your combat charms 2 years into a game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T02:29:15-07:00","id":1400665,"title":"","content":"The player in question joined in January or February and is a coworker of the players. I kept trying to help him out (Exalted is his first RPG and its a complicated beast), but he just doesnt care to remember the rules really and had to be reminded what his dice totals were 2 sessions ago. It would be a social faux-pas to kick him but he's moving next month so it solved itself.<br /> <br /> I'm over it now. I planned for a Trex and 2 combatants, I got 1 combatant. I will say the Initiative trick worked great on a puzzle boss i spoke about earlier, and the 2 snakes method worked on a Totally-Not-the-Sliver-Queen monster from earlier in the game. They also both worked in DnD if that matters at all. <br /> <br /> Anyway, that's my peace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T02:49:59-07:00","id":1400671,"title":"","content":"Bad roll of the dice there Goblin Slayer :P Seriously though they seem to be fine methods though I like the puzzle enemy one better. Personally I often use environment, situations, and terrain to spice up my big bads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","user":"Arkayriel","date":".  cuz I can't spell apparently 07-03-2020, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T03:50:10-07:00","id":1400687,"title":"","content":"Just as an observation that I've made after running a game for several years;<br /> <br /> a lot of times, for me, it seems like players will often try to come up with unconventional or sneaky solutions to combats versus just punching someone to death. To me, this is part of where I start to see a lot of inventiveness in players who go 'well yes, I could just punch him, but what if I blow out the wall of the tower so we're both falling to our deaths, then my winged friend swoops in and saves me while the bad guy falls to his death?'<br /> <br /> In instances like these, often I feel like that, so long as the players are having fun, and I have to assume the idea of trying different ways of winning an encounter are them having fun, I don't mind too much about it. I think one of the worst things you can do in that instance is rigidly hold onto the 'you have to drop all their health levels' fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T06:02:53-07:00","id":1400713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkayriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1400640#post1400640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how in the hell do you forget about your combat charms 2 years into a game?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, superheroes forget about their powers all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T06:46:53-07:00","id":1400720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1400713#post1400713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, superheroes forget about their powers all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they've just got bad players lol. I see what you're saying but I'm more relieved to know the player has only been playing since January. It's one thing to make a less than optimal decision or to forget about an older charm you haven't used in awhile but would be useful for this particular fight. It's another to forget what most of your charms do unless combats are really few and far between. Still I have played with a much older guy who had trouble remembering his charms as exalted was new to him. He'd been playing DnD for like 35 or more years...so yeah, it happens. Still strange to me when it does though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T07:01:37-07:00","id":1400725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkayriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1400640#post1400640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how in the hell do you forget about your combat charms 2 years into a game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh... you have a LOT of Charms two years into a game.<br /> <br /> Like, Cynis Ganan has Earth Dragon Form, Become the Hammer and Force of the Mountain. I literally couldn't tell you what other Charms he has.<br /> <br /> Actually... that's not quite true. A Deathknight knocked him Prone, nearly killing him, because I forgot he has that Earth Dragon Charm that stops you being knocked Prone. I forget what it's called.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T07:11:22-07:00","id":1400729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365948-can-your-big-bad-villain-take-5-solars-at-once?p=1400725#post1400725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh... you have a LOT of Charms two years into a game.<br /> <br /> Like, Cynis Ganan has Earth Dragon Form, Become the Hammer and Force of the Mountain. I literally couldn't tell you what other Charms he has.<br /> <br /> Actually... that's not quite true. A Deathknight knocked him Prone, nearly killing him, because I forgot he has that Earth Dragon Charm that stops you being knocked Prone. I forget what it's called.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I get that. It just sounded like he forgot most if not all of what his thrown charms did. Even do to lack of investment that seemed weird. You're not going to forget what Earth Dragon Form does, or ISoB anytime soon anymore than you're going to forget your weapons stats. Just seemed odd unless the game had little to no combat. I mean we're not talking about a Dawn brawler with 30 brawl charms here. But I'll concede the point, fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","user":"Arkayriel","date":".  cuz I'm really. really bad at spelling today apparently 07-03-2020, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}